/* Ported from Olivia Today (outputs/olivia-today) by work/olivia-today/port-to-site.mjs. Edit the source there, then re-run the port. */
// @ts-nocheck
export default {"planets":{"sun":{"planet":"sun","houses":{"1":{"en":{"theme":"The start of your personal year","text":"The Sun is back in your sign for the weeks around your birthday, and the spotlight tends to swing onto you: your face, your body, the way you walk into a room. Others may notice you more, and it gets easier to see what no longer fits, from a haircut to a habit. A birthday often makes people count the years, which can stir the wish to reinvent everything at once. Start one thing, not five.","scene":"Perhaps you catch your reflection in a shop window and, on the spot, book the haircut you’ve been postponing since spring.","do":"Start the one change you keep promising yourself, this week.","avoid":"Turning your birthday into a yearly performance review.","ask":"What do you want people to notice about you this year?"}},"2":{"en":{"theme":"The month to know your price","text":"For the next four weeks the Sun brings your money into view: the salary, the side income, the subscriptions you forgot you pay for, the things you own and the things that own you. It’s a good month to look at the numbers soberly. You might notice how closely your mood follows your balance, perhaps because earning became a way to prove your worth. Price your hours as if you believed they were worth it.","scene":"Picture the bus home: you open the banking app, find three subscriptions you’d forgotten and feel oddly proud for having looked.","do":"Cancel one subscription and write down what your hour costs.","avoid":"Answering “whatever you think is fair” when someone asks your rate.","ask":"What would you charge if you weren’t afraid of seeming greedy?"}},"3":{"en":{"theme":"When your words can travel further","text":"The Sun is moving through your house of messages and short distances, so this month tends to run on texts, calls, errands and quick trips across town. Ideas may land better than usual; notice whether people start quoting you back to yourself. The pull to join every conversation can be strong, as if being in the loop were the same as being alive. Answer the threads that matter properly; the rest can live with a thumbs-up.","scene":"Say you’re answering your brother on the tram, booking a class on the walk home and drafting the perfect reply to a neighbour’s note.","do":"Send the email, post or pitch you’ve been drafting in your head.","avoid":"Replying to everyone and saying nothing you actually meant.","ask":"Which conversation this month is worth more than ten quick replies?"}},"4":{"en":{"theme":"When home takes the main stage","text":"This month the Sun sinks to the base of your chart, into the house of home and family, the place you come back to at night. The flat, the fridge, the parents and the role you play at the family table all draw attention. Work ambitions can feel muted, as if something at the foundation wants fixing first. Notice whether you turn back into the twelve-year-old you were whenever a relative raises an eyebrow.","scene":"Maybe you spend a free Saturday rearranging the living room and realise you’re prouder of it than of anything you did at work.","do":"Fix the one thing at home you step around every day.","avoid":"Taking on every family errand to prove you’re the good one.","ask":"What would make your home feel like it’s on your side?"}},"5":{"en":{"theme":"A month for showing off a little","text":"The Sun walks into your house of pleasure, flirting and making things, and for once the month invites you to have fun on purpose. Romance can warm up, a hobby may grow into a small obsession, and any children around you might want an audience. Perhaps you hold back from what you love because doing it badly in public feels worse than not doing it at all. Be an amateur, loudly.","scene":"You might catch yourself posting the drawing, the song or the cake you made, then checking the reactions every ten minutes with a grin you’d never admit to.","do":"Book a date, a class or a night out purely for pleasure.","avoid":"Waiting until you’re good at something before letting anyone see it.","ask":"What did you love doing at ten that you quietly stopped?"}},"6":{"en":{"theme":"Fixing the way your days run","text":"For the next few weeks the Sun shines on the unglamorous machinery of your life: the work queue, the sleep schedule, the gym bag by the door, the colleague who keeps forwarding you their tasks. Small fixes tend to pay off quickly, and simply being competent can feel good. Perfectionism is worth noticing: the point where improving your routine turns into auditing yourself all day. Change one habit, not your whole personality.","scene":"It could be as small as a Sunday night spent colour-coding your calendar, setting a gym alarm and feeling almost smug about a clean desktop.","do":"Choose one habit — sleep, water, a walk — and keep it daily.","avoid":"Doing a colleague’s job because it’s quicker than saying no.","ask":"Which daily habit would make the next month kinder to your body?"}},"7":{"en":{"theme":"The month of the other person","text":"The Sun is crossing the sign opposite yours, your seventh house, so this month tends to belong to the people across the table: a partner, a business ally, an ex, a rival you can’t stop measuring yourself against. It can be easiest to see yourself in how they respond to you. The weeks favour negotiation and the overdue talk; notice, too, when you let their mood set yours.","scene":"It might look like a dinner where you hear yourself say “I want this to be fair”, and realise you’ve been waiting months to say it.","do":"Say what you want from the partnership in one sentence.","avoid":"Agreeing to everything so the evening stays nice.","ask":"What do you keep expecting from others that you could give yourself?"}},"8":{"en":{"theme":"Opening the envelope you’ve been avoiding","text":"This month the Sun brings into view the parts of life you usually keep in a drawer: joint money, loans, taxes, the deposit someone still owes you, and who you really trust with your body and your secrets. One honest hour with the paperwork can change a lot. If you avoid the statement or the conversation, perhaps needing someone feels like losing control. Read the statement; a known number is often easier to carry than the dread.","scene":"Perhaps, at the kitchen table, you open the letter from the tax office, read it twice and feel lighter for knowing the number.","do":"Find out exactly what you owe and what you’re owed.","avoid":"Keeping money secrets from someone who shares your bills.","ask":"Who do you trust with the truth about your money and your body?"}},"9":{"en":{"theme":"When your world wants to get bigger","text":"The Sun is moving through your house of distance and big ideas, so this month the usual streets can feel small. Perhaps you want a ticket, a course, a book that rearranges your head, a conversation with someone from far away. The stretch is traditionally read as good for applications, visas, publishing or anything that needs a stamp. You might catch yourself preaching your new theory at dinner before you’ve lived with it for a week.","scene":"Maybe it’s midnight and you have six tabs open — a flight, a language app, a master’s programme — and you’re happier than you’ve been in weeks.","do":"Take one real step towards the trip, the course or the application.","avoid":"Lecturing friends about a book you started on Tuesday.","ask":"Which belief of yours would you like to test against real life?"}},"10":{"en":{"theme":"Your work in full daylight","text":"This month the Sun climbs to the highest point of your chart, the house of career and reputation, and draws attention to your work whether you planned it or not. Bosses and clients may notice your name more, and a role or a pay rise can feel easier to bring up. If recognition feels like proof the effort was worth it, overworking just to be seen can look tempting. Ask directly instead of hoping someone spots you.","scene":"Say your name comes up in a meeting you weren’t invited to, and for once you feel pleased instead of anxious.","do":"Ask your manager directly for the role, raise or project.","avoid":"Staying late just so someone sees the light still on.","ask":"What do you want to be known for at work in five years?"}},"11":{"en":{"theme":"Your people, your plans","text":"The Sun is in your house of friends and futures, so this month the calendar tends to fill with group dinners, birthdays, community events and the kind of chat that turns into a plan. Being more visible in the crowd can feel good and slightly exposing. If you catch yourself measuring your life against friends’ news, use the company instead: say your wish out loud to people who can help.","scene":"Imagine a friend’s birthday where you mention, half-joking, the project you’ve been sitting on, and someone across the table says they know just the person.","do":"Tell three friends what you’re working towards this year.","avoid":"Comparing your life to the highlights in the group chat.","ask":"Which friendships pull you towards the future you actually want?"}},"12":{"en":{"theme":"The quiet weeks before your birthday","text":"The Sun is passing through the last house of your chart, the weeks just before your birthday, and your battery may run lower than your calendar assumes. Sleep can stretch longer, crowds can feel louder, and old memories tend to surface at odd hours. Perhaps you push through because rest without a reason feels like laziness. Clear the backlog, sleep more, and let the new year start clean.","scene":"Picture a Sunday alone sorting old photos and unsent drafts, and feeling less lonely than you did in a crowded bar last week.","do":"Finish or formally close one project before your birthday.","avoid":"Cramming big new launches into the tired weeks before your birthday.","ask":"What are you ready to finish before your next year begins?"}}},"signs":{"aries":{"en":"Aries season is read as the starting gun of the zodiac year. Patience tends to run short and courage high, and these weeks favour the ideas you start before you’ve finished thinking."},"taurus":{"en":"Taurus season tends to slow things to the pace of a good meal. People often want comfort, money they can count and plans that last; rushing anyone seldom helps."},"gemini":{"en":"Gemini season often fills the calendar with conversations, short trips and half-read articles. Curiosity runs high and attention short, so it helps to write things down."},"cancer":{"en":"Cancer season draws attention homeward: family, food, old photos, the people who knew you before. Feelings often sit closer to the surface, and kindness can go further."},"leo":{"en":"Leo season is read as a time for being seen. Generosity, flirting, birthdays and big gestures tend to come easily, and so can wounded pride when nobody claps."},"virgo":{"en":"Virgo season favours lists, fresh notebooks and quiet repairs. Many people want to get organised; notice any urge to criticise those who haven’t yet."},"libra":{"en":"In Libra season many people want things fair, pretty and agreed. It favours partnerships and making peace, and tends to slow decisions that might upset someone."},"scorpio":{"en":"Scorpio season turns attention below the surface: money, sex, secrets, grief. Small talk often thins out, and loyalties can feel quietly tested."},"sagittarius":{"en":"Sagittarius season tends to widen the view: travel plans, big opinions, honest jokes. Optimism is easy to find, and so is the urge to promise more than you can deliver."},"capricorn":{"en":"Capricorn season favours long goals and serious work. Effort and results tend to earn respect, sentiment goes quiet, and many people take stock of what this year actually built."},"aquarius":{"en":"Aquarius season favours friends, causes and odd new ideas. People often want freedom and better systems, and can seem cool exactly when you want warmth."},"pisces":{"en":"Pisces season tends to blur the edges: dreams can run vivid, empathy high, deadlines loose. The zodiac’s last month suits rest, art and finishing what’s old."}}},"moon":{"planet":"moon","houses":{"1":{"en":{"theme":"A mood that shows on your face","text":"The Moon is in your sign for a day or two, and feelings tend to sit right on the surface: in your face, your stomach, your tone of voice. Hunger, tiredness and irritation can come on faster and louder than usual. People may read you easily today, which feels exposing if you’re used to looking fine no matter what. Try eating first, then decide whether the problem is still a problem.","scene":"Maybe someone asks “are you okay?” before you’ve said a word, and you realise you’ve been frowning at your screen since nine.","do":"Eat a proper meal before replying to anything that annoys you.","avoid":"Pretending you’re fine while your face says otherwise.","ask":"What is your body asking for before your head joins in?"}},"2":{"en":{"theme":"The pull of comfort you can buy","text":"The Moon is passing through your house of money and possessions, and today security may feel physical: a full fridge, a soft jumper, a decent balance in the account. You might crave good food and familiar things, and spending can work like a sedative, perhaps because owning something solid calms the part of you that worries it could all run out. Comfort is fine; it’s worth glancing at the basket before you pay.","scene":"Picture going in for bread and leaving with cheese, candles and a scarf you didn’t need, calmer and slightly guilty.","do":"Cook something filling from what’s already in the fridge.","avoid":"Treating a low mood with a full online shopping basket.","ask":"What makes you feel safe that doesn’t cost anything?"}},"3":{"en":{"theme":"The need to talk it out","text":"With the Moon in your house of messages and short trips, feelings tend to find their way into words today. If you think out loud, a long voice note to your sister or a chat with a neighbour on the stairs can settle more than an hour of thinking in circles. Your mind may run fast and sleep may be light. When thoughts start looping, try a short walk or an errand.","scene":"Perhaps you record a four-minute voice note about a minor annoyance, play it back, and feel half of it already gone.","do":"Call a sibling or a chatty friend instead of texting.","avoid":"Rereading the same message until it sounds worse.","ask":"What are you trying to say that hasn’t found the right listener yet?"}},"4":{"en":{"theme":"Old comforts and a quiet night in","text":"The Moon is in your house of home and family, where it is traditionally most at ease, and you might notice a pull towards the sofa, the old blanket, the food someone cooked for you as a child. Social plans can look exhausting and your own kitchen perfect. A single phone call may stir old family feelings, because home is where your oldest reflexes live. Stay in if you can, and let that be enough.","scene":"It might look like cancelling drinks, making your grandmother’s soup from memory and ending up texting your mum to ask how much dill goes in.","do":"Cook a dish from your childhood or call home.","avoid":"Forcing yourself out when your body is asking to stay in.","ask":"What does home need to feel like for you to rest?"}},"5":{"en":{"theme":"Room for delight, not duty","text":"The Moon moves through your house of pleasure and play, so your mood may brighten the moment something is fun and sink the moment it isn’t. You might catch yourself wanting attention, a flirt, music loud in the car, dessert before the main course. Underneath there is often a simple need to be enjoyed rather than relied on. Take one unproductive hour, and notice if you’re sulking because nobody clapped.","scene":"It could be as small as putting on the song you loved at seventeen while making dinner, then dancing with a wooden spoon.","do":"Do one thing today purely because it’s fun.","avoid":"Saving the fun for after the chores are done.","ask":"When did you last feel enjoyed rather than needed?"}},"6":{"en":{"theme":"The calm of a tidy desk","text":"The Moon is in your house of daily work and the body, so today your mood tends to live in your routine. A clear desk, a walk at lunch and water before coffee can steady you, while skipped meals and a messy inbox may go straight to your stomach. The urge to fix every small thing often comes from wanting control when feelings misbehave. Do the chores, then stop before you start reorganising your colleagues.","scene":"Say it’s eleven at night: you scrub the bathroom, give the cat an extra treat and feel calmer than you did all working day.","do":"Eat lunch away from the screen and take a short walk.","avoid":"Fixing colleagues’ mistakes to calm your own nerves.","ask":"Which part of your body tells you first that you’re overloaded?"}},"7":{"en":{"theme":"Feelings shaped around one person","text":"The Moon is passing through your house of partners, and for a day or two your feelings may take shape around one other person. A partner’s tone, a friend’s slow reply or a colleague’s coldness can land harder than usual. When you want closeness and reassurance, you might try to earn it by being agreeable rather than saying what you need. Ask plainly instead of testing whether they can guess.","scene":"Suppose your partner says “fine” in a flat voice, and you spend the next hour guessing what you did wrong instead of asking.","do":"Ask for the hug, the call or the evening together.","avoid":"Taking a tired face or a short reply personally.","ask":"What do you need from the person closest to you today?"}},"8":{"en":{"theme":"When feelings go underground","text":"With the Moon in your house of intimacy and shared money, feelings tend to go deep and private today. You might want real closeness or none at all, and small things, like a phone turned face-down or an unpaid share of the bill, may feel like signs of something bigger. That suspicion is often an old lesson: perhaps trusting too soon once cost you. Name what you’re afraid of, then believe the answer you get.","scene":"You might catch yourself awake at one in the morning, replaying a remark from dinner and checking the joint account for no clear reason.","do":"Ask the direct question instead of quietly investigating.","avoid":"Checking someone’s phone or online status to calm your nerves.","ask":"Where are you bracing for betrayal instead of asking for reassurance?"}},"9":{"en":{"theme":"The wish for a bigger view","text":"The Moon is moving through your house of distance and big questions, and today your mood may want room. The usual walls can feel close, and a train window, a long walk, a documentary or a talk about what life is for often feeds you better than another task. Small routines tend to feel like a cage when you’re hungry for meaning. Change the scenery, even if it’s only a different café.","scene":"On the way home, perhaps, you get off two stops early just to walk a street you’ve never walked, and your shoulders drop.","do":"Walk somewhere new or sketch out a trip, even an imaginary one.","avoid":"Picking a fight about politics because you’re bored.","ask":"Where would you go tomorrow if nothing held you back?"}},"10":{"en":{"theme":"Work that gets under your skin","text":"The Moon crosses the top of your chart, your house of career and reputation, and today feelings may follow you to work. A boss’s short email or a public compliment can hit you in the chest, not just the head. Wanting to look competent, you might hide tiredness to keep the image intact. Do the job well, then go home and let someone see you off duty.","scene":"Imagine your manager replies “ok.” with no emoji, and you reread your own email three times looking for the mistake.","do":"Write down what you finished today and close the laptop on time.","avoid":"Treating one curt email from your boss as a verdict.","ask":"Whose approval at work are you still waiting for?"}},"11":{"en":{"theme":"A day that asks for your people","text":"The Moon is passing through your house of friends and shared plans, so your mood may rise and fall with the group around you. A good conversation can do more than an hour alone with your thoughts. If you feel oddly flat, perhaps you’ve simply gone too long without people who know you well.","scene":"It might start with opening the group chat to send one meme and end with planning a dinner for Saturday.","do":"Message the friend you’ve been meaning to reply to for a week.","avoid":"Reading one quiet reply as proof that nobody cares.","ask":"Who makes you feel more like yourself after an hour together?"}},"12":{"en":{"theme":"Thin skin and a need for quiet","text":"The Moon is in the hidden house of your chart, and for a day or two your skin may feel thinner, your feelings quiet and strange. Crowds can seem loud and dreams vivid, and you might tear up at an advert without knowing why. Often that’s old tiredness asking to be noticed, and pushing through tends to make it louder. Keep plans light and write down what you haven’t said aloud.","scene":"It could look like a film you’ve seen five times, a blanket pulled over your head and every message left until morning.","do":"Go to bed an hour earlier than usual tonight.","avoid":"Filling the silence with scrolling until two in the morning.","ask":"What feeling have you been too busy to notice this week?"}}},"signs":{"aries":{"en":"Moods tend to run hot and fast: impatient, brave, quick to snap and quick to forgive. It’s worth moving your body early and counting to five before replying."},"taurus":{"en":"Moods like to settle into the body: hungry, slow, stubborn, soothed by good bread and clean sheets. Comfort helps; being rushed can make anyone dig in."},"gemini":{"en":"Moods easily turn chatty and scattered: plenty of texts, plenty of half-finished sentences. Talking can help, as long as the phone doesn’t sleep on your pillow."},"cancer":{"en":"Moods lean tender and homeward: many people want soup, family and someone who remembers how they take their tea. Feelings often sit close to the surface, so go gently."},"leo":{"en":"Moods may crave warmth and an audience: generous, dramatic, easily flattered and easily hurt. Give someone a sincere compliment, and wear the good shirt."},"virgo":{"en":"Moods usually get practical and twitchy, quick to notice the crumbs, the typo, the late reply. Tidying a drawer can do more than analysing a feeling."},"libra":{"en":"Moods are drawn to company and fairness: pleasant evenings, matching plates, nobody upset. Decisions may slow down, and a small kindness often works better than winning the argument."},"scorpio":{"en":"Moods can sink deep and go quiet: intense, private, suspicious of small talk. One honest conversation or a long bath often does more than a crowded room."},"sagittarius":{"en":"Moods tend to lift towards the horizon: restless, funny, impatient with detail. A walk, a plan for a trip or a big honest conversation can help more than staying in."},"capricorn":{"en":"Moods are inclined to turn sober and businesslike: less chatter, more lists, a stiff upper lip. Getting one hard thing done may feel better than talking about feelings."},"aquarius":{"en":"Moods often cool and step back: space, ideas and friends appeal more than fuss. Feelings can slip out sideways as opinions, so ask what’s underneath."},"pisces":{"en":"Moods readily go soft and porous: tearful at adverts, dreamy, soaking up whatever the room feels. Music, water and a quiet evening are good company; alcohol tends to hit harder."}}},"mercury":{"planet":"mercury","houses":{"1":{"en":{"theme":"The voice that walks in first","text":"Mercury is crossing your first house, and these weeks bring into view how much the way you talk shapes the way people meet you. You might find yourself thinking faster, interrupting more, starting three things before lunch. Underneath there is often an old habit of explaining yourself before anyone asks, perhaps because being misread feels worse than being wrong. It is worth catching the moment you start running on nerves: half-finished sentences, cold half-drunk coffee, a jaw you clench without noticing.","scene":"Say someone new asks what you do, and you hear yourself give a three-minute answer, with footnotes, before they’ve finished their drink.","do":"Say the short version first, then stop and let them ask.","avoid":"Over-explaining yourself to people who didn’t ask for a reason.","ask":"What do you keep explaining that nobody asked you to justify?"}},"2":{"en":{"theme":"Saying the number out loud","text":"Mercury moving through your second house draws attention to the money conversation you’ve been postponing: the invoice, the raise, the subscription you forgot, the price you quote a client. You may even do sums in your head while brushing your teeth. Often the hard part isn’t the maths but saying a figure aloud, because naming your price hands someone else the chance to raise an eyebrow. Notice if you keep checking the banking app instead of making the call.","scene":"Maybe you type your rate into an email, delete it, type a lower one, and stare at the cursor for a full minute.","do":"Send the invoice or the price today, without an apology attached.","avoid":"Discounting your price before anyone has even asked.","ask":"What number do you find hardest to say out loud?"}},"3":{"en":{"theme":"When every message feels like your job","text":"Mercury is on home ground in your third house, and these weeks draw attention to the traffic of ordinary life: messages, errands across town, a sibling who wants to talk, a neighbour with news. Your mind may feel quick and nosy in a good way, and doing tends to teach you faster than reading. Notice whether replying instantly has started to feel like proof you’re reliable, so that you answer everything and say very little.","scene":"Perhaps you’re on the bus answering your sister, a work chat and the landlord at once, and you miss your stop.","do":"Mute two group chats and call one person back instead.","avoid":"Passing on a rumour because it’s too good not to.","ask":"Which conversation this week actually changed what you think?"}},"4":{"en":{"theme":"The dialect you learned at home","text":"Mercury in your fourth house tends to bring the talking home: calls with a parent, the family group chat, a plumber to book, the utility bill nobody has read. Your mind may drift back to childhood rooms and things said at dinner years ago. With family you might slip into the voice you had at fourteen, perhaps because that’s the dialect you learned first. Worth noticing whether you are replaying an old argument instead of having the current one.","scene":"Picture it: you call home about one small thing, and forty minutes later you’re arguing about a family holiday from 2009.","do":"Book the repair you keep mentioning, or sort one drawer of papers.","avoid":"Answering a parent in the tone you had at fourteen.","ask":"Which family sentence still plays in your head, and whose voice is it?"}},"5":{"en":{"theme":"Letting wit do the flirting","text":"In your fifth house, Mercury is traditionally linked with verbal play: the flirty text you redraft three times, a story you start writing for fun, a board game that turns competitive, a child’s hundredth why. Ideas often come easily when nothing is at stake. You might prefer being clever to being sincere, because a joke can always be taken back and a feeling can’t. See whether the banter has become so good that nobody ever says what they want.","scene":"You could spend twenty minutes on a two-line reply to someone you like, then delete the one honest word.","do":"Send one message that’s warm instead of witty.","avoid":"Hiding a real compliment inside a joke.","ask":"What feeling are you joking about instead of naming?"}},"6":{"en":{"theme":"A list for every worry","text":"With Mercury in your sixth house, ordinary days can start to feel like logistics: work email, the shared calendar, a colleague whose instructions make no sense, the dentist appointment you keep rescheduling. Your mind may crave systems, and fixing a clumsy process tends to come naturally. When you’re anxious, a list is often the first move, because a tidy list feels like control and a worry doesn’t. Notice where the strain shows: a tight stomach, the itch to correct everyone’s spelling.","scene":"It could be as small as rewriting your to-do list in a nicer notebook instead of doing the first item.","do":"Do the ten-minute task that’s been on your list all week.","avoid":"Correcting a colleague’s grammar when they asked about the deadline.","ask":"What does your body do when your inbox gets full?"}},"7":{"en":{"theme":"Talks at a table for two","text":"Mercury in your seventh house gathers the important conversations at a table for two: a partner, a business ally, a client, the contract that deserves a proper read. These weeks favour thinking with one person opposite you. You might catch yourself listening for the reply you had braced for instead of the one you got, perhaps because being right feels safer than being surprised. It helps to ask before you argue.","scene":"It might look like this: the person closest to you says one sentence about the weekend, and you reply to the argument you rehearsed on the way home.","do":"Repeat back what they said before you answer it.","avoid":"Signing a contract you’ve only skimmed on your phone.","ask":"What do you want from this person, besides being right?"}},"8":{"en":{"theme":"Where money and trust get tangled","text":"Mercury is moving through your eighth house, where money and trust get tangled: the tax return, the loan terms, who pays what from a shared account, the talk about sex or debt you both avoid. Your mind may turn detective and want the real story. Researching can feel easier than asking outright, because asking means admitting how much the answer matters. It is worth asking once rather than scrolling back through old messages for evidence.","scene":"Imagine reading the tax letter twice before breakfast, then searching one phrase online until you’ve convinced yourself it’s a disaster.","do":"Ask the money question directly, in one plain sentence.","avoid":"Treating a short reply as evidence of a secret.","ask":"What answer are you afraid of getting if you ask straight?"}},"9":{"en":{"theme":"Booking the ticket in your head","text":"Mercury in your ninth house can make your mind hungry for a bigger map: a course, a language app, flights you price at 1 a.m., a visa form, a long article you finish. Opinions about politics, faith and how to live often feel urgent and worth arguing over. You may collect information to avoid choosing, because a trip you’re still researching can’t disappoint you. Ask whether winning an argument at dinner is worth losing the room.","scene":"You might have fourteen tabs open about a city you’ve never been to, and not a single night booked.","do":"Book one real thing this week: a class, a train, a weekend away.","avoid":"Turning every disagreement into a lecture with sources.","ask":"What would you study if nobody needed it to be useful?"}},"10":{"en":{"theme":"Every word on the record","text":"Mercury crossing your tenth house puts the spotlight on how your words land with people who decide things: the boss, the client, the panel, whoever reads your CV. These weeks suit pitching, presenting and asking about the next step. You might over-edit, perhaps because part of you believes one clumsy sentence could undo years of work. Check that sounding professional hasn’t made it hard to hear what you actually want.","scene":"Think of a three-line email to your manager, rewritten seven times and still opening with “Sorry to bother you”.","do":"Send the pitch at version three, not version eleven.","avoid":"Agreeing in the meeting and complaining about it afterwards.","ask":"What do you want to be known for, in one sentence?"}},"11":{"en":{"theme":"Thinking better in company","text":"Mercury in your eleventh house favours thinking in company: a friend who asks the sharp question, an online community, a meetup, the chat where half-formed plans get tested. Saying a hope aloud to people you trust can make it real enough to start. Notice the pull to agree with the group to keep your place in it, as if disagreeing could cost you the invitation.","scene":"Suppose you mention a half-serious idea in the group chat, and by evening three friends are asking when it launches.","do":"Tell one friend the plan you’ve only told your notes app.","avoid":"Laughing along at a group opinion you privately disagree with.","ask":"Who do you think more clearly around, and when did you last call them?"}},"12":{"en":{"theme":"A head that talks after midnight","text":"Mercury slipping through your twelfth house can turn up the voice in your head and turn down everything else. You may need more quiet to think, and your clearest ideas often surface in the shower, on a walk, half asleep. You might also rehearse conversations you never intend to have, because a draft can’t hurt you and a reply can. If you reach for the phone in bed, ask whether your mind wanted a notebook instead.","scene":"Picture yourself awake at 3 a.m., polishing the perfect reply to something a colleague said three years ago.","do":"Keep a notebook by the bed and empty your head into it.","avoid":"Telling everyone you’re fine while arguing with them in your head.","ask":"What are you saying to yourself that you haven’t said to anyone?"}}},"signs":{"aries":{"en":"Mercury in Aries often thinks in headlines: fast decisions, blunt replies, the first draft sent before the second thought. Good for starting, less patient with details."},"taurus":{"en":"Mercury in Taurus is traditionally read as slow thinking that means every word. Ideas need to be useful, solid, preferably affordable; once a mind is made up, it rarely shifts."},"gemini":{"en":"Mercury in Gemini is at home: quick, curious, funny, able to hold three conversations and a podcast at once. It favours ideas and can be slippery about follow-through."},"cancer":{"en":"Mercury in Cancer listens for tone more than words and can remember what was said years ago, word for word. Kitchen-table talks often do better than email."},"leo":{"en":"Mercury in Leo speaks to be heard: stories with a punchline, opinions delivered with conviction, a talent for persuading a room. Feedback can sting more than it needs to."},"virgo":{"en":"Mercury in Virgo likes to edit everything: the plan, the spreadsheet, the sentence you just said. Precise, useful, sometimes quietly anxious, and very good at spotting the one typo."},"libra":{"en":"Mercury in Libra weighs both sides out loud and usually drafts the diplomatic version first. Good for negotiating, often slow to deliver a plain no."},"scorpio":{"en":"Mercury in Scorpio listens for what isn’t said. Questions tend to go straight to the sore spot, secrets stay kept, and a vague answer can sharpen suspicion."},"sagittarius":{"en":"Mercury in Sagittarius thinks big and talks frankly, sometimes to the point of tactlessness. It loves the overview, skips the footnotes and can promise more than the calendar holds."},"capricorn":{"en":"Mercury in Capricorn thinks in plans, deadlines and consequences. Messages may turn brief and dry, like memos: well suited to contracts and hard talks, stingy with kind words."},"aquarius":{"en":"Mercury in Aquarius thinks sideways: odd connections, unexpected ideas at the bus stop, strong opinions about how systems should work. Brilliant in theory, often cool in tone."},"pisces":{"en":"Mercury in Pisces thinks in images and hunches, not lists. Words can go soft and suggestive: lovely for comforting a friend, less dependable for deadlines and fine print."}},"retro":{"1":{"en":"Your self-presentation is open for an edit: the bio, the profile photo, the way you introduce yourself, the habit of answering before you’ve heard the question. Slowing down helps; a second take often lands better."},"2":{"en":"The retrograde turns attention to money paperwork: the refund you never chased, the subscription still charging you, the rate you quoted too low last year. Recheck the numbers and renegotiate calmly rather than panic-cancel everything."},"3":{"en":"A season for revisiting old messages: the sibling you owe a call, the neighbour you misread, the text sent to the wrong chat. It invites you to double-check addresses and times, reread before sending and clear up misunderstandings by phone."},"4":{"en":"Family talk tends to loop back in this review season: a parent retelling an old story, the repair that wasn’t done properly, the box of papers nobody sorted. Worth redoing the job at home and hearing the story once more, actually listening."},"5":{"en":"Mercury’s backward weeks can turn your thoughts to an old flirtation or a shelved creative project. Reread the old draft before starting fresh; if an ex writes, reply only if it still seems wise next morning."},"6":{"en":"Work admin asks for a second look: the email thread nobody resolved, the instruction you misunderstood, the appointment you forgot to confirm. A good season for repairing the process, not your whole routine, and checking times twice."},"7":{"en":"Tradition reads these weeks as a time to revisit old agreements: a contract clause, a promise made to a partner, a misunderstanding with a client. Reread before re-signing, ask what was meant and let an old argument end differently."},"8":{"en":"These weeks bring shared paperwork into view: a tax query, an old debt, the joint account nobody reconciled, a conversation about trust left half-finished. Gather the documents, correct errors calmly and finish the abandoned talk."},"9":{"en":"This is a traditional time to return to travel plans and studies: a delayed booking, a visa form with a typo, the course you dropped halfway. It favours rechecking every date and document; going back to finish something counts as progress."},"10":{"en":"Career conversations are worth revisiting: the pitch that stalled, feedback from a boss you brushed off. If an old employer gets in touch, follow up politely; revise the CV and hold big announcements until the details are checked."},"11":{"en":"A good stretch for picking up old threads with friends: the group you drifted from, the project everyone abandoned, the friend you owe a reply. Reconnect, rethink the plan and check a rumour before you forward it."},"12":{"en":"Nights in this season can bring unsent drafts and unspoken thoughts to mind: an old apology, a half-kept secret, a dream that keeps recurring. Write it down first; decide in daylight whether anyone needs to read it."}},"retroGeneral":{"en":"Mercury retrograde is the roughly three weeks, a few times a year, when Mercury appears to move backwards across the sky. Astrologers traditionally read it as an editing season: a time to reread, recheck dates, back up your phone and reopen conversations that ended badly. If something needs signing, read it twice first."},"station":{"retrograde":{"en":"Mercury’s apparent standstill before turning back is often read as a pause. If a reply stalls, the laptop freezes or you lose your thread mid-sentence, take it as a cue to slow down, back up files and reread before sending."},"direct":{"en":"When Mercury seems to pause and turn forward, tradition reads the shift as gradual. The turning day can feel foggy; a few days on often suits sending the held reply, signing the reread contract or restarting a paused plan."}}},"venus":{"planet":"venus","houses":{"1":{"en":{"theme":"At ease in your own skin","text":"Venus is crossing your first house, the one that governs your body, your face and how you walk into a room. For a few weeks you may feel easier to like and notice it in small things: a stranger smiling back, the haircut that works, the coat you nearly gave away looking right again. Feeling attractive can make you gentler with everyone, including yourself. If you find yourself saying yes just to keep the smiles coming, that is worth a second look.","scene":"Perhaps you catch your reflection in a shop window, stand a little straighter and walk in to try on something you weren’t going to buy.","do":"Wear the thing you’ve been saving for a better day.","avoid":"Buying a new look to rescue a bad mood.","ask":"When do you feel most at home in your own body?"}},"2":{"en":{"theme":"When taste runs ahead of budget","text":"Venus in your second house turns your eye to money, belongings and your own worth. Perhaps you want fewer, better things: the good olive oil, the wool coat, the cup that feels right in your hand. Spending and self-worth are often tangled here: it can be easy to undercharge for your work, then overpay for a candle to feel better about it. These weeks favour a fresh look at what you charge and a pause before shopping tired.","scene":"Picture yourself at the checkout holding a beautiful, slightly ridiculous thing and telling yourself you’ve earned it, which might even be true.","do":"Leave the lovely thing in the basket overnight.","avoid":"Treating a price tag as a verdict on your worth.","ask":"What would you charge if you believed you were worth it?"}},"3":{"en":{"theme":"Charm that lives in your messages","text":"Venus is moving through your house of messages, siblings and short trips, so charm tends to travel through your thumbs. The right words may come more easily: for the awkward text, the thank-you you owe a neighbour, the reply that makes your sister laugh after a cold month. Even the walk to the shop can feel prettier. Smoothing every conversation into agreement can be tempting, because being pleasant feels safer than being clear.","scene":"Say you rewrite a two-line text four times so it sounds warm but not too keen, then send the first version anyway.","do":"Send the compliment you thought of and didn’t say.","avoid":"Typing “sounds great” when you mean “not really”.","ask":"Which conversation have you been keeping pleasant instead of honest?"}},"4":{"en":{"theme":"Love starts at the kitchen table","text":"Venus is settling into your fourth house: the flat, the family, the parents whose voices still live in your head. You may want home to look and feel right — a lamp moved, fresh flowers, the dish your grandmother used to make — because when the room is in order, so are you. Calls with family can go more gently than usual. It’s worth noticing if that calm is being bought by swallowing what you actually think.","scene":"Maybe you spend Sunday afternoon moving the sofa a metre to the left and feel oddly, completely better.","do":"Invite someone over and cook one thing you’re proud of.","avoid":"Nodding along at the family table to keep dinner pleasant.","ask":"What makes your home feel like yours, not just where you sleep?"}},"5":{"en":{"theme":"Pleasure without needing a reason","text":"Venus is in your fifth house of romance, play and making things, and is traditionally read as permission to enjoy yourself without earning it first. Flirting can feel easier, a hobby you dropped may want you back, and a night of dancing might do more than a productive evening. Attraction tends to follow fun rather than effort. Ask yourself whether it’s the rush of being wanted you’re after, or the person.","scene":"It might look like saying yes to a last-minute drink, picking the louder shirt and laughing harder than you have all month.","do":"Book one evening purely for fun: a gig, a class, a late film.","avoid":"Messaging an old flame only to check you’ve still got it.","ask":"When did you last enjoy something without needing to be good at it?"}},"6":{"en":{"theme":"Love that shows up as help","text":"Venus is moving through the part of your chart that runs your days: the to-do list, the job, the body that carries you through it. Affection here tends to be practical. You may feel most loved when someone notices you’re tired and quietly takes something off your plate, and perhaps you love the same way, often without saying so. Notice whether you have started keeping silent score.","scene":"You might catch yourself doing the dishes for the third night running, rehearsing a complaint instead of asking for help.","do":"Ask plainly for one specific kind of help.","avoid":"Turning a small chore into a test of how much you’re valued.","ask":"What would make an ordinary weekday feel cared for?"}},"7":{"en":{"theme":"When two feels like the easier number","text":"Venus is crossing your seventh house, the one about partners, close one-to-one bonds and the agreements you sign. These weeks draw attention to the air between you and the person across the table: an apology that lands, a negotiation finding its middle, a date that feels less like an interview. You may want harmony badly enough to read every pause as trouble. The question is whether you agree so smoothly that the other person never meets the real you.","scene":"It could be as small as saying “I don’t mind, you choose” about the restaurant, then spending dinner wishing you’d named the place you wanted.","do":"Say your preference first, before asking what they’d like.","avoid":"Signing anything because the other side was charming about it.","ask":"What do you want from the person closest to you but haven’t asked for?"}},"8":{"en":{"theme":"Closeness with the lights on","text":"Venus is in your eighth house, where desire, trust and shared money overlap. Attraction tends to run deeper and less polite here, and so do questions of who pays: the joint account, the loan to a friend, the gift that came with strings. Talking about money can feel more naked than undressing, because it shows what you fear losing. A present or a night together can become a way to skip that talk; this placement favours having it.","scene":"Picture splitting the dinner bill to the last penny, then lying awake wondering why it felt so cold.","do":"Say one true sentence about money to the person you share it with.","avoid":"Paying for everything so that nobody can ask more of you.","ask":"Who do you trust with your body but not with your bank balance?"}},"9":{"en":{"theme":"Falling for somewhere else","text":"Venus is travelling through your ninth house of distance, study and big ideas, and it is easy to fall a little in love with elsewhere: a city you saw in a film, a language you’re learning on your phone, a lecturer who explains things beautifully. You might be drawn to whatever makes you feel larger than your usual life. There can be a pull to romanticise faraway places until home starts to look small.","scene":"Maybe you check flights to a city you have no reason to visit, only to picture who you’d be there.","do":"Learn ten words of the language you keep daydreaming in.","avoid":"Booking an expensive escape from a life you haven’t tried changing.","ask":"Who do you become in a place where nobody knows you?"}},"10":{"en":{"theme":"When charm counts at work","text":"Venus is crossing the top of your chart, the tenth house of career, reputation and the people above you. Traditionally this favours coming across well in public: an interview that feels warm, a pitch that lands, your boss laughing in the right place. If goodwill is there, it’s a good moment to ask for the title, the budget or the move. You might catch yourself settling for praise, because being liked can feel like enough when it isn’t.","scene":"Say someone senior compliments you in the lift and you replay it all afternoon, slightly embarrassed by how much it matters.","do":"Ask for one specific thing while the room likes you.","avoid":"Taking a compliment from your boss as payment.","ask":"What do you want to be known for, beyond being nice to work with?"}},"11":{"en":{"theme":"Friendship that feels like falling in love","text":"Venus is in your eleventh house of friends, groups and the future you’re planning, so the sweetest moments are often found in company. A new friend can feel instantly familiar, an old one warm to reconnect with, and a group dinner may restore you more than a date would. Feeling lovable when you’re included can make every invitation hard to refuse. Keeping up with a crowd you’ve outgrown can quietly cost money and evenings.","scene":"Perhaps you almost skip a friend’s birthday drinks, go anyway and leave with two new numbers and a plan for Thursday.","do":"Introduce two friends who would like each other.","avoid":"Splitting a pricey bill to prove you still belong.","ask":"Which friends make your hopes feel realistic rather than silly?"}},"12":{"en":{"theme":"Love you keep to yourself","text":"Venus is moving through your twelfth house, the hidden back room of the chart where you rest and keep what you don’t say aloud. Desire tends to go quiet and private: a crush you tell nobody about, a long bath, a song you play only when alone. Wanting someone out of reach can feel safer than wanting someone who might answer. It’s easy to spend these weeks in love with a maybe; noticing it is a start.","scene":"It might be late at night: you reread an old conversation, phone dimmed, and decide not to message, again.","do":"Do one kind thing today that nobody else ever needs to know about.","avoid":"Keeping a door open for someone who never walks through it.","ask":"What are you longing for that you haven’t admitted even to yourself?"}}},"signs":{"aries":{"en":"Venus in Aries tends to fall fast and say so first. Attraction reads like a dare: bold texts, quick crushes, impulse buys, and boredom that can set in just as quickly."},"taurus":{"en":"Venus in Taurus loves slowly and through the senses: good bread, soft fabric, an unhurried evening. Loyalty runs deep, and so, often, does the habit of staying too long."},"gemini":{"en":"Venus in Gemini is traditionally charmed by a quick mind. Flirting tends to live in words — banter, voice notes, late-night replies — and curiosity often outruns commitment."},"cancer":{"en":"Venus in Cancer loves by looking after: soup, remembered birthdays, a spare key. Tenderness tends to come easily, and so can the hurt of feeling taken for granted."},"leo":{"en":"Venus in Leo likes romance with a little theatre: grand gestures, being chosen in public, compliments that sound like applause. It is generous and warm, and can feel quietly wounded when ignored."},"virgo":{"en":"Venus in Virgo tends to show love through small fixes: the shelf put up, the typo caught, the vitamins left out. Devotion is real; the inner critic usually is too."},"libra":{"en":"Venus in Libra is traditionally at home: manners, beauty, fairness, the art of the second date. Peace can come easily, sometimes at the cost of wishes left unsaid."},"scorpio":{"en":"Venus in Scorpio prefers depth to charm: loyalty, secrets, all-or-nothing attraction. Small talk can feel like a waste, and jealousy tends to run closer to the surface."},"sagittarius":{"en":"Venus in Sagittarius tends to fall for freedom and laughter: the stranger on the train, the person who says yes to the trip. Honesty is charming here; clinging rarely is."},"capricorn":{"en":"Venus in Capricorn loves with a long view: a coat that lasts ten years, a person who turns up on time. Affection tends to show in effort, rarely in words."},"aquarius":{"en":"Venus in Aquarius often falls for the friend first: the odd, independent, interesting one. Attraction runs through ideas, and closeness that comes too early can feel like a cage."},"pisces":{"en":"Venus in Pisces loves without edges: romantic, devoted, moved to tears by a song. Kindness runs high, and so can the urge to rescue someone who shows no sign of changing."}},"retro":{"1":{"en":"A time to review how you look and present yourself: the haircut you miss, the style you outgrew, the habit of shrinking to be liked. The drastic fringe can wait."},"2":{"en":"Money and self-worth ask for a second look: the subscription you forgot, the thing you returned and still want, the rate you’ve charged for years. It’s a good moment to read the bank statement before buying anything big."},"3":{"en":"Old conversations are worth revisiting: the sibling you stopped calling, the message you never answered. If an ex’s “hey, stranger” appears, there’s no hurry to reply; a kind word doesn’t have to become a reunion."},"4":{"en":"This review season turns towards family history: the parent you’ve half forgiven, the flat you left too fast, the childhood dish you can’t get right. Repairing and rearranging suit it better than hurrying into a new lease."},"5":{"en":"A season for old pleasures and the memory of old flames. If the guitar under the bed catches your eye, pick it up; if an ex likes your story at 1 a.m., think twice."},"6":{"en":"Old habits around work and health are up for review: the job you tolerate, the routine you abandoned, the colleague you never quite made peace with. The season favours revising over quitting in a mood."},"7":{"en":"Old love stories are traditionally reread in this season: the argument you two never finished, the pattern you repeat with new faces. If an ex suggests coffee, listen fully and decide nothing over the first cup."},"8":{"en":"The review here traditionally covers debts of every kind: money you lent and stopped mentioning, the card you’re still paying off, the person you shut out without a word. It invites honesty before any new joint arrangement."},"9":{"en":"An old belief or a far-off place may tug at you: the course you abandoned, the city you loved at twenty, the faith or teacher you outgrew. Revisiting them can be enough; the one-way ticket can wait."},"10":{"en":"Unfinished business at work is worth a look: the job you left with regret, the ambition you shelved to seem easygoing. If a former boss likes your post, reconnecting suits now; renegotiating suits the time after Venus turns direct."},"11":{"en":"Lapsed friendships may be on your mind: the friend you drifted from, the one you secretly fancied, the hope you stopped mentioning aloud. If you message one, there’s no need to rejoin the whole chat."},"12":{"en":"Buried feelings can drift closer to the surface: the ex who still turns up in your dreams, the crush you never confessed, the midnight comfort-shopping. Writing it down before telling anyone may help."}},"retroGeneral":{"en":"Roughly every eighteen months Venus appears to walk backwards for about six weeks. It is traditionally a season for second looks, not first moves: exes, old wants and old spending may come to mind, so you can ask what you value now. Astrologers suggest repairing what’s worth it and saving new vows, big purchases and drastic haircuts for later."},"station":{"retrograde":{"en":"Venus’s pause before turning back is often read as a wobble in desire. If a crush cools, the thing in your basket loses its shine or an old name surfaces, notice what you miss; love decisions can wait."},"direct":{"en":"Venus seems to pause and turn forward again, a moment traditionally read as clarifying. It may be easier to tell which ex was nostalgia and which purchase was worth waiting for. After a few days, act on what survived the review."}}},"mars":{"planet":"mars","houses":{"1":{"en":{"theme":"A shorter fuse, a longer stride","text":"Mars is crossing your first house for six weeks or so, and it tends to register in the body first: more appetite for effort, less patience for waiting your turn. You might catch yourself starting things before you’ve finished deciding, perhaps because standing still can feel like losing. Notice whether the same heat makes you sharp with people who are simply slower. Better to burn it off in a workout than through a conversation.","scene":"Maybe you take the stairs two at a time, book a boxing class at midnight, and feel personally offended by a slow cashier.","do":"Book one workout hard enough to leave you quiet afterwards.","avoid":"Snapping at people for not moving at your speed.","ask":"What have you been waiting for permission to start?"}},"2":{"en":{"theme":"Fighting for what you’re worth","text":"Mars in your second house tends to turn money into a matter of pride. These weeks can bring up the wish to earn more, charge more, and stop doing the favour-priced work you quietly resent. Often the push comes from a simple place: being tired of feeling cheap in your own eyes. Notice whether the same mood starts doing the spending, buying the expensive thing to prove a point nobody asked you to make.","scene":"Say you open the invoice you’ve sent the same client for two years, look at the rate, and, for once, change the number.","do":"Name a higher price out loud and stop talking.","avoid":"Rage-buying something expensive after a bad day at work.","ask":"Where are you still accepting less because asking feels rude?"}},"3":{"en":{"theme":"Typing faster than you think","text":"Mars in your third house tends to speed up your mouth, your thumbs and your driving. You might catch replies coming out sharper than you meant, a debate brewing in the comments, the commute turning into a contest with every car that cuts in. Perhaps months of held-back opinions have loosened the lid. The speed is better spent learning something hands-on than winning a text argument with your brother.","scene":"Say you rewrite a reply to a neighbour four times, each version shorter and colder, then send the coldest one.","do":"Wait ten minutes before sending anything you typed while annoyed.","avoid":"Firing off replies faster than you can read them.","ask":"Which conversation are you rehearsing instead of having?"}},"4":{"en":{"theme":"Friction under your own roof","text":"Mars in your fourth house brings heat indoors. It can stir the urge to fix the dripping tap, repaint the hallway, throw out the boxes you’ve moved twice, and also a readiness to bristle at a parent’s tone or a flatmate’s dishes. Old family tempers can flicker back to life, perhaps because home is the one place you stop performing patience. The rooms make a better target for that force than the people living in them.","scene":"It could be as small as clearing one kitchen drawer at ten at night, and by midnight the whole cupboard is on the floor.","do":"Pick one repair at home and finish it this week.","avoid":"Reopening the oldest family argument over Sunday dinner.","ask":"What at home have you been tolerating that you could actually fix?"}},"5":{"en":{"theme":"When desire stops waiting to be asked","text":"Mars in your fifth house puts desire up front: attraction, flirting, sex, the thrill of a risk you usually talk yourself out of. The first move may feel easier, and creative work tends to go faster with something to win. Perhaps the pull comes from being tired of wanting things politely. Notice the competitive streak: a board game with the kids or a five-a-side match can become a contest you didn’t need to win.","scene":"Picture texting first, suggesting the bar instead of the café, and enjoying the small jolt of not knowing their answer.","do":"Make the first move on something you want, a person or a project.","avoid":"Turning a friendly game into a grudge match.","ask":"What would you go after if looking foolish cost nothing?"}},"6":{"en":{"theme":"Racing through the to-do list","text":"Mars is moving through your sixth house, the part of your life made of work hours, chores and the body’s maintenance. These weeks favour clearing a backlog that would normally take a month, and hard training can feel good rather than punishing. If busyness is what calms you, colleagues who work at a normal pace may start to look lazy. Notice what the sprint asks of your back and your lunch break.","scene":"It might look like clearing the inbox before your coffee cools, snapping at the printer, and still feeling annoyed that a colleague left at five.","do":"Do the dreaded task first, then stop at a set time.","avoid":"Judging colleagues by how fast they reply to you.","ask":"What are you trying to outrun by staying this busy?"}},"7":{"en":{"theme":"When a partner turns sparring partner","text":"Mars in your seventh house turns up the heat in your closest one-to-one bonds: partners, business allies, rivals. Directness tends to rise on both sides, yours included, and friction and attraction both sit closer to the surface. Sometimes it can seem that the person across the table is carrying the anger you’re too polite to own. Fair disagreement, settled the same day, can leave a contract or a relationship clearer.","scene":"Perhaps you argue about whose turn it is to book the holiday and realise halfway through it’s about something older.","do":"Say what you want in one sentence, without the backstory.","avoid":"Letting your partner carry anger that is actually yours.","ask":"What do you want from them that you haven’t asked for directly?"}},"8":{"en":{"theme":"Debts, desire and the joint account","text":"Mars in your eighth house turns attention to what’s shared: the joint account, the loan, the tax form, the deep end of intimacy. You may want the truth about who owes whom and feel less willing to pretend a debt or a trust problem isn’t there. Desire can run strong and possessive, perhaps because closeness feels safer when you’re the one in control. The paperwork is worth tackling; sex and money make poor leverage.","scene":"Suppose you open the tax letter that’s sat sealed for a week, call the bank, and feel oddly turned on by your own nerve.","do":"Write down every debt you owe and every one owed to you.","avoid":"Using money or sex to win a quiet power struggle.","ask":"Where are you holding on to control because trusting feels unsafe?"}},"9":{"en":{"theme":"Restless for a bigger map","text":"Mars in your ninth house can make your world feel too small. It stirs the wish to book the flight, start the course, pitch the article, or win the argument about politics at the dinner table. Often the push comes from a fear of staying the same person in the same town forever. A goal with a deadline gives it somewhere to go; without one, notice if it slides into preaching at whoever sits closest.","scene":"It might start as a polite comment under a news post; twenty minutes later you’re drafting a full essay with sources.","do":"Set a date for the course or trip you keep researching.","avoid":"Trying to convert people who never asked for your opinion.","ask":"Where would you go if the only price were nerve?"}},"10":{"en":{"theme":"Ambition with its sleeves rolled up","text":"Mars in your tenth house, the house of career, can make ambition feel physical. You might find yourself wanting the promotion, the bigger client, the title on the door, and readier to say so in the meeting than to grumble in the corridor later. Perhaps part of the drive is anger at being underestimated. Spend it on work people can see; clashes with bosses are worth choosing as if each one goes on your record.","scene":"Imagine answering your boss’s vague email with three bullet points and a deadline, and feeling a small thrill as you press send.","do":"Ask for the role, raise or project you want, by name.","avoid":"Taking on your boss in public when a private word would do.","ask":"Who are you still trying to prove wrong with your work?"}},"11":{"en":{"theme":"Rallying the group, or rowing with it","text":"Mars in your eleventh house puts fire into friendships, teams and the plans you share with them. You might catch yourself organising the fundraiser, starting the running club or rewriting the group project at 1 a.m. Often the drive comes from wanting the future sooner than other people seem to. Notice where impatience starts overruling the group you meant to lead, and the friends in it.","scene":"It could start with one small change you suggest in the group chat, and by evening you’re somehow running the whole thing.","do":"Ask a friend to train, build or plan something with you.","avoid":"Treating friends’ slower pace as a lack of loyalty.","ask":"Which friend would you want beside you in a real fight?"}},"12":{"en":{"theme":"When anger keeps you up at night","text":"Mars in your twelfth house tends to send your drive underground. Perhaps you feel tired without a clear reason, sleep badly, or notice irritation leaking out as sarcasm where the direct thing went unsaid. This stretch favours working behind the scenes, alone, without needing anyone to watch. Swim, walk, lift: a private outlet for the body gives unspoken anger somewhere to go other than 3 a.m.","scene":"Picture lying awake replaying a conversation from Tuesday, polishing the sharp reply you didn’t send, word by perfect word.","do":"Write the angry letter by hand, then put it in a drawer.","avoid":"Swallowing anger all day and chewing on it at night.","ask":"What are you angry about that you haven’t admitted to anyone?"}}},"signs":{"aries":{"en":"Mars in Aries is at home: fast, direct, first through the door. Courage comes easily here and patience less so; anger tends to flare and cool within the hour."},"taurus":{"en":"Mars in Taurus is slow to start and hard to stop: it builds with its hands, savours long dinners and slow sex, and tends to dig in when pushed."},"gemini":{"en":"Mars in Gemini fights with words: quick replies, sharp jokes, ten tabs open at once. Drive scatters easily, so one finished task can be worth five brilliant starts."},"cancer":{"en":"Mars in Cancer fights for its people and tends to sulk before it shouts. Anger slips out sideways, as a slammed cupboard or a cold silence; name the hurt underneath."},"leo":{"en":"Mars in Leo wants to win where people can see it. Generous, proud, theatrical in a quarrel, it often works hardest for applause and bristles fastest when ignored."},"virgo":{"en":"Mars in Virgo fights by fixing. Effort tends to go into lists, systems and the gym routine, and anger can surface as criticism of how someone loaded the dishwasher."},"libra":{"en":"Mars in Libra dislikes open conflict and fights for fairness instead. Decisions can stall while it weighs both sides, and anger may wait a long time behind a polite smile."},"scorpio":{"en":"Mars in Scorpio is patient, private and relentless. Desire runs deep, grudges tend to last, and it would rather wait a month for the right move than waste one."},"sagittarius":{"en":"Mars in Sagittarius aims far: big plans, long hikes, blunt truths. It fights for beliefs, can get bored halfway, and is apt to say the tactless thing with a grin."},"capricorn":{"en":"Mars in Capricorn is traditionally at its best: disciplined, strategic, built for the long climb. It tends to keep its temper, meet deadlines and quietly outwork louder people."},"aquarius":{"en":"Mars in Aquarius fights for causes and against being told what to do. Cool in a row, stubborn about principle, its instinct is to rebel first and explain later."},"pisces":{"en":"Mars in Pisces moves like water: indirect, intuitive, easily worn down. It often fights for the underdog, sidesteps confrontation and works best through music, swimming or care."}},"retro":{"1":{"en":"Your own drive comes up for review. If stamina dips or an old ache speaks up, take the hint; a start you rushed earlier may ask to be done properly. Think lighter weights and better form."},"2":{"en":"A season for revisiting money battles: the raise you didn’t push for, the debt you argued about, the purchase you made out of spite. Calm renegotiation suits it better than rage-quitting a steady income."},"3":{"en":"Old arguments by text are worth a second look: the sibling, the neighbour, the unanswered thread. Notice what car repairs and commute delays do to your temper, and reread before you send, then reread again."},"4":{"en":"If family tempers from years ago return to the kitchen table, this season invites you to let old rows end differently. It favours finishing the half-finished home project before starting the renovation."},"5":{"en":"An old flame, a dropped creative project, a risk you backed out of: traditionally a time to look again. If a rematch tempts you, ask whether you still want it or only want to win."},"6":{"en":"Stalled work and dropped training plans are back under review. If an old colleague conflict stirs, notice what stayed unfinished; the body tends to want recovery more than new records. Mend the routine rather than overhaul it."},"7":{"en":"An old fight with a partner, ex or rival, or a stalled contract needing new terms, may be up for review. Before you argue, check whether you’re fighting this person or someone from before."},"8":{"en":"A traditional season for reviewing old debts, tax questions and unfinished conversations about trust. If desire cools or grows complicated, give it time. Settle the paperwork and step out of the old power struggle."},"9":{"en":"Worth revisiting now: a course you quit, a trip that fell through, a visa or legal matter that wants a second round. It favours reworking the plan over arguing about who was right."},"10":{"en":"Career battles invite a second, calmer look: the promotion that went elsewhere, the boss you clashed with, the project that stalled. Rework the pitch quietly: prepare the move now, make it once Mars turns direct."},"11":{"en":"A friendship that cooled after a row, or a group plan that stalled, may ask for another look. Rejoin, repair or leave cleanly; the old argument by message can stay where it is."},"12":{"en":"Buried anger can be easier to notice at night: in dreams, in sleepless hours, in a grudge you thought you’d dropped. Work on it privately: a long walk, a trusted friend, a page of honest writing."}},"retroGeneral":{"en":"Every two years or so, Mars appears to move backwards for about ten weeks. Astrologers traditionally read it as a review season: drive tends to slow, old anger is easier to notice, stalled projects ask for another look. It suits finishing, repairing, rebuilding fitness and rematching with a better plan more than picking new fights or launching on impulse."},"station":{"retrograde":{"en":"Mars appears to stall before turning backwards, and the days around it are often likened to pressing the accelerator in neutral. If tempers run short, hold off on the fight or the big launch."},"direct":{"en":"Mars appears to stand still and turn forward again. This is read as the moment the stalled project, the delayed decision or the postponed conversation can move, slowly at first. Give it a week before pushing at full speed."}}},"jupiter":{"planet":"jupiter","houses":{"1":{"en":{"theme":"Permission to take up more room","text":"Jupiter in your first house is traditionally read as a year for taking up more room: letting yourself be seen, warming a conversation as you walk in, treating a fresh start as less of a gamble. Much of it is permission, which begins when you stop waiting to be asked. Notice the pull towards size for its own sake: more plans, more yeses, more second helpings than one body and one calendar can carry.","scene":"Perhaps you turn up to a party where you know nobody and leave with two new numbers and a plan for Thursday.","do":"Start the project you keep calling “someday”.","avoid":"Saying yes to every offer simply because it flatters you.","ask":"What would you start this year if you trusted yourself a little more?"}},"2":{"en":{"theme":"Knowing what your work is worth","text":"With Jupiter in your house of money, this year draws attention to earning more and, just as often, to spending more. Asking for a raise, a better rate or a second client can feel easier once you believe your work is worth it. It’s easy to miss the quiet inflation: the pay rise that vanishes into nicer coffee, a bigger phone and a subscription you forgot you had.","scene":"Picture quoting a higher rate than last year, holding your breath, and the client simply replying, “Fine, send the invoice.”","do":"Write down what share of any extra income you’d like to keep.","avoid":"Spending a raise in your head before it reaches your payslip.","ask":"What would you charge if you were sure your work was worth it?"}},"3":{"en":{"theme":"Every errand as a small lesson","text":"Jupiter in your third house can turn your everyday radius into a classroom: the commute, the group chat, the neighbour, the sibling you only text on birthdays. This year tends to teach fastest through doing — a short course, a weekend trip, the newsletter you’ve meant to start. Curiosity is often generous but unfocused, so you might catch it scattering into twelve open tabs, three half-finished courses and a phone that never stops buzzing.","scene":"Maybe, on the train home, you sign up for a weekend course, then text your brother to ask if he wants to come.","do":"Choose one course or skill and finish it before starting another.","avoid":"Making promises in group chats that slip your mind by Friday.","ask":"What could you learn this year just by doing it every day?"}},"4":{"en":{"theme":"Room for a bigger table at home","text":"Jupiter in your fourth house turns the year towards the most private part of life: the flat, the family, the place you go when the door closes. Traditionally it’s a year for moving, renovating, taking in a relative or making peace with a parent, often because you want a base that feels generous rather than merely adequate. Worth asking is whether you’re building more house than your life needs, or your budget allows.","scene":"Say you’re standing in an empty flat with a tape measure, already deciding where the long table goes and who sits at it.","do":"Mend or upgrade the one thing at home you use every day.","avoid":"Filling the house with guests until there is no room for you.","ask":"What would make your home feel generous rather than just good enough?"}},"5":{"en":{"theme":"Pleasure without needing an excuse","text":"Jupiter in your fifth house is often read as a year of more: more flirting, more making, more nights out, more time on the floor with a child or a project you love. Joy can come more easily once you stop rationing it like a reward for finished work. If you find yourself chasing the high — the bet, the crush, the third bottle — perhaps the quieter pleasure was the real one.","scene":"It could be as small as posting the drawing you nearly deleted and, by evening, three strangers asking whether you take commissions.","do":"Book one evening a week for something you do purely for joy.","avoid":"Raising the stakes every time something starts to feel good.","ask":"What did you love doing before anyone paid or praised you for it?"}},"6":{"en":{"theme":"Better work, not just more","text":"Jupiter in your sixth house tends to enlarge the ordinary week: more tasks, more requests, and sometimes a better job or a colleague who teaches you to do it well. Your body may respond quickly to small good habits this year — a walk, earlier sleep, a real lunch. Notice whether being useful has started to feel like a privilege, so that you keep saying yes until the calendar has no empty squares left.","scene":"You might catch yourself agreeing to cover a colleague’s project, then noticing it’s the fourth extra thing you’ve taken on this month.","do":"Keep one daily habit small enough to do on your worst day.","avoid":"Taking on extra work just because you’re the one who can.","ask":"Which part of your workday would you keep even if nobody noticed?"}},"7":{"en":{"theme":"What other people bring out in you","text":"Jupiter in your seventh house puts the people beside you at the centre of the year: a partner, a business ally, a good lawyer, a friend turned collaborator. You tend to grow when someone takes you seriously, and you may be unusually open to a person who sees more in you than you do. You might catch yourself handing them the steering wheel, or signing a generous-looking contract you haven’t read to the end.","scene":"It might look like coffee with an old friend who says, “We should do this together,” and for once you both mean it.","do":"Read every contract to the last page before you sign it.","avoid":"Mistaking someone’s generosity towards you for a plan for your life.","ask":"Who brings out the version of you that you’d like to keep?"}},"8":{"en":{"theme":"Growth through what you share","text":"Jupiter in your eighth house brings into view what you share: a partner’s income, a loan, a grant, a family sum, a debt you’d like to see shrink. Closeness can deepen too, when you’re willing to say what you usually swallow. Credit may feel easy this year, and it’s worth noticing that borrowing on optimism is still borrowing: the bill outlasts the mood.","scene":"Perhaps you and your partner open the banking app together, and this time the conversation ends in a plan instead of a silence.","do":"Before borrowing, write down how and when you’d pay it back.","avoid":"Borrowing on the strength of a good mood.","ask":"What would you share more freely if you trusted it to return?"}},"9":{"en":{"theme":"Widening the map you live by","text":"Jupiter is at home in your ninth house, and the year invites distance: a long flight, a degree, a teacher who rearranges your thinking, the book you’ve long meant to write. Growth tends to come from stepping outside the language and habits you were raised in. Its shadow is the tourist of meaning, always booking the next trip or course and preaching last month’s discovery to people who never asked.","scene":"Picture a map spread over the kitchen table at midnight, and you realise you’re no longer asking whether to go, only when.","do":"Book the trip or send the application you’ve circled for over a year.","avoid":"Collecting certificates instead of using what you already know.","ask":"Which place or subject keeps pulling at you, year after year?"}},"10":{"en":{"theme":"Letting your name travel further","text":"Jupiter at the top of your chart favours being seen for your work: a promotion, a bigger client, a boss who mentions you in rooms you’re not in. Ambition can feel less like greed and more like an invitation it would be rude to refuse. Every title on offer can be tempting, yet a bigger role brings a bigger inbox, and applause is a poor substitute for evenings you no longer have.","scene":"Maybe your manager forwards you an email with one line typed on top: “They asked for you by name.”","do":"Put your name on the work you’ve been doing anonymously.","avoid":"Accepting a bigger title without asking what it costs in hours.","ask":"What do you want to be known for in five years?"}},"11":{"en":{"theme":"Finding the right crowd","text":"Jupiter in your eleventh house tends to fill the year with people: a new circle, a club, a team, a friend of a friend who knows exactly whom you should meet. Plans that felt like daydreams can start to look possible once you say them aloud to the right group. Saying yes to every invitation can leave you with two hundred contacts and nobody to call at 2 a.m.","scene":"Say you mention a half-formed idea at a birthday dinner, and someone across the table says, “I know exactly who you should meet.”","do":"Say your biggest plan aloud to three people who could help.","avoid":"Collecting new contacts while old friends quietly go silent.","ask":"Which friendship do you want to still have in ten years?"}},"12":{"en":{"theme":"Growing where nobody can see","text":"Jupiter in your twelfth house is often a quieter chapter, with growth taking place offstage: in therapy, in long sleep, in a notebook, in help you give without credit. Traditionally this placement is read as quiet protection, as if someone were looking after you behind the scenes, which can make retreat feel safe. Notice when rest starts turning into hiding — another episode, another glass, another month of not saying what you want.","scene":"Perhaps you cancel a plan, sleep ten hours and wake knowing the answer to something you’ve circled for months.","do":"Protect one hour a week alone, with no screen.","avoid":"Helping everyone in secret and resenting that nobody notices.","ask":"What are you quietly preparing for that you haven’t said out loud?"}}},"signs":{"aries":{"en":"Jupiter in Aries champions whoever goes first: new businesses, bold applications, solo starts. Courage tends to be contagious, though notice how much more gets started than finished."},"taurus":{"en":"Jupiter in Taurus values what you can touch: savings, property, gardens, good bread. Comfort can feel earned and solid, while appetites for money and dinner tend to grow quietly."},"gemini":{"en":"Jupiter in Gemini tends to multiply everything: courses, chats, side projects, opinions. Learning can feel quick and curiosity generous, though facts and gossip often travel at the same speed."},"cancer":{"en":"Jupiter in Cancer turns growth towards home: families, kitchens, roots, the urge to protect one’s own. Generosity often flows most easily towards kin, and nostalgia has unusual pull."},"leo":{"en":"Jupiter in Leo tends to make generosity theatrical: big gestures, brave creative work, birthday parties that get out of hand. Warmth spreads fast, and so can the appetite for applause."},"virgo":{"en":"Jupiter in Virgo seeks growth through improvement: better systems, cleaner diets, useful skills, honest work. Progress lives in the details, and so, often, does the urge to fix everyone."},"libra":{"en":"Jupiter in Libra favours partnerships, contracts, weddings and good design. Diplomacy is valued, fairness tends to come into fashion, and plenty of people say yes just to keep the peace."},"scorpio":{"en":"Jupiter in Scorpio deepens rather than widens: investments, inheritances, therapy, research, long-kept secrets. People tend to grow by facing their fears, and power is often read as gathering in fewer hands."},"sagittarius":{"en":"Jupiter in Sagittarius is at home, and travel, study, publishing, faith and big opinions tend to flourish. Optimism often runs high, with a matching taste for preaching."},"capricorn":{"en":"Jupiter in Capricorn tends to grow only what is earned: careers, institutions, long-term plans. Progress here looks like patient work, and optimism wears a suit and checks the budget."},"aquarius":{"en":"Jupiter in Aquarius draws attention to networks: communities, technology, causes, unlikely friendships. The future can feel shared and exciting, though ideals sometimes outrun the people meant to live by them."},"pisces":{"en":"Jupiter in Pisces is traditionally read as generous compassion and thin boundaries: art, music, charity, faith, long sleep. Kindness spreads easily; notice whether escapism and wishful thinking spread with it."}},"retroGeneral":{"en":"For about four months each year Jupiter turns retrograde, a stretch traditionally read as growth turning inward. The emphasis shifts from reaching out to review: the course, the move, the yes you gave too fast. It invites you to check whether what you’re growing is still what you want, and to keep only that."},"station":{"retrograde":{"en":"Jupiter seems to stand still before turning retrograde. For a few months big plans may feel less urgent, which makes this a good moment to stop adding and check what you’ve already said yes to."},"direct":{"en":"Jupiter stations direct, a turn often read as permission to move again, now with clearer judgement. Of the plans you’ve been reconsidering, notice which survived your doubts; this month favours giving it a real start."}}},"saturn":{"planet":"saturn","houses":{"1":{"en":{"theme":"Becoming someone you can rely on","text":"Saturn crossing your first house opens a chapter of two or three years that draws attention to growing up a little more in public. It can feel heavier, as if you were being tested, and charm alone may not carry you as far as it used to. What you build now — a body you look after, a way of saying no, a reputation for finishing — can become the foundation of the next decade.","scene":"Perhaps you turn down a fun but pointless plan, and for once you don’t feel the need to over-explain why.","do":"Pick one commitment to yourself and keep it every day this week.","avoid":"Mistaking tiredness for proof that you’re failing.","ask":"What would the most reliable version of you do differently this month?"}},"2":{"en":{"theme":"Putting a floor under your money","text":"Saturn in your second house is traditionally read as a slow lesson, over two or three years, in what money is actually for. Income can feel capped and you might catch yourself weighing every purchase, perhaps because some part of you is braced for not having enough. The chapter favours building a floor: savings you don’t touch, a price you can defend, a worth that isn’t your balance. Notice whether caution is turning into stinginess, with others and with yourself.","scene":"You might catch yourself walking past something you’d have bought without thinking a year ago, and the small “no” feels surprisingly good.","do":"Write down what “enough” means to you, in real numbers.","avoid":"Undercharging because asking for more feels like asking for trouble.","ask":"What do you buy to feel safe, and does it work?"}},"3":{"en":{"theme":"When words carry more weight","text":"Saturn in your third house tends to slow the fast lane of life: messages, errands, the commute, the sibling who needs you. You might find yourself thinking twice before you hit send, because careless words seem to cost more than they used to. It’s a good chapter for a hard, slow skill — a language, a driving test, a qualification. It’s worth noticing if you stay silent until you sound perfect.","scene":"Say you rewrite a two-line message to your sister three times and cut the sarcasm, and for once the reply is kind.","do":"Give one hard skill fifteen minutes a day, every day.","avoid":"Sending important messages late at night, angry or exhausted.","ask":"What would you say more often if you weren’t afraid of sounding wrong?"}},"4":{"en":{"theme":"Fixing the roof yourself","text":"Saturn in your fourth house draws attention to the foundations: the lease or mortgage, the boiler, the parent who needs more from you, the family rule you’ve outgrown. Home can feel more like a job than a refuge, perhaps because you’re now fixing what used to be fixed for you. What you build here can hold for decades. You might catch yourself running your home the way a strict parent would.","scene":"It might look like sitting at your parents’ kitchen table with their bills spread out, realising you’re the one explaining things now.","do":"Fix the one thing at home you’ve been stepping around for months.","avoid":"Carrying the family’s problems as if nobody else could.","ask":"Which family rule are you still obeying that no longer fits your life?"}},"5":{"en":{"theme":"Turning play into craft","text":"Saturn in your fifth house brings pleasure into view as a decision: a hobby that wants to become a craft, a romance that asks for commitment, a child who needs a firmer you. Fun can go flat for a while, often because a fear of being judged sits in the front row whenever you play. What this chapter can build is creative work you’re proud of, made slowly, and a love that survives an ordinary Tuesday.","scene":"Maybe you practise the same song every evening for a month, badly, until one night it starts to sound like music.","do":"Put creative practice in your calendar like a meeting you can’t move.","avoid":"Quitting something you love because you’re not good at it yet.","ask":"What would you make if nobody you knew ever saw it?"}},"6":{"en":{"theme":"When routine becomes your backbone","text":"Saturn in your sixth house makes the daily grind the main subject: the weight of the workload, a demanding manager, a body less forgiving of late nights and skipped lunches. Your back, teeth or sleep can become the place where years of “I’ll deal with it later” are felt. Habits started in this chapter tend to stick. Notice whether you’re proving your worth in overtime, as if exhaustion were a qualification.","scene":"It could be as small as booking the dentist you’ve postponed for two years and, while you’re at it, the physiotherapist.","do":"Fix your bedtime and keep it, weekends included.","avoid":"Putting your body last because you’re too busy to be ill.","ask":"Which daily habit would your body thank you for in five years?"}},"7":{"en":{"theme":"Promises you can actually keep","text":"Saturn in your seventh house brings into view how much weight your closest bonds can carry: the relationship, the business partner, the deal you’ve lived on without writing down. Over these two or three years, half-promises can feel harder to live with, and the question becomes whether to commit, renegotiate or walk away. Perhaps part of you fears being trapped and part fears being left, and both can make you go quiet. What you choose to keep can be built to last.","scene":"Picture you and your partner sitting down with a notepad to say out loud who pays for what, and who does what.","do":"Put one unspoken agreement with your partner into plain words.","avoid":"Keeping the peace by not saying what you need.","ask":"What are you willing to promise, and what are you no longer willing to?"}},"8":{"en":{"theme":"Paying down what you owe","text":"Saturn in your eighth house draws attention to the paperwork of closeness: the loan, the tax return, the joint account, sometimes an inheritance or an estate to sort out. The chapter favours paying down debts, money and otherwise, slowly and on schedule. Intimacy can grow more honest, because trust tends to grow only as fast as it’s earned, on both sides. Part of the work is noticing the pull to control everything so nothing can hurt you.","scene":"Imagine making the last payment on a card you’ve carried for years, then sitting in the car for a minute, oddly emotional.","do":"List every debt you have, with dates, on one page.","avoid":"Lending money you can’t spare just to keep the peace.","ask":"Who has earned your trust slowly, and have you told them?"}},"9":{"en":{"theme":"Earning the right to an opinion","text":"Saturn in your ninth house tends to turn big ideas into long work: the degree, the visa, the legal case, the book that takes three drafts. Beliefs you inherited are held up against real life, and letting some of them go can feel lonelier than doubt ever did. This chapter invites you to stop quoting other people and become someone worth quoting. If a rulebook starts to replace thinking, that rigidity is worth noticing.","scene":"It might be eleven at night when you close the textbook and realise you can now explain what baffled you three months ago.","do":"Choose one long course of study and pencil in a weekly time for it.","avoid":"Defending a belief you’ve never tested yourself.","ask":"Which of your opinions have you actually earned?"}},"10":{"en":{"theme":"A title that comes with weight","text":"Saturn at the top of your chart is traditionally read as both a harvest of years of work and an audit. It draws attention to responsibility — a bigger role, a team, a decision with your name on it — and to whatever was built on shortcuts. You may feel watched, as if people now judge you by your record, not your promise. Steadiness here can grow into the authority you once had to ask for.","scene":"Perhaps, in a meeting, the room goes quiet and turns to you, and you realise they’re waiting for your decision, not your opinion.","do":"Finish what has your name on it before starting anything new.","avoid":"Taking every criticism as a verdict on your whole career.","ask":"Which responsibility are you ready to carry, and which should you hand back?"}},"11":{"en":{"theme":"Noticing who really turns up","text":"Saturn in your eleventh house brings the shape of your circle into view: a friendship that fades, a group chat gone quiet, a smaller and sturdier circle that remains. You might also find yourself running things — the committee, the team, the shared project nobody else wants to organise. Any loneliness in this chapter can be useful, because it shows you who turns up. Long-term hopes can grow serious too: fewer of them, with real dates attached.","scene":"You might notice it’s the same three friends who always reply, show up and stay to help clear the table.","do":"Turn up, in person, for the friends who always turn up for you.","avoid":"Keeping friendships alive out of guilt rather than warmth.","ask":"Who would you trust with your house keys, and do they know?"}},"12":{"en":{"theme":"Closing the old chapter properly","text":"Saturn in your twelfth house is traditionally read as the quiet end of a long cycle: a couple of years for finishing, clearing out and sleeping more than you’d admit. Old fears and unsaid things can surface at 3 a.m., not to punish you but perhaps because they were never dealt with. It favours closing old accounts: the therapy, the apology, the boxes from your last move. Notice the urge to launch something big before the old is done.","scene":"Picture opening the drawer of letters you’ve avoided for a year and dealing with them, one envelope at a time.","do":"Finish or honestly drop one old project this month.","avoid":"Drowning out the quiet with noise, plans and screens.","ask":"What are you still carrying that you could put down this year?"}}},"signs":{"aries":{"en":"Saturn in Aries is read as slowing the sprint: it favours fresh starts built to last and leaders measured by what they finish. Disciplined courage tends to count for more than impatience."},"taurus":{"en":"Saturn in Taurus tends to make money, land and food serious subjects: budgets, prices and the question of what lasts. It favours security built slowly, by hand."},"gemini":{"en":"Saturn in Gemini brings discipline to information: rules for schools, media and platforms come into focus. It favours fewer words carrying more weight, and slower, deeper, more exact learning."},"cancer":{"en":"Saturn in Cancer puts weight on home and family: housing costs, ageing parents, the care nobody pays for. Feelings tend to be guarded, and belonging becomes something to build on purpose."},"leo":{"en":"Saturn in Leo asks for authority without applause: it invites talent to become craft and leaders to earn their stage, and it brings pride under review. Even joy can take discipline."},"virgo":{"en":"Saturn in Virgo draws attention to the daily systems: health care, working conditions, standards, small print. Craft and reliability tend to earn respect, while perfectionism and worry can run high."},"libra":{"en":"Saturn in Libra brings relationships and agreements under review: contracts, courts, marriages, alliances. It frames fairness as something built in writing, not just expected."},"scorpio":{"en":"Saturn in Scorpio is read as bringing debts, taxes, power and secrets into hard light. Trust tends to be earned slowly, and what was hidden can ask to be settled."},"sagittarius":{"en":"Saturn in Sagittarius holds beliefs up against facts: universities, courts, churches and borders come under scrutiny. Optimism asks for evidence, and teachers are invited to live what they preach."},"capricorn":{"en":"Saturn in Capricorn is at home: institutions, careers and long plans invite rebuilding from the foundations. It honours hard work, shows the limits of shortcuts and asks ambition to grow up."},"aquarius":{"en":"Saturn in Aquarius is read as building the future by committee: rules for technology, communities and networks. It invites ideals to become working systems, and independence to learn cooperation."},"pisces":{"en":"Saturn in Pisces puts edges on what usually drifts: care work, art, faith, sleep, the screen at 2 a.m. It suggests that compassion needs limits, and dreams a schedule."}},"retroGeneral":{"en":"For four to five months each year Saturn turns retrograde, and the inspection is read as moving indoors. It invites a quiet stress test of what you’ve built — the routine, the promise, the five-year plan — a chance to mend what is cracking while it is small and hand back the jobs that were never yours."},"station":{"retrograde":{"en":"Saturn seems to stand still before turning retrograde, and these days are often read as heavy: deadlines can press harder and old responsibilities ask for review. A moment to reinforce what carries weight before taking on more."},"direct":{"en":"Saturn turns direct after months of review. What you repaired may feel able to carry weight again. The station favours commitment and setting the schedule; decisions made around it are traditionally read as long-lasting."}}},"uranus":{"planet":"uranus","houses":{"1":{"en":{"theme":"When the old image stops fitting","text":"Uranus in your first house is traditionally read as roughly seven years in which the person you show the world stops fitting. A haircut, a new handle online, a body you treat differently, an unplanned “I’m not doing that any more”: change here tends to move in jolts rather than plans. Underneath, perhaps, is a need to look like who you’ve become, not who you were. Notice whether you’re rebelling against people who were only describing you.","scene":"Picture yourself in the hairdresser’s chair asking for the cut you’ve wanted for years; their hesitation only makes you surer.","do":"Drop one habit you keep only because people expect it.","avoid":"Torching good things just to prove you’re free.","ask":"Which part of how people see you no longer feels true?"}},"2":{"en":{"theme":"Income in an unfamiliar shape","text":"For about seven years Uranus crosses your second house, an era that tends to unsettle the shape of earning you grew up with. It might look like a salary turning into invoices, a side project out-earning the job, a windfall and a lost contract in the same season. Often the deeper wish is to earn in a way that feels like yours, not merely safe. You might catch yourself reading every swing as a sign to quit.","scene":"Say you compare this month’s income with last month’s, find no pattern at all, and feel more curious than scared.","do":"Work out what one lean month would actually cost you.","avoid":"Selling something you love in a panicked week.","ask":"What would you earn money doing if nobody needed to approve it?"}},"3":{"en":{"theme":"A mind tired of its old routes","text":"These years Uranus runs through your house of messages, neighbours and siblings, and your mind often grows restless on its familiar tracks. Perhaps you learn a skill from videos at 1 am, rethink a view you’ve held since school, or find a sibling easier, or harder, to talk to. Thinking can speed up because it’s bored, not because it’s sure. Worth noticing: the urge to send the message while it’s still hot.","scene":"Maybe on the bus an idea strikes you so sharply that you voice-note yourself three times before your stop.","do":"Write the idea down tonight; sleep before sending it.","avoid":"Picking fights in the comments just to feel awake.","ask":"Which opinion of yours is older than your current life?"}},"4":{"en":{"theme":"Wanting roots and an open door","text":"Uranus crossing your fourth house is roughly seven years that bring into view how settled home really feels. It can show up as the itch to move again, a parent’s circumstances shifting, someone moving in or out, the home office quietly swallowing the flat. Part of you may want roots and part of you a door you can walk out of. If “freedom” is really a way of dodging one hard conversation at home, that is worth naming.","scene":"Perhaps you’re packing boxes again, wrapping the same mugs in newspaper, and realise you’ve stopped hanging pictures because you assume you’re leaving anyway.","do":"Hang one picture, even in a flat you don’t mean to keep.","avoid":"Making every family change a reason to pack a bag.","ask":"What does home need to be now, not when you were ten?"}},"5":{"en":{"theme":"The pull of the unplanned","text":"This seven-year stretch of Uranus in your fifth house tends to loosen the script for romance, play and making things. Attraction can feel fast and strange: someone outside your type, a long-distance thing, a hobby that takes over your weekends for a year and then fades. Perhaps you want to be surprised by your own life, because predictable has started to feel like old. Notice when you’re chasing the jolt and calling it love.","scene":"It could be as small as a pottery class booked on a whim: you leave with clay under your nails and someone’s number.","do":"Book one thing this week that you’d normally talk yourself out of.","avoid":"Blowing up something steady just because it’s become familiar.","ask":"When did you last surprise yourself, and what were you doing?"}},"6":{"en":{"theme":"When the routine starts to chafe","text":"These are the years Uranus moves through your sixth house: the job, the calendar, the body that has to keep up. Nine-to-five can start to feel like a cage, a new tool may change how you work, and sleep or nerves may ask for a schedule you didn’t choose. Often you work best when nobody stands over you. If you’re tempted to quit the job, ask whether only the timetable needs to change.","scene":"You might catch yourself moving the laptop to the kitchen at 6 am, the only hour nobody can ask you for anything.","do":"Rearrange one fixed hour of your day to suit your body.","avoid":"Treating every new rule at work as a personal insult.","ask":"Which part of your workday would you keep if you could redesign it?"}},"7":{"en":{"theme":"Closeness that needs more air","text":"For around seven years Uranus sits in your house of partners and one-to-one deals, an era that asks closeness to make room for freedom. You may be drawn to people who resist being pinned down. Shared plans can feel less fixed: a partner’s new job or city, a contract ending early, another starting within a week. The wish is for someone beside you, not breathing down your neck. Before slamming a door, ask whether it only needs to open wider.","scene":"Picture your partner booking a solo trip, and the first feeling you notice is not hurt but a strange, quiet envy.","do":"Say out loud how much time alone you need each week.","avoid":"Ending a relationship by text to skip the hard conversation.","ask":"What kind of freedom would let you stay?"}},"8":{"en":{"theme":"Freedom inside what you share","text":"Uranus moving through your eighth house is a seven-year stretch that draws attention to what you share: a joint account, a loan, a partner’s income, the trust you hand someone in bed. An inheritance, a tax bill or a debt cleared in one go can change the maths quickly. Underneath, there is often a refusal to feel owned, by a lender or by a lover. It’s worth reading the small print before cutting any ties.","scene":"It might look like reading the loan agreement line by line and realising you’ve been paying for a life you left years ago.","do":"List every shared account and subscription you’re still tied to.","avoid":"Making joint commitments in a week you feel reckless.","ask":"Whose money or approval do you still feel owned by?"}},"9":{"en":{"theme":"Outgrowing what you were taught","text":"Uranus in your ninth house is often read as some seven years of redrawing the map of what you believe. Perhaps a last-minute ticket stretches into months abroad, an online course stands in for the degree you never finished, or a faith or politics you grew up with stops making sense in one conversation. You may learn fastest when slightly lost. It helps to check whether one dogma is just being swapped for a shinier one.","scene":"Say you’re in a city where you can’t read the signs, and for the first time in years your head goes quiet.","do":"Sign up for the course you keep bookmarking.","avoid":"Lecturing friends about the worldview you adopted last month.","ask":"Which belief did you inherit rather than choose?"}},"10":{"en":{"theme":"Work beyond the job title","text":"Uranus in your tenth house is a seven-year era that makes it easier to notice how little your career wants a ladder. Perhaps you feel the pull to change fields, go freelance or be known for a side skill rather than the title; if a restructuring ends a role you’d outgrown, it may feel like release. If you’d rather be strange and respected than safe and invisible, controlling bosses can feel unbearable. The temptation is to burn a reference you’d value later.","scene":"Maybe someone asks what you do for a living, and the honest answer takes three sentences and makes you grin.","do":"Write down the work you’d do if job titles didn’t exist.","avoid":"Quitting in the meeting instead of after the plan.","ask":"What do you want to be known for that isn’t on your CV?"}},"11":{"en":{"theme":"Finding your strange people","text":"Uranus is at home in your eleventh house of friends and future plans, and for seven years or so your circle tends to reshuffle. Old friends can drift as your life changes speed, while new ones turn up through a forum, a protest, a running club, a late-night side project. You may need people who don’t flinch at the version of you that’s emerging. If a loyal friend has started to feel unexciting, consider whether the friendship changed or only your speed.","scene":"Perhaps you leave a group chat you’ve muted for a year and join a much odder one the same evening.","do":"Go once to the meetup you keep scrolling past.","avoid":"Measuring old friendships by how new they still feel.","ask":"Who gets excited when you describe the future you want?"}},"12":{"en":{"theme":"Breaking the pattern nobody sees","text":"Uranus in your twelfth house is often described as a quiet seven years lit by flashes in the dark. Sleep can go strange, insights tend to surface at 3 am, and a stranger’s offhand remark may crack open a habit you’ve repeated since childhood. Much of the rebellion stays private, perhaps because you’d rather not be watched while you’re half-changed. If a realisation keeps you awake, see what it asks of you in daylight.","scene":"Imagine waking at 3:40, seeing the old pattern with total clarity and typing it into your notes before it fades.","do":"Keep a notebook by the bed and use it tonight.","avoid":"Scrolling in the dark to drown out the restlessness.","ask":"Which habit would you break if nobody ever found out?"}}},"signs":{"aries":{"en":"Uranus’s seven-year stay in Aries is read through start-ups, protests, solo ventures and a shared hunger to be first. Patience tends to run thin, and ideas come elbows out."},"taurus":{"en":"Uranus in Taurus, a seven-year collective era, brings money, food and land into question: new currencies, unstable prices, farming rethought. What felt solid can start to look negotiable, including what’s in your wallet."},"gemini":{"en":"Uranus in Gemini is a seven-year era read as rewiring how we talk, learn and get around: new devices, AI in every inbox, faster news, transport rethought. Attention tends to scatter mid-sentence."},"cancer":{"en":"Uranus in Cancer marks a generation that rethinks home and family: new ways of living together, homes that double as offices, kinship chosen, not inherited. Belonging gets redefined at the kitchen table."},"leo":{"en":"Uranus in Leo is linked with an era that electrifies fame, art and play: new kinds of celebrity, rebellious self-expression, children raised to stand out. Many want a stage, and the stage keeps moving."},"virgo":{"en":"Uranus in Virgo draws a generation’s attention to reinventing work and health: new tools at the desk, alternative medicine, wellness gadgets, jobs automated. Routines get rebuilt, often around a machine."},"libra":{"en":"Uranus in Libra is a generational era associated with rewriting marriage and partnership: divorce growing ordinary, new kinds of couple, fairness argued in public. Relationships ask for room to breathe."},"scorpio":{"en":"Uranus in Scorpio, a generational era, tends to bring taboos into the open: sexual revolutions, financial shocks, secrets leaked overnight, buried things surfacing unannounced."},"sagittarius":{"en":"Uranus in Sagittarius stirs questions of belief and borders: cheap flights, new religions, global study, information crossing every frontier. Restlessness for the wider world can become a generation’s signature."},"capricorn":{"en":"Astrologers link Uranus in Capricorn with shaken institutions: wobbling banks, tested governments, cracking hierarchies. Its generation tends to doubt career ladders and to ask authority to earn respect again."},"aquarius":{"en":"Uranus in Aquarius, its own sign, is said to bring the future closer: networks, online communities, new social movements, technology that rewires friendship. Being different can become a group identity."},"pisces":{"en":"Uranus in Pisces is read as unsettling art, faith and escape: virtual worlds, new spiritual movements, music and film reinvented. For its generation, the line between real and imagined grows strange."}},"retroGeneral":{"en":"Every year Uranus spends about five months appearing to move backwards. Astrologers read this as the urge for change going underground: plans to quit, move or break free tend to be tested in private before anyone acts on them. It’s a good season to rethink a rebellion, finish an experiment, or notice which freedom you actually want."},"station":{"retrograde":{"en":"Uranus seems to stand still before turning back, a week or two often read as a spike of restlessness: urges to quit, cut ties, move or blurt the truth. Note them down; the ones still burning a month later are worth a serious look."},"direct":{"en":"Uranus appears to turn forward again after months read as inner rehearsal. Changes you’ve been quietly planning — the move, the new job, the clean break — may start to feel possible in daylight. If one still feels right, begin with its smallest irreversible step."}}},"neptune":{"planet":"neptune","houses":{"1":{"en":{"theme":"When your outline goes soft","text":"Neptune in your first house marks a misty decade or more that tends to soften the edges of who you are. People often see what they want in you, and because blending in can feel kinder than disagreeing, you might catch yourself becoming the mirror of whoever’s in the room. Your body can feel more sensitive: to coffee, alcohol, crowds, a sad film. Notice whether your outline is fading so slowly it goes unseen.","scene":"Picture catching your reflection in a shop window and, for a second, not being sure you look like yourself.","do":"Say one clear preference out loud today, even about lunch.","avoid":"Agreeing with everyone and calling it being easygoing.","ask":"Who are you when nobody is looking at you?"}},"2":{"en":{"theme":"The banking app you’d rather not open","text":"For well over a decade Neptune washes through your second house, and money can start to feel foggy. You might give generously, undercharge for work you love, avoid looking at your account for weeks and then wonder where it went. Perhaps part of you suspects that caring about money would make you less kind. Worth noticing whether you’ve let the fog set your worth, when a plain spreadsheet would do it better.","scene":"Say you pay for everyone’s drinks again, then check your balance in the taxi and feel a small cold drop.","do":"Look at your last month of spending, all of it, tonight.","avoid":"Working for free because asking for money feels unkind.","ask":"What would you charge if you believed your work was worth it?"}},"3":{"en":{"theme":"Hearing the tone, missing the detail","text":"For more than a decade Neptune drifts through your third house, and thinking tends to turn more image than list. You might daydream on the commute, write better at midnight than at a desk, and miss the detail in a message everyone else caught, because you’re listening to tone, not words. A sibling or neighbour can feel close one month and unreadable the next. Notice when you’re replying to what you imagined someone meant.","scene":"Maybe you reread a short text from your sister four times, hearing a different tone of voice each time.","do":"Ask what they meant before you write back.","avoid":"Signing something you’ve only skimmed on your phone.","ask":"Which conversation are you having only in your head?"}},"4":{"en":{"theme":"Home that lives in memory","text":"Neptune in your fourth house is a long chapter in which home can become partly a feeling you chase. Perhaps you live far from where you grew up, care for a parent whose needs are hard to see clearly, or cook your grandmother’s soup just to smell her kitchen again. What you miss is often a time, not a place. It’s worth asking whether you’re waiting for the perfect home instead of unpacking this one.","scene":"Picture standing in a new flat that’s perfectly fine and still feeling homesick for somewhere you can’t quite name.","do":"Make one corner of this home unmistakably yours tonight.","avoid":"Taking on a parent’s sadness as if it were yours.","ask":"What did home smell, sound or taste like when you felt safe?"}},"5":{"en":{"theme":"Falling for the person you imagine","text":"Neptune in your fifth house lays a decade or more of soft focus over romance, art and play. You might fall for who someone could be, write songs or stories you didn’t know were in you, or lose whole evenings to films, wine or a crush who never quite texts back. Being moved may matter more than being sure. Catch the moment you love the dream so hard you miss the person beside you.","scene":"Maybe you’ve built a whole future with someone from three conversations and already know which song would play at the wedding.","do":"Spend one evening making something, not consuming something.","avoid":"Rescuing a lover and calling it romance.","ask":"Do you like this person, or the story you tell about them?"}},"6":{"en":{"theme":"When days don’t hold their shape","text":"Neptune’s long stay in your sixth house, fourteen years or so, tends to dissolve the edges of your workday. Job descriptions can go vague, you might end up doing the emotional chores nobody put in your contract, and your body may react more to things it used to shrug off: caffeine, late screens, a colleague’s bad mood. You can absorb a room before you realise it. Worth asking whether helpfulness is quietly wearing you thin.","scene":"Perhaps you stay late fixing a colleague’s mistake, tell yourself it’s nothing, then lie awake with a headache.","do":"Write tomorrow’s three tasks on paper, and log off at six.","avoid":"Taking on a colleague’s mood as if it were your job.","ask":"Which part of your day leaves you drained, and why?"}},"7":{"en":{"theme":"Idealising the one you love","text":"Neptune in your seventh house is a long era, often fourteen years, when close relationships tend to be soaked in longing. You might see the best in a partner, sometimes a version only you can see, and drift towards people who seem to need saving or to read your mind. Agreements can stay unspoken because spelling them out feels unromantic. Perhaps ask whether you’re forgiving the same thing so often it has stopped being forgiveness.","scene":"Say your partner forgets the thing again, and you’re already explaining to yourself why it isn’t really their fault.","do":"Say one expectation out loud, plainly, without softening it.","avoid":"Mistaking being needed for being loved.","ask":"What do you keep forgiving that you’ve never actually discussed?"}},"8":{"en":{"theme":"Where you end and they begin","text":"For a decade and more Neptune moves through your eighth house, and the line between yours and theirs can blur. This era draws attention to the vague places: joint money, a loan to a friend that quietly becomes a gift nobody discussed, an inheritance tangled in paperwork and old family feelings. In intimacy you may want to dissolve completely and lose yourself in the trying. Ask where a feeling stands in for a written agreement.","scene":"Perhaps you lend money to someone you love, and neither of you mentions it again, though you think about it every month.","do":"Put one shared money arrangement in writing today.","avoid":"Paying someone’s debt to avoid a painful conversation.","ask":"What have you handed over that you’d like to have back?"}},"9":{"en":{"theme":"Searching for something to believe","text":"Neptune in your ninth house is a long era of searching: for a teacher, a faith, a place that feels like the answer. Perhaps you read late into the night, book a retreat, fall for a city before you’ve seen it in winter, or quietly lose a belief that held you up for years. Part of you may want meaning delivered whole. Notice whether you’re handing your judgement to the first voice that sounds certain.","scene":"It might look like a lecture at midnight, then another, and waking up having half-planned a move to a country you’ve never visited.","do":"Check one claim you’ve accepted before you share it.","avoid":"Following a teacher who discourages questions.","ask":"What are you hoping someone else can explain for you?"}},"10":{"en":{"theme":"Work that has to mean something","text":"Neptune spends well over a decade in your tenth house, and success may not feel like enough without meaning. A career that looks good on paper may feel hollow, while work in care, art, film or a cause tugs at you even when it pays less. Your public image can be harder to control: people project onto you, for better and worse. Worth seeing whether you’re waiting for a calling instead of drafting a plan.","scene":"Picture a recruiter offering more money, and you hear yourself asking whether the job helps anyone at all.","do":"Write the next practical step towards the work you dream about.","avoid":"Letting a boss’s charm stand in for a contract.","ask":"What would meaningful work look like on an ordinary Tuesday?"}},"11":{"en":{"theme":"Giving yourself to a cause","text":"Neptune in your eleventh house is a long era when friendship and the future you dream of tend to blur. You might give hours to a cause, a choir, a volunteer group or an online circle that feels like belonging. Being needed can feel so much like being wanted that it’s harder to see which friends call mainly when they want something. Consider whether a group that never asks what you need is getting everything.","scene":"Maybe you volunteer to organise the group’s fundraiser again, though last year you cried in the car afterwards.","do":"Tell one friend honestly what you need from them.","avoid":"Saying yes to every group request to feel included.","ask":"Which friendships give back, and which ones only take?"}},"12":{"en":{"theme":"The quiet that refills you","text":"Neptune in your twelfth house, its own territory, is a long era with thin walls between your feelings and everyone else’s. Dreams can turn vivid; you might cry at adverts and need more sleep and more hours alone than people around you understand. Solitude tends to refill you, but a bottle, a feed or a show at 2 am can feel the same from the inside. It helps to tell escape from rest.","scene":"It could be as small as cancelling plans, turning off every light but one and feeling the week drain from your shoulders.","do":"Book one evening alone with no screen and no drink.","avoid":"Calling it rest when it’s really hiding.","ask":"What are you trying not to feel when you reach for the phone?"}}},"signs":{"aries":{"en":"Neptune in Aries, a generational placement, tends to dream in the shape of courage: new heroes, faith in starting over, ideals that demand action. Bravery and recklessness can blur."},"taurus":{"en":"Across its fourteen-year stay, Neptune in Taurus tends to romanticise land, food and the body: slow living, real bread, money that feels solid. Comfort can become a kind of faith."},"gemini":{"en":"Neptune in Gemini is read as an era of blurred words and facts: rumours outrun news, stories feel truer than data, everyone talks at once, language turns dreamy and slippery."},"cancer":{"en":"For a generation, Neptune in Cancer tends to idealise home, homeland and mother: nostalgia runs high, families can become sanctuaries or myths, and the longing to belong somewhere is everywhere."},"leo":{"en":"Neptune in Leo is read as glamour turned into faith: film idols, grand romance, the spotlight as salvation. It can teach a generation to long for the great love story."},"virgo":{"en":"Neptune in Virgo tends to dream through work and health: duty as devotion, cures and diets as hope, service as a calling. Worry and perfectionism can seep into ordinary days."},"libra":{"en":"A generational dream of love and fairness, Neptune in Libra idealises peace songs, soulmates and the perfect partnership. Harmony can be worshipped while conflict is quietly avoided."},"scorpio":{"en":"Neptune in Scorpio tends to romanticise the forbidden: sex, death, secrets, the occult. For a generation, intensity can pass for love, and fear and desire blur in the collective imagination."},"sagittarius":{"en":"Neptune in Sagittarius is read as an era’s dream of the whole world: gap years, gurus, globalisation, faith in a future without borders, belief and wishful thinking spreading easily."},"capricorn":{"en":"Neptune in Capricorn is read as trust in institutions dissolving: banks, money and governments look like stories we agreed to believe. A generation may idealise success, then quietly doubt it."},"aquarius":{"en":"Neptune in Aquarius tends to dream of connection through machines: online utopias, global networks, faith that technology can save us. As belonging moves online, loneliness can follow it there."},"pisces":{"en":"Neptune in Pisces, its own sign, tends to flood a whole generation with feeling: streaming, escapism, spiritual searching, compassion for strangers. Boundaries can soften, and fact and fiction blur."}},"retroGeneral":{"en":"For about five months each year Neptune appears to move backwards, a season traditionally read as the fog thinning a little. Any illusion you’ve been living inside can be easier to see: the job, the person, the habit you romanticised. It favours honest reality checks, quieter faith and fewer rescues."},"station":{"retrograde":{"en":"As Neptune seems to pause before turning back, these days are often read as a thickening haze: dreams can get loud, motives blur, and it’s easy to believe what you wish. Big promises can wait for clearer days."},"direct":{"en":"Neptune turns forward, a shift often read as imagination flowing outward again. Ideals you have tested in private can go out into the world: the song, the cause, the generous act. Worth keeping the reality checks you learned."}}},"pluto":{"planet":"pluto","houses":{"1":{"en":{"theme":"When your old skin stops fitting","text":"Pluto crossing your first house is one of the longest chapters of a life, often fifteen years or more, and its subject is you. The body is often part of the story, through discipline or a change in health, as is the way people react when you walk in. You might grow more intense, harder to fool, less willing to perform. Sometimes the fear of change shows up as controlling every part of yourself.","scene":"Maybe someone from school doesn’t recognise you at first, and you realise you don’t miss the person they remember.","do":"Skip one thing today that you do only to seem harmless.","avoid":"Treating every comment about your looks as an attack.","ask":"What part of your old self are you ready to lay to rest?"}},"2":{"en":{"theme":"Weighing what you’re really worth","text":"Pluto in your second house is a long era in which money tends to become a question of power. It brings questions of earning, rebuilding and letting go into view: the income you depend on, possessions carried for a decade, a number in your account you chase until it feels like safety. Underneath, perhaps, is a fear of depending on anyone again. Notice whether savings are becoming a fortress with no door.","scene":"Perhaps you check your savings for the third time today, not to spend them, just to feel the floor under your feet.","do":"Name the exact amount that would make you feel safe.","avoid":"Using money to control the people who depend on you.","ask":"What did you learn about money the day you felt powerless?"}},"3":{"en":{"theme":"The thing nobody says out loud","text":"For a good fifteen years Pluto works through your third house, and it tends to take apart the way you think and talk, piece by piece. You might research things obsessively, notice what people avoid saying, and find that small talk starts to feel like lying. A sibling rivalry, an old family story or a neighbour feud can return to mind for a closer look. It is worth noticing when sharper words start to work as weapons.","scene":"Picture your brother saying one sentence at dinner, and twenty years of family history rearranging itself in your head.","do":"Ask the question you’ve avoided asking your sibling.","avoid":"Winning an argument by saying the cruellest true thing.","ask":"Which family story have you never questioned out loud?"}},"4":{"en":{"theme":"What stops with you","text":"Pluto in your fourth house is a deep chapter that digs into the foundations of home and family. Perhaps a parent is ageing, a house is being sold, or an old secret is being spoken at the kitchen table. You carry family habits older than you, from silences to tempers, and this era invites you to choose which stop with you. The temptation is to fight for control of a home rather than build one.","scene":"Say you’re clearing out your parents’ attic and find yourself keeping a single cracked cup and nothing else.","do":"Name one family habit you refuse to pass on.","avoid":"Turning a house into a battlefield over who’s in charge.","ask":"Which family rule are you still obeying without meaning to?"}},"5":{"en":{"theme":"Desire with teeth","text":"Pluto in your fifth house is a long era in which love, pleasure and creative work tend to go all-or-nothing. Perhaps a romance takes over your life, a project eats your weekends for years, or a new baby or a child’s hard year reorders your priorities. You may want to be changed by what you love, so half-hearted fun can feel wasted. The shadow here is mistaking obsession and jealousy for proof of love.","scene":"Maybe you check whether they’ve seen your story, then check again, and hate how much the answer matters.","do":"Pour tonight’s intensity into something you make, not someone you watch.","avoid":"Testing a lover’s loyalty to feel in control.","ask":"What do you want so much that it frightens you?"}},"6":{"en":{"theme":"Rethinking the body and the workday","text":"For fifteen years or more Pluto works slowly through your sixth house, drawing attention to daily life down to the studs. Tiredness can prompt a rethink of how you eat and sleep; who holds power at work may be harder to ignore; a habit hidden for years may ask to be looked at. Perhaps you crave control of your routine because chaos once cost you. Notice if health is becoming a punishment.","scene":"It could be as small as throwing the cigarettes in the bin at the bus stop and meaning it this time.","do":"Change one daily habit and tell nobody until it sticks.","avoid":"Fighting a colleague for control of a project nobody owns.","ask":"Which habit runs you, rather than the other way round?"}},"7":{"en":{"theme":"Who holds the power between you","text":"Pluto in your seventh house is a long era when close relationships can become the place you’re remade. It brings into view what a marriage rests on, a business partner who feels like a rival, someone who gets under your skin. A bond can turn into a quiet tug-of-war over who needs whom more, perhaps because you know the cost of being the one who needs. Notice any urge to control a partner to avoid being left.","scene":"It might look like winning the argument about whose turn it is to compromise, and the flat feeling colder than before.","do":"Tell your partner one need without attaching a condition.","avoid":"Keeping score of who apologised first.","ask":"What frightens you about loosening your grip on the reins?"}},"8":{"en":{"theme":"What you owe and what you inherit","text":"Pluto in your eighth house is on home ground, a long era in which shared money, intimacy and loss tend to go all the way down. An inheritance, a divorce settlement or a debt can invite a total rethink, and grief can change who you trust. Sex and closeness may stop feeling casual, perhaps because you want someone to see the parts you hide. Notice whether secrets or money are becoming a hold over someone.","scene":"Suppose you’re sitting with a solicitor over a parent’s papers, learning more about them in an hour than in thirty years.","do":"Write down every debt and who it binds you to.","avoid":"Giving up what’s yours just to end an argument faster.","ask":"What would you let someone see if you trusted them fully?"}},"9":{"en":{"theme":"Beliefs you’ve earned, not borrowed","text":"Over fifteen or twenty years Pluto moves through your ninth house, and it tends to test the worldview you were handed. Perhaps a move abroad changes far more than your address, a degree or a long legal fight takes years, a faith you held cracks and something tougher grows in its place. You may need answers you’ve earned, not borrowed. It’s easy to grow as rigid about the new truth as about the old.","scene":"You might catch yourself defending a view you’d have mocked ten years ago, and noticing you’re not embarrassed, just sure.","do":"Read one serious argument against what you now believe.","avoid":"Converting friends to the truth that saved you.","ask":"Which belief would you still hold if it cost you something?"}},"10":{"en":{"theme":"Ambition that wants real power","text":"Pluto in your tenth house often spans the better part of two decades, and your career tends to become the arena where you’re tested. The questions are concrete: how fast to climb, how much of your identity rests on one role, what it means to lead people who once ran you. Ambition may sharpen, perhaps because powerlessness at work feels like powerlessness everywhere. Ask yourself whether you are becoming the boss you swore you’d never be.","scene":"Say your old boss emails asking for advice, and you take a long, slightly too satisfied moment before replying.","do":"Write down what you’d do with power you already have.","avoid":"Staying in a role because leaving feels like losing.","ask":"What would success look like if nobody had to lose?"}},"11":{"en":{"theme":"Friendships that go to the root","text":"Pluto spends two decades or so in your eleventh house, and it draws attention to your circle down to the roots. Friendships that run on habit may feel thinner, while a few may deepen into something close to family, and a movement or cause can become central to your life. Shallow belonging can start to feel lonelier than being alone. It’s worth asking whether a group decides who you’re allowed to be.","scene":"Perhaps you realise the friend you see every week hasn’t asked about your life in months, and you stop making excuses for it.","do":"Tell one friend what they’ve meant to you, specifically.","avoid":"Staying in a group out of fear of being talked about.","ask":"Which friendship would survive you telling the whole truth?"}},"12":{"en":{"theme":"What lives in the basement","text":"Pluto in your twelfth house is a long, underground era in which the real work tends to go on where nobody can see it. Old fears may surface in dreams, therapy can go deeper than you planned, and a compulsion kept private can come into sharper focus. Perhaps you’ve survived by keeping certain things locked away, and they now want air. The harder edge is guarding a secret so tightly it starts to run your days.","scene":"Imagine telling one person the thing you swore you’d take to the grave, and the ceiling staying where it is.","do":"Write the unsayable thing on paper, then decide who sees it.","avoid":"Feeding a private compulsion and calling it coping.","ask":"What are you still protecting that no longer protects you?"}}},"signs":{"aries":{"en":"Astrologers read Pluto in Aries as a generational era that tests courage and willpower: new leaders, new weapons, pioneers who refuse permission, and a hunger to dominate."},"taurus":{"en":"Pluto in Taurus, a placement a whole generation shares, draws attention to wealth and land: who owns the soil, money and food, which fortunes fade or take root."},"gemini":{"en":"Astrologers link Pluto in Gemini, a generation-wide theme, with information as power: printing, propaganda, fights over who controls the message, words as weapons, literacy as freedom."},"cancer":{"en":"Pluto in Cancer is traditionally read as a generational focus on home and homeland: displaced families, rebuilt nations, food and shelter as matters of survival, belonging as something fought for."},"leo":{"en":"Pluto in Leo, shared by a whole generation, is read as power gathered in personalities: stars, strongmen, youth cultures demanding to be seen, self-expression as pride and survival."},"virgo":{"en":"Pluto in Virgo, a generational signature, is linked with an overhaul of work and health: automation, new medicine, workplaces reorganised around efficiency, control reaching into daily details."},"libra":{"en":"Pluto in Libra draws a generation’s attention to power inside relationships: marriage rewritten, divorce and equality argued over, diplomacy as a battleground, who gives way to whom made political."},"scorpio":{"en":"Pluto in Scorpio, its own sign, is read as a generation’s era of bringing sex, death, debt and secrets into the light: intimacy questioned, hidden fortunes, broken taboos."},"sagittarius":{"en":"Astrologers read Pluto in Sagittarius as a generation’s remaking of belief and borders: globalisation, religious extremes, information without limits, truth as something fought over."},"capricorn":{"en":"Pluto in Capricorn, a generational marker, is read as an era that strips institutions bare: failing banks, exposed governments, giant corporations, power showing its machinery, trust in question."},"aquarius":{"en":"Pluto in Aquarius is a generational backdrop, read as power moving into networks: algorithms, platforms, online crowds that can topple or steer governments, and ownership of the code."},"pisces":{"en":"Pluto in Pisces is a generational placement read through faith and feeling: mass longing, new faiths, water and addiction, medicine for the mind, power hidden in what can’t be seen."}},"retroGeneral":{"en":"Pluto spends about five months of every year appearing to move backwards, and astrologers read this as its struggles turning inwards. Tension with a boss, a parent or a habit can become a private reckoning. It suits therapy, long walks with hard thoughts, and letting something that has run its course end properly."},"station":{"retrograde":{"en":"The weeks when Pluto seems to stand still before turning back are often read as a tightening. If an obsession, a rivalry or a fear about money grips harder, naming it plainly tends to loosen it."},"direct":{"en":"When Pluto turns forward after months of digging, what you’ve faced in private can start to show in your choices. It favours the move you’ve been circling: saying the hard thing, claiming what’s yours, ending what’s finished."}}}},"aspects":{"sun-moon":{"conj":{"en":"New moon: what you want and what you feel can line up for once, even with the tank reading low. Traditionally it is a moment to start one small thing — a savings pot, a running plan, a first page — and to go to bed earlier than pride suggests."},"soft":{"en":"Head and heart pull in the same direction more easily today. When plans feel doable and people feel easy, the day suits sorting the family pickup schedule, cooking something proper or finishing the task you’ve been postponing because of mood."},"hard":{"en":"What you need and what you’re pushing for can pull apart, which is perhaps why small things — a late reply, a sink full of dishes — feel like verdicts. Name the need before you argue the point, and finish one thing instead of starting three."}},"sun-mercury":{"conj":{"en":"Thought and intention fuse, so it can be easier to know what you mean and say it. These days favour pitches, applications and the message you’ve redrafted for a week. Worth noticing: being so sure of your point that you stop hearing anyone else’s."},"soft":{"en":"Words may land closer to the way you meant them, which suits the cover letter, the awkward email or one honest explanation you owe someone."},"hard":{"en":"Talk can outrun listening. Before sending anything heated, try reading it aloud once and deleting the last line."}},"sun-venus":{"conj":{"en":"Charm may come easily, and so can spending. You might notice people warming to you faster and compliments landing more readily, while a haircut or a new jacket feels like a fine idea. Spend the goodwill on one cooled friendship, and let any purchase bigger than a week of groceries wait a night."},"soft":{"en":"Pleasant company and easier apologies — an evening for inviting someone to dinner, or saying aloud the warm thing you usually only think."},"hard":{"en":"Wanting to be liked competes with wanting to be yourself. Notice where you’re agreeing just to keep the evening smooth."}},"sun-mars":{"conj":{"en":"Drive and identity fuse, and the wish to win can feel urgent. It favours a hard workout, a wardrobe purge or asking for the raise. If your fuse runs short in traffic or in the group chat, try reading a delay as a delay, not an insult."},"soft":{"en":"Effort can turn into results without drama: a good stretch to start the project you’ve been circling, carry the boxes, call the landlord. Courage may come cheaper these days, so the task you’ve avoided longest is a fair place for it."},"hard":{"en":"Irritation can rise fast and look for a target: a slow colleague, a partner’s tone, the printer. The heat is useful when it has somewhere to go — a sprint, a heavy bag, a scrubbed oven — before it lands on a person."}},"sun-jupiter":{"conj":{"en":"Confidence and generosity travel together. The contact invites you to aim a little higher than usual and to accept what is offered generously, while noticing the urge to promise more than one week can hold."},"soft":{"en":"Timing tends to feel kind, as if effort is met halfway. It is a good moment to ask for the favour, send the pitch, book the trip or introduce two people who should know each other. Generosity, given or received, can go further than usual, so say exactly what you want."},"hard":{"en":"Big appetite, thin margins. Optimism can outrun the facts, so it helps to keep the vision and check the numbers before committing time or money you don’t have. One fewer yes this week can be a gift to next month."}},"sun-saturn":{"conj":{"en":"Effort can feel heavier and praise thinner, as if someone in charge — a boss, a parent, your own inner accountant — wants proof. The weight suits solid tasks: the tax form, the budget, a deadline you can actually keep. Rest counts as discipline too."},"soft":{"en":"Steady work tends to be seen, and senior people may be more willing to listen. Slow tasks — the spreadsheet, the dentist booking, the lease renewal — can go more smoothly. Ask for the structure you need: a clear brief, a fixed date, a signature."},"hard":{"en":"If a wall appears where you hoped for a door — a rejection, a delay, a “not yet” from someone with authority — it may sting because you want to be taken seriously. Perhaps read it as a spec rather than a verdict, and ask what exactly would change the answer."}},"sun-uranus":{"conj":{"en":"Restless with your own routine, you might catch yourself wanting to quit, move, cut your hair and rewrite the plan by Friday. Some of it may be overdue. One bold change you can undo — a new route, a new class — is a gentler test than torching anything permanent."},"soft":{"en":"Good days for a smart experiment. An unexpected idea, contact or app can shed light on an old problem, and your less conventional side may be easier to show. Worth trying the shortcut, pitching the odd idea, saying yes to the last-minute invite."},"hard":{"en":"Plans can shift at short notice — a cancelled train, a changed brief, someone’s unexpected “I need space”. A jolt like that often shows where you’ve been holding on too tightly. A spare hour in the diary helps, and big decisions can wait until your pulse settles."}},"sun-neptune":{"conj":{"en":"Edges blur. You may feel kind, porous and slightly unfocused, and the to-do list often loses to daydreams. Music, painting, a long bath or quietly helping someone suit the mood. Contracts and first impressions are harder to read: check the facts, and notice whether a soft heart is doing the lending."},"soft":{"en":"Imagination and compassion run easily, which suits a first draft, the room makeover, a call to the friend who’s having a hard month. Your read on people tends to be quieter and truer; the sense of who needs a softer word is worth trusting."},"hard":{"en":"Fog and fatigue: deadlines can slip, messages get misread, and escaping into a series, a bottle or someone else’s crisis may look tempting. Writing things down and confirming times in writing helps, as does asking the plain question even if it feels rude."}},"sun-pluto":{"conj":{"en":"Intensity rises. The wish for control — of the project, the money, the story — can grow, and who holds power over you comes into clearer view. The force suits one deep clean: cancelling the subscription, having the hard talk, deleting the thread you reread at night."},"soft":{"en":"Focus goes deep. It becomes easier to get to the bottom of a budget, a medical question or a messy file, and people may trust you with the real story. Ask the question underneath the question, and renegotiate from steady ground."},"hard":{"en":"Power struggles come into view: a boss who micromanages, a partner who refuses to budge, your own need for the last word. Something may be asking to end. Before any fight, decide what you’re willing to lose, and leave secrets out of it."}},"moon-mercury":{"conj":{"en":"Thoughts come with feelings attached today, so you might find yourself talking about what’s bothering you before you’ve decided to. It suits a voice note to someone close or a page of journaling more than answering work email while annoyed."},"soft":{"en":"Conversations flow more easily today, and the right tone with a parent, a neighbour or a child’s teacher is simpler to find. A day for the calls you’ve been dodging, a shopping list that actually covers the week, or the small admin pile."},"hard":{"en":"Head and gut may disagree today, and it can show in your texts: too long, too sharp, sent too fast. One comment can loop in your mind for hours. A twenty-minute pause before replying helps, and so does eating before any serious conversation."}},"moon-venus":{"conj":{"en":"Soft mood, sweet tooth. Comfort calls — a good meal, clean sheets, someone’s hand — and kindness comes more easily than usual. Lovely for a date or making up after a cold week; just notice if shopping is standing in for a hug."},"soft":{"en":"People may feel easier to be around today, and forgiveness can flow more readily both ways. Host a small dinner, send the thank-you note, buy flowers for the kitchen table: small pleasures can mend more than big gestures."},"hard":{"en":"You might want affection and still feel slightly unappreciated, so a forgotten text or a tired partner can hit harder than it should. Comfort-spending and comfort-eating may tempt. Ask for the hug directly instead of testing whether anyone notices."}},"moon-mars":{"conj":{"en":"Quick temper, quick hands. Feelings tend to turn straight into action: perhaps you clean the flat in an hour, snap at the slow driver, text before thinking. It helps to burn it off in the body first — a run, a hard class, carrying something heavy."},"soft":{"en":"Feeling and drive agree today: there is less distance between wanting to do something and being able to. Tackle the chore with a deadline, stand up for a friend, or have the honest talk while your nerve is still warm."},"hard":{"en":"Irritability can run high today, with hunger, noise and other people’s pace feeling like provocations. Arguments at home may flare over nothing — the thermostat, the dishwasher. Eating on time, moving your body and lowering your voice one notch before answering all help."}},"moon-jupiter":{"conj":{"en":"Big heart, big portions. Optimism and generosity run high, and you might want to feed people, plan holidays and say yes to everything. Lovely for family time or a hopeful conversation; worth leaving some room in the appetite and the budget."},"soft":{"en":"An open-handed mood today. Kindness is easier to notice, small favours are easier to ask for, and good news is more readily shared. Ask a relative for help, invite someone new to lunch, or book the class you’ve been meaning to try."},"hard":{"en":"Too much of a good thing: another drink, another helping, one more promise to help. Feelings can inflate, so a minor slight feels like betrayal and a small win like proof of everything. Halve the portion, and let the big commitment sleep a night."}},"moon-saturn":{"conj":{"en":"A heavy, sober mood: you may feel older, lonelier or simply tired, and fun can look like work. Moon contacts are brief: weather, not climate. It suits dull, solid tasks — bills, a deep clean, a call to a parent — and an early night."},"soft":{"en":"Calm, practical feelings today. Promises are easier to keep without strain, and others may lean on you. Good for prepping the week’s meals, setting a budget with a partner, or an honest talk with an older relative about something real."},"hard":{"en":"It can feel as if you’re unsupported or judged, and a cool reply from a parent or boss may land like rejection. Old guilt tends to surface. Lonely decisions can wait today: do one responsible thing, then one kind thing for yourself — a warm meal, a bath."}},"moon-uranus":{"conj":{"en":"Restless and twitchy today: sitting still is hard, plans may change on a whim, and something different calls. Sleep can be patchy. A new route, rearranged furniture or a message to someone unexpected scratches the itch; quitting anything can wait a day."},"soft":{"en":"A light, curious mood today. Surprises can feel welcome and improvising comes easier: a last-minute plan, a fix nobody else saw, a funny reply that breaks the tension. The spontaneous invite is worth a yes."},"hard":{"en":"Nerves on edge: a change of plans, a cancelled meeting, a partner who wants space just when you want closeness can all jar more than usual. Freedom and comfort may both call at once. A buffer in the schedule helps, and so might skipping coffee after lunch."}},"moon-neptune":{"conj":{"en":"A dreamy, absorbent mood: you might pick up everyone’s feelings and lose track of your own. Music, swimming, a nap or a film can soothe today. Wine-fuelled confessions and lending money to a sad story are worth leaving for another day."},"soft":{"en":"A tender, intuitive day. It can be easier to sense what someone needs before they say it, and creative work flows. Sketch, cook without a recipe, call the friend who’s grieving, or sit through a child’s long story — patience comes more naturally today."},"hard":{"en":"Foggy and thin-skinned today: you might misplace keys, misread a tone, feel vaguely guilty about nothing specific. Drifting into scrolling or a second glass can look tempting. Drink water, set one alarm for the important thing, and check before assuming."}},"moon-pluto":{"conj":{"en":"Feelings run deep and private today. Jealousy, an old hurt or an urge to purge the wardrobe can surface from nowhere. The intensity can be put to use: clear one drawer, write the unsent letter, and keep the 3 a.m. thoughts out of the group chat."},"soft":{"en":"Emotional courage comes more readily today. A hard truth may be easier to hear without falling apart, and others might open up to you. Good for therapy, a frank talk about money with family, or clearing out what you’ve long outgrown."},"hard":{"en":"Intense and suspicious today: a delayed reply can read like a sign, and the wish to control what you can’t may grow. Old family patterns tend to flare. Notice the urge to check someone’s phone or win the fight; do something physical first, then talk."}},"mercury-venus":{"conj":{"en":"Words warm up. Compliments, flirting and diplomacy come more easily, which suits love letters, negotiations, design choices and calming a tense email thread. Say the appreciative thing out loud, and notice if charm starts dodging the actual question."},"soft":{"en":"Tact may come easily these days. It can help with asking for a discount, writing the wedding toast, clearing up a misunderstanding with a colleague, or saying out loud what you love about someone. Pleasant words can open doors that blunt ones would slam."},"hard":{"en":"Saying the nice thing and saying the true thing can feel like opposites. You might catch yourself softening feedback until it means nothing, or agreeing to a plan you dislike. The contact asks for kind and clear in the same sentence, and an honest price for your work."}},"mercury-mars":{"conj":{"en":"Sharp mind, sharp tongue. Thinking and typing speed up, and debates feel winnable — useful for deadlines, cold emails and fixing what broke yesterday. Tone is the price: reread before sending, and argue with the point, not the person."},"soft":{"en":"Decisive thinking. It becomes easier to cut through a messy meeting, make the call nobody wanted to make, or clear the paperwork quickly. A good few days to pitch, haggle or write the complaint letter, when firmness can sound less like hostility."},"hard":{"en":"Arguments can start in comment threads and end with slammed laptops. Everyone may feel sure while nobody seems to listen, and haste tends to show in small slips, like a typo to the boss. Sleep on the angry email, and give the day a few spare minutes."}},"mercury-jupiter":{"conj":{"en":"Ideas get big and talk gets generous. These days suit pitching, teaching, planning a trip or signing up for a course. Notice any overpromising — telling three people “easy, by Friday” — and perhaps write the plan down and cut it by a third."},"soft":{"en":"Open minds and good conversations. The contact favours the contract, the application or the hard question that deserves a fair hearing, and new material can stick more easily. Send the proposal, ask the expert, book the consultation, read the long article you saved."},"hard":{"en":"Too many words, too few details. It is easy to skim the contract, exaggerate in the meeting or argue about principles instead of the plan. Read the small print, double-check the flight date, and let someone else talk for a while."}},"mercury-saturn":{"conj":{"en":"Serious, deliberate thinking. Words may come slowly but carry weight, which favours contracts, exams, budgets and the email that has to be exactly right. Worry can get louder too; a written list is kinder than rehearsing it at night."},"soft":{"en":"Clear, structured thinking. Paperwork that scared you can look more manageable, and precision tends to be noticed by senior people. File the forms, finish the report, put agreements in writing. A short, plain message often does more than a long clever one."},"hard":{"en":"Communication can feel stuck: delayed replies, a “no” to your proposal, criticism that feels personal. Notice if you start doubting your own competence. Ask for specific feedback, fix one concrete thing, and try not to read silence as a final answer."}},"mercury-uranus":{"conj":{"en":"Lightning-fast ideas and abrupt turns of thought. You might see a solution sideways, say something surprisingly blunt, or change your mind three times by lunch. Write every idea down — a couple may be good — and back up your files while you’re at it."},"soft":{"en":"Inventive thinking. A new tool, a fresh angle or a stranger’s comment can shift something you’ve been stuck on for weeks. Brainstorm, rewrite your CV, try the app, message the person you met once at a conference."},"hard":{"en":"Nerves and glitches are the classic picture: plans changed by text, Wi-Fi dropping mid-call, a remark so blunt the meeting freezes — possibly yours. Pause before reacting, keep a backup copy, and leave resignations out of reply-all."}},"mercury-neptune":{"conj":{"en":"Imagination floods language. Poems, lyrics, stories and gentle conversations flow more easily than spreadsheets and directions. Give these days to creative drafts and patient listening, and check every time, address and number twice."},"soft":{"en":"Words carry feeling. The right way to comfort, persuade or describe something hard to name may be easier to find. Write the eulogy, the song, the fundraising post, or the message that might help a friend feel less alone."},"hard":{"en":"Mixed signals and half-truths. A promise can be vaguer than it sounded, a detail can go missing, and it is easy to hear what you hoped to hear. Get it in writing, let a feeling settle before you sign or send money, and say plainly what you mean."}},"mercury-pluto":{"conj":{"en":"Thinking turns investigative. The real reason, the hidden clause, the whole story start to matter, and persuasion can tip into pressure. Research, audit, interview — and notice if you’re interrogating a partner instead of asking."},"soft":{"en":"Penetrating focus. Reading between the lines of a contract, a medical report or a hesitant friend’s message comes more easily. It favours research, negotiation, therapy, or the honest conversation that can actually change something."},"hard":{"en":"Words can turn into weapons: someone pushes, someone digs, a secret slips, an argument goes straight for the sore spot. Before saying the thing that can’t be unsaid, ask what you actually want to change — then say only that."}},"venus-mars":{"conj":{"en":"Desire wakes up. Attraction, flirting and creative drive run together, and it is easier to notice who you actually want, not who’s convenient. Make the move, plan the date, start the art project — and leave jealousy out of the talking."},"soft":{"en":"Chemistry may come easily. Romance, intimacy and teamwork tend to flow, and making up after a fight may take just one honest sentence. Ask someone out, plan a weekend for two, or pair up on a project with someone whose rhythm matches yours."},"hard":{"en":"Wanting and pleasing collide. Sexual tension, irritation with a partner, or a row over who does more around the house can flare. Closeness and independence may both pull at once. Ask for what you want without turning it into a complaint."}},"venus-jupiter":{"conj":{"en":"An abundant mood: generosity, good food, gifts and easy affection. Social plans tend to multiply and people may be readier to say yes. Throw the dinner, pitch the creative idea, buy something beautiful — once. Notice any urge to overspend just to keep a pleasant feeling going."},"soft":{"en":"Warmth that tends to come back to you. Relationships, sales and creative work can feel lifted, and a kind word may travel further than usual. Ask for the rate you deserve, reconnect with an old friend, say yes to the invitation that feels like a treat."},"hard":{"en":"Too much sweetness: overdoing food, shopping or flattery, and saying yes to everyone so nobody is disappointed. Pick one party, set a spending cap before you open the app, and notice when flattery seems to come with a request attached."}},"venus-saturn":{"conj":{"en":"Love gets serious. Commitment, loyalty and boundaries can matter more than romance, and feeling lonely or tested is part of the picture. A fitting time to define a relationship, set a budget, or let go of something that only looked good. Quality over quantity, in people and in purchases."},"soft":{"en":"Steady affection. Long relationships can deepen, older people’s advice is worth hearing, and money decisions tend towards the sensible. Plan the shared savings, renew the lease, have the talk about next year, or choose the coat made for ten winters."},"hard":{"en":"Love can feel rationed: a partner who seems cold, a cancelled date, tight money, and the question of whether you’re enough. Buying affection or begging for reassurance rarely gives what’s missing. Name one specific need; settling one small debt may soothe more than shopping."}},"venus-uranus":{"conj":{"en":"Unexpected attraction and restless taste. You might fall for someone surprising, crave a new style, or want more freedom inside a relationship. Something different — a new haircut, a different kind of date — can satisfy the craving before any permanent change to a person or a bank balance."},"soft":{"en":"The contact makes room for pleasant surprises in love and money, and for noticing them: a spontaneous date, an unusual gift, an idea for a side income. Say yes to the last-minute plan, try the gallery or class you’ve never been to, and flirt a little."},"hard":{"en":"Love meets freedom, and the pull between them can jolt. It might show as needing space from a partner, a crush out of nowhere or a purchase made on pure impulse. Ask for space without punishing, return what you bought on a whim, and give a new feeling a week before acting on it."}},"venus-neptune":{"conj":{"en":"Romance in soft focus. Music, art, longing and tenderness are heightened, and the best in people is easy to see — sometimes more than is there. Make something beautiful, plan a dreamy date, and keep your bank card and your judgement in your own hands."},"soft":{"en":"Compassion and imagination run generous. Love can feel kind rather than dramatic, and creative work takes on a quiet beauty. Donate, volunteer, write the love letter, repaint a room, or forgive someone who has genuinely been trying."},"hard":{"en":"Rose-tinted glasses. It is tempting to idealise someone, overlook a red flag or spend on a fantasy, and disappointment tends to live in the gap between the dream and the person. Ask the boring question, check the price twice, and watch who shows up reliably, not beautifully."}},"venus-pluto":{"conj":{"en":"Attraction can turn magnetic, even obsessive. Desire, jealousy and the wish to merge completely run high, and money questions inside love come into view. Feel all of it, and leave their phone alone. Good for intimacy, deep honesty and a creative project you give everything to."},"soft":{"en":"Love can deepen through honesty. Trust may grow more easily and closeness mend, and money, sex or the past can become things you talk about without blowing up. Have the real conversation, rework a shared budget, or commit fully to the person or project you chose."},"hard":{"en":"Love can turn into a power struggle: jealousy, control over money, emotional blackmail, an old flame. All or nothing may feel like the only options. Notice where you’re testing someone instead of trusting them, and give yourself room from anyone who seems to need you small."}},"mars-jupiter":{"conj":{"en":"Big push, big confidence. Further and faster can feel irresistible — a longer run, a bolder pitch, a bigger project. Launches, sport and the thing you’ve delayed suit this mood. Worth pacing yourself: overreaching often shows as an overbooked calendar and a body asking for rest."},"soft":{"en":"Effort and reward can feel closer together. Courage may find its opening more readily, which suits the sports goal, the business move or the hard conversation. Apply for the bigger role, sign up for the race, propose the plan — momentum is easier to find these days."},"hard":{"en":"Overconfidence and impatience. You might take on too much, argue on principle, or spend to feel bigger, and bold gambles can look braver than they are. Finish what you started before adding more, and read the fine print on anything “once in a lifetime”."}},"mars-saturn":{"conj":{"en":"Effort meets resistance. If you push and the door pushes back — paperwork, a slow boss, a body that wants rest — frustration can build. Strength training is the useful image: steady reps, not a sprint. One well-built task is worth ten half-started ones."},"soft":{"en":"Stamina with a plan. Ambition and patience can stop fighting, which makes long, unglamorous work easier to move: the renovation, the thesis chapter, the debt payoff, the training block. Pick the hardest task, break it into steps, and do the first two before lunch."},"hard":{"en":"One foot on the gas, one on the brake. Delays, rules and other people’s caution can feel infuriating; notice whether pushing harder is only straining your back, your budget or the relationship. Rather than forcing the locked door, look for the person who has the key."}},"mars-uranus":{"conj":{"en":"Bursts of action and impatience: the urge to quit the class, book the flight, take the reckless shortcut, say exactly what you think. It favours breaking a stuck pattern, with a slower hand for anything that can’t be undone."},"soft":{"en":"Bold, inventive action. The unconventional approach deserves a trial: a new workout, a fast pivot at work, a clever fix for a broken thing. Run the experiment, change the routine, say yes to the adventurous plan while reflexes feel quick."},"hard":{"en":"Short fuses and abrupt blow-ups. A minor annoyance can turn into a slammed door or a resignation letter, and a broken machine or plan may feel like the last straw. Work your body hard, add a buffer to travel, and let anger cool before any irreversible move."}},"mars-neptune":{"conj":{"en":"Drive goes soft and foggy. The wish to act may not find its target, and fatigue can come early. Dance, swimming, yoga, art or volunteering suit it well. Skip the passive-aggressive standoff and say plainly what you want instead of sighing."},"soft":{"en":"Action guided by intuition and compassion. Effort tends to feel lighter when it serves something beyond you. Join the park clean-up, help a neighbour move, practise an art, take a long swim. Quiet persistence can do more than force these days."},"hard":{"en":"Motivation can leak away. Confusion, low stamina or an unspoken conflict may make it hard to fight for anything. It might feel as if someone is quietly working against you — or perhaps you’re the one avoiding a fight. Rest without guilt, get the facts first, and choose one clear goal."}},"mars-pluto":{"conj":{"en":"Raw force. Ambition, anger and desire can run at full volume, and a week may hold a month’s work. It suits renovating, clearing out, training hard or rebuilding a plan from scratch. Aimed at a person, force usually meets force, so the work is the better target."},"soft":{"en":"Concentrated, determined effort. What others gave up on can feel within reach: a stubborn repair, a long negotiation, a fitness goal, a rescue job at work. Choose the one thing you want most and give it everything — effort like this tends to compound."},"hard":{"en":"Power struggles and compulsion. If someone pushes and you feel the urge to push back harder — at work, at home, in traffic — rage can feel righteous. Stepping out of the room, burning the anger off at the gym and keeping threats off the table all suit this contact."}},"jupiter-saturn":{"conj":{"en":"A twenty-year reset, as astrologers read it, of how societies grow and govern: institutions and careers reorganise around new rules, and the late-2020 conjunction is often linked with the move of work onto screens. Personally, it asks which long project deserves your next two decades, and invites starting it modestly."},"soft":{"en":"Usually read as a sensible season for growth: expansion and caution cooperate, and markets, institutions and long plans can rise without overheating. For you, it favours one ambitious step with a realistic budget — a degree, a home, a business you can sustain."},"hard":{"en":"This contact pictures a collective tug-of-war between growth and limits: stimulus against austerity, hope against rules, boom against correction. In one life it may feel like a clash between ambitions and obligations. It invites growth where the foundation already holds, and trimming where it doesn’t."}},"jupiter-uranus":{"conj":{"en":"Astrologers link this contact with a collective appetite for breakthrough: tech booms, abrupt market leaps, mass enthusiasm for the new, openings that seem to appear and vanish fast. In your own life, notice which idea excites you, and how much of the thrill is about money."},"soft":{"en":"Seen as a wide opening for innovation: new tools spreading quickly, unusual careers becoming viable, the old way no longer the only way. It favours learning the new skill, launching the side project, applying abroad — an invitation to anyone willing to experiment."},"hard":{"en":"Restless times are the theme here: bubbles, abrupt reversals, revolts against the way things are run, a hunger for freedom faster than systems can adjust. On a personal scale, if one good week makes a stable job look like a cage, a side step can test the leap first."}},"jupiter-neptune":{"conj":{"en":"Collective idealism and collective fog, in the traditional reading: faith, charity, art and spiritual seeking surge, and so do hype, scams and bubbles built on a good story. Give generously, make something beautiful, and ask what any miracle-sounding promise actually rests on."},"soft":{"en":"A gentle collective tide towards compassion and imagination is how the contact is often pictured: humanitarian causes gaining support, art and film finding wide audiences, faith turning less dogmatic. Volunteer, give regularly, take the creative course — goodwill tends to grow when it’s practical."},"hard":{"en":"Often read as a period of inflated promises: miracle cures, get-rich schemes, leaders selling a dream, hope outrunning evidence. Closer to home, it invites keeping the faith while checking the facts, and giving to causes whose results you can actually see."}},"jupiter-pluto":{"conj":{"en":"Concentrated collective power is what this contact symbolises: vast fortunes, institutions growing bigger and more controlling, ambition on a grand scale, wealth and influence changing hands. Personally, it draws attention to long-term leverage — skills, ownership, savings — rather than a quick win."},"soft":{"en":"Traditionally favourable years for deep regeneration, read through money flowing into rebuilding, research breakthroughs scaling up and people finding leverage to shift entrenched situations. Privately, it suits steady repair: paying down a debt, building something long-term, rebuilding a career on firmer ground."},"hard":{"en":"Astrologically this contact stands for collective struggles over wealth and control: monopolies challenged, scandals exposed, ambition that overreaches. In everyday terms, it brings into view any deal that asks you to hand over too much control, and the pull to stake security on a shot at more."}},"saturn-uranus":{"conj":{"en":"Old order and new invention collide and fuse, and astrologers often read the late-1980s conjunction alongside the fall of the Berlin Wall and the birth of the web. Structures crack and rebuild in this symbolism. The personal question is which rules still protect you and which you’ve outgrown."},"soft":{"en":"Practical innovation is the keynote here: reform without revolution, new technology meeting sensible rules, old institutions modernising, stable professions absorbing new tools. A fitting backdrop for retraining, updating a business model, or building structure around a freer way of working."},"hard":{"en":"Symbolically, this is collective tension between control and freedom: restrictions against liberties, old industries against disruption, rules that feel broken yet refuse to budge. Individually it can feel like being caught between security and change; small, structured steps often serve better than one dramatic exit."}},"saturn-neptune":{"conj":{"en":"Dreams meet the reality check. The 1989 conjunction is often linked with collapsing ideologies, and the 2026 one is read as a question of what our ideals actually cost to build — faith, collectively, under audit. Personally, it invites giving your vaguest dream a budget, a date and a first boring step."},"soft":{"en":"Ideals take practical form, as this contact is read: charities becoming institutions, art finding funding, compassion turning into policy. In a working life, the years it spans can favour turning a calling into a job — the studio, the clinic, the course you’ve dreamed of teaching."},"hard":{"en":"Read as years of disillusionment: institutions losing credibility, propaganda and fear blurring the facts, systems quietly eroding. It can feel as if hopes are dissolving under pressure. The contact invites keeping one dream, giving it a structure, and letting the rest go without bitterness."}},"saturn-pluto":{"conj":{"en":"A heavy collective reckoning that astrologers place roughly every 35 years, when systems that stopped working come under scrutiny and power structures harden or crumble. In your own life, it suits rebuilding one area from the foundation up, patiently and with no shortcuts."},"soft":{"en":"Slow, serious rebuilding is the classic image: governments and companies reforming what’s rotten, long-term infrastructure taking shape, discipline bearing deep fruit. On a personal level, it favours the change that takes years: clearing a long debt, mastering the craft, rebuilding your health."},"hard":{"en":"In astrological terms, this is collective pressure between authority and upheaval: rules tightening, budgets shrinking, people arguing about who holds power, fear making systems rigid. Notice where fear makes you rigid too, and which hard change you would rather choose than wait for."}},"uranus-neptune":{"conj":{"en":"A rare fusion of invention and imagination: astrologers read the early-1990s conjunction through the web, raves and a new language for dreams. Generations born under it are said to think in networks. If you were born near it, it may be part of why you want technology to mean something."},"soft":{"en":"A long, quiet current in which technology and imagination cooperate, as astrologers picture it: digital art, online communities, tools that make inspiration easier to share. Those tools can serve something beautiful or useful — the gap between dreaming and building may feel narrower than it was."},"hard":{"en":"The contact is linked with collective confusion between invention and illusion: tech utopias that turn into nightmares, disinformation at the speed of light, revolutions that dissolve into mist. It favours healthy scepticism towards the shiny promise, and one offline habit that brings you back to earth."}},"uranus-pluto":{"conj":{"en":"Astrologers read the 1960s conjunction as a generational detonation: civil rights, the sexual revolution, youth in revolt against the old order. Those born under it are often said to carry a radical streak; in you, it may be the stubborn part that refuses rules that crush people."},"soft":{"en":"A long window, in the astrological reading, for radical change without wreckage: reforms taking root, technology redistributing power, old taboos fading. It favours making one deep change stick — a new city, a new profession, a new relationship with your body."},"hard":{"en":"Associated with years of upheaval: protest movements, financial shocks, institutions shaken by what they hid, change moving whether or not anyone plans for it. For you, it draws attention to the change you can steer — a job, a city, a habit — rather than waiting for a bigger one."}},"neptune-pluto":{"conj":{"en":"Astrologers call it the seed of a 500-year cycle, last planted around 1892 and read alongside the birth of electricity, cinema, psychoanalysis and mass ideology — a collective dream remaking the world. In a family, it is ancestral weather: the beliefs your great-grandparents built their lives on."},"soft":{"en":"A slow undercurrent running since the 1940s, in which beliefs are read as changing the way coastlines do, too slowly to see in a year. Your grandparents’ rules about work, faith and family can soften without anyone voting on it. Notice one inherited fear and ask whether it’s still yours."},"hard":{"en":"A rare collective strain between dreams and power, which astrologers have linked with times when empires and faiths cracked together: ideals turned into weapons, grief gone underground. Inwardly, it invites separating what you truly believe from what you were simply taught to fear."}}},"transits":{"sun>sun":{"conj":{"en":"The Sun is back on your natal Sun: your solar return, the birthday reset. Birthdays can sting, often because you quietly compare yourself with the person you planned to be by now. If an inner audit starts, it can wait. Write one sentence about what this next year is for, and let someone buy you cake."},"soft":{"en":"The Sun is in easy step with your natal Sun: for a day or two, feeling like yourself can take less effort, with more stamina and less second-guessing, perhaps because nothing is asking you to be someone else. A good moment for something with your name on it: the pitch, the application, the haircut."},"hard":{"en":"The Sun is squaring off with your natal Sun: for a day or two, this contact shows where the plan you made around your birthday meets real life. If you feel tired or oddly unseen, it is often because you’re carrying tasks that aren’t yours. Hand one back, politely, while it is still a task, not a grudge."}},"sun>moon":{"conj":{"en":"The Sun is crossing your natal Moon: feelings you usually manage alone tend to show on your face, and your needs can be harder to tuck away. For a day or two, try naming one out loud — an early night, a hand with dinner — while it is still a need rather than a mood."},"soft":{"en":"The Sun is in easy contact with your natal Moon: what you want and what you need can agree for once, and you might notice your shoulders drop and home feel good to return to. The next day or two favour settling the family plan or home decision you’ve been circling."},"hard":{"en":"The Sun is pressing on your natal Moon: the goal and the need can pull apart, and the body is often where it shows — a tight jaw, a bad night, sugar at four. Notice whether you keep going as if rest were optional. For a day or two, choose the need once, on purpose."}},"sun>mercury":{"conj":{"en":"The Sun is crossing your natal Mercury: your head may feel clearer and your sentences more finished than usual. For a day or two, it’s a fitting moment to send the pitch or write the difficult email. See whether hearing yourself so well leaves less room to hear others, and ask one real question back."},"soft":{"en":"The Sun is in friendly contact with your natal Mercury: explaining what you want without rehearsing it twelve times can come more naturally, perhaps because you’re not fighting your own doubts as hard. For a day or two, try saying out loud the thing you’ve been drafting in your head in the shower."},"hard":{"en":"The Sun is at odds with your natal Mercury: pride can slip into your sentences. A neutral comment may read as criticism, and the urge to win the thread rather than end it can be strong, as if being right were the same as being seen. For a day or two, reread before you send."}},"sun>venus":{"conj":{"en":"The Sun is crossing your natal Venus: it may be easier to like what you see in the mirror, and to let others see it too. For a day or two, wanting nice things need not feel like a flaw. Wear the good shirt, book the table, and quote your real rate instead of the apologetic one."},"soft":{"en":"The Sun is flattering your natal Venus: being relaxed rather than trying tends to draw people closer, and money talk may feel less awkward than usual. For a day or two, it’s a nice moment to plan the date, buy the small good thing, or ask for the better price."},"hard":{"en":"The Sun is chafing against your natal Venus: the wish for proof that you’re worth something can grow louder, and it tends to leak out — a basket of things you don’t need, a sulk when nobody mentions the haircut. For a day or two, try saying what you’d like to hear instead of testing people."}},"sun>mars":{"conj":{"en":"The Sun is crossing your natal Mars: you might feel your engine turn over, wanting to start, compete, finish. Slow people and slow wifi can feel like personal insults, often because ambition and temper share a fuse. For a day or two, aim it at one hard task, then at the gym."},"soft":{"en":"The Sun is giving your natal Mars a tailwind: effort can seem to pay back quickly, and your body might have more in it than usual. Confidence here tends to grow from moving, not from thinking about moving. For a day or two, start the thing you’ve been postponing — the run, the course, the wardrobe clear-out."},"hard":{"en":"The Sun is clashing with your natal Mars: when your drive meets resistance, it can feel personal. Notice what sets you off — a colleague’s tone, a long queue, a partner’s one-word text. For a day or two, burn it off physically — stairs, a run, a heavy bag — before you reply to anyone."}},"moon>sun":{"conj":{"en":"The Moon is crossing your natal Sun: for a few hours today, what you feel and who you are can point the same way, which often makes you easier to read. A good window for the visible thing — the call, the post, the ask — while your face and your words agree."},"soft":{"en":"The Moon is lending your natal Sun a few supportive hours: when your mood backs your plans, the body tends to find fuel and the to-do list can look doable. It’s worth noticing how that feels, with nothing in you arguing. Use the window for one task that needs heart and nerve: a first draft, a tricky call."},"hard":{"en":"The Moon is pulling against your natal Sun: for a few hours, mood and plans may want different things, and you might feel off without quite knowing why — hungry, touchy, slightly exposed. Eat something real, and let one bad mood stay a mood rather than a verdict on your whole life."}},"moon>moon":{"conj":{"en":"The Moon is back on your natal Moon: your lunar return, the monthly reset of your emotional clock. For a few hours you may feel thin-skinned, as your oldest needs rise to the surface — your food, your bed, your people. Meet them plainly, then notice which one you’ve been skipping all month."},"soft":{"en":"The Moon is in easy step with your natal Moon: for a few hours body and mood tend to cooperate, and what you need may be clear without any argument with yourself. Cook something familiar, tidy one corner, call someone who knew you at fifteen."},"hard":{"en":"The Moon is squaring off with your natal Moon: for a few hours your needs and your day may not match — perhaps you crave quiet in a loud office, or company when everyone’s busy. Often the stomach notices first. Eat, drink water, and let any text you’re tempted to send wait until the mood has passed."}},"moon>mercury":{"conj":{"en":"The Moon is crossing your natal Mercury: for a few hours, feelings tend to find words fast. You might talk more, replay old conversations, start the long voice note. The hours suit a heart-to-heart better than a work email, since your mood may be doing some of the typing. Draft now, send after dinner."},"soft":{"en":"The Moon is in friendly contact with your natal Mercury: for a few hours, saying how you feel may work without the usual tangle, as if head and gut were using the same language. Write it down, or tell someone what you need without blaming them."},"hard":{"en":"The Moon is needling your natal Mercury: for a few hours your mood can edit what you hear. A short reply may read as cold, a question as an accusation, often because the feeling comes first and the reasons are invented after. Ask what they meant before you answer what you heard."}},"moon>venus":{"conj":{"en":"The Moon is crossing your natal Venus: for a few hours softness may be what you’re after — good bread, clean sheets, a hand on your back. Pleasure tends to calm you quickly when mood and taste agree. Say yes to the small nice thing, and tell someone you’d like company tonight."},"soft":{"en":"The Moon is warming your natal Venus: for a few hours liking yourself may take less work, and that ease tends to show. It could be as small as a laugh over small talk with the barista. Use the mood to make up with someone after a cold few days."},"hard":{"en":"The Moon is pressing on your natal Venus: for a few hours, wanting comfort can send your hand to the nearest version — a full basket, a second dessert, an ex’s profile. The need is real, even if the target is off. Name the feeling first, then see if you still want the thing."}},"moon>mars":{"conj":{"en":"The Moon is crossing your natal Mars: for a few hours feelings tend to go straight to your hands. Irritation can flare hot, and so can desire, as if there were no gap between feeling and doing. Spend it on a hard workout or the jammed drawer rather than the group chat."},"soft":{"en":"The Moon is backing your natal Mars: for a few hours the wish to act and the body may agree, and courage tends to cost less. Use the window for the chore you’ve been dodging, a hard set at the gym, or a firm, friendly no."},"hard":{"en":"The Moon is provoking your natal Mars: for a few hours small things — a slow till, a sigh from your partner — can land as attacks. Often that is tiredness or hurt wearing armour. Get it out of your body before you answer: a brisk walk, cold water, ten push-ups."}},"mercury>sun":{"conj":{"en":"Mercury is crossing your natal Sun: for a day or two, thoughts often circle back to you — your plans, your reputation, what you should have said. Calls and forms with your name on them may need more attention than usual. Update the CV or bio, and talk to yourself like a decent colleague would."},"soft":{"en":"Mercury is in friendly contact with your natal Sun: for a day or two, explaining what you want in one go is more within reach when words and aims agree. A good moment to pitch yourself, sign up for the course, answer the recruiter, and hear how clear a point sounds without hedging."},"hard":{"en":"Mercury is at odds with your natal Sun: for a day or two, feedback can sound personal and over-explaining becomes tempting, perhaps because pride is listening for criticism. Crossed wires about who said what are easy to fall into. Check the thread before reacting, and ask whether you’re defending what nobody attacked."}},"mercury>moon":{"conj":{"en":"Mercury is crossing your natal Moon: for a day or two feelings tend to look for words. Perhaps you go over what your mother said, or text home more than usual. If the talking turns into looping at night, say it once to one person who listens, then put the phone down."},"soft":{"en":"Mercury is in friendly step with your natal Moon: for a day or two, talking things through can be genuinely calming, since a feeling often shrinks once it’s named. Make the family call, have the sensible chat about chores, write down what you need."},"hard":{"en":"Mercury is snagging on your natal Moon: for a day or two, an offhand comment can land in a soft spot, and you may answer sharper than you feel. Arguing facts rarely mends a mood when the hurt isn’t about the facts. Say “I need a minute” and take it."}},"mercury>mercury":{"conj":{"en":"Mercury is back on your natal Mercury, where it stood when you were born: for a day or two, thinking in your own voice, not the one you borrow for meetings, can feel natural again. Shelved ideas are worth a second look: open the old notes file and see whether one feels ready."},"soft":{"en":"Mercury is in friendly contact with your natal Mercury: for a day or two your mind may work the way it likes to, and fiddly things — the tax form, the new app, the long article — can feel like less of a slog. Learn one thing properly, then explain it to someone."},"hard":{"en":"Mercury is squaring off with your natal Mercury: for a day or two facts can take a shape your mind doesn’t like, which makes skimming, assuming and misreading easier. It could be as small as the wrong time, the wrong attachment, the wrong person in cc. Read every message twice, and check dates against the calendar."}},"mercury>venus":{"conj":{"en":"Mercury is crossing your natal Venus: for a day or two your words may sound warmer and a little flirty, perhaps because your thoughts keep drifting to what you like. Send the compliment, write the note, negotiate the price — charm has its place in money talk, too."},"soft":{"en":"Mercury is in a sweet angle to your natal Venus: for a day or two, kind words tend to come more easily, which makes it a good moment to repair things. Apologise for the sharp text, plan a date, or talk through the shared budget without a fight."},"hard":{"en":"Mercury is tangling with your natal Venus: for a day or two there may be a pull to analyse affection instead of feeling it — rereading their text, counting the kisses, wondering what “ok” meant. Money talk can knot up the same way. Call instead of typing; tone carries what text drops."}},"mercury>mars":{"conj":{"en":"Mercury is crossing your natal Mars: for a day or two words can take on an edge while patience runs short, and you might think fast and say it faster. Use it to write the complaint, chase the late invoice, argue the case — and give anything personal ten minutes before you send it."},"soft":{"en":"Mercury is backing your natal Mars: for a day or two deciding quickly and acting on it the same afternoon tends to feel simple, when thinking and doing aren’t arguing. Clear the admin backlog, give one straight instruction, book the thing you keep researching."},"hard":{"en":"Mercury is clashing with your natal Mars: for a day or two, words can turn into fights fast — a comment thread, a sibling, a driver who cuts in. It can feel as if your mind is looking for a target for the heat. Write the furious reply, delete it, and go for a run."}},"venus>sun":{"conj":{"en":"Venus is crossing your natal Sun: for a day or two, warmth aimed your way may be easier to notice — a softer face in the mirror, a stranger holding the door, a friend picking up the bill. None of it has to be earned. Accept the invitation and the compliment without arguing."},"soft":{"en":"Venus is in sweet contact with your natal Sun: for a day or two, goodwill tends to be within easy reach. Warmth often gets you further than pushing, so it suits the photos, the haircut, the meeting where you need someone on your side. Wear the colour you usually save."},"hard":{"en":"Venus is tugging at your natal Sun: for a day or two the wish to be liked can grow strong enough to bend you — agreeing to plans you don’t want, paying for the round, laughing at unfunny jokes. Do one thing today purely because you enjoy it, audience or not."}},"venus>moon":{"conj":{"en":"Venus is touching your natal Moon: for a day or two, comfort may be easier to let in. Notice the small kindness that lands where you needed it, and how home, food or a familiar person can soothe more than usual. Receive it without rushing to pay it back."},"soft":{"en":"Venus is at a gentle angle to your natal Moon: for a day or two the people at home may feel easier to love, perhaps because pleasure and safety are asking for the same thing. Cook for someone, put flowers on the kitchen table, mend a small rift with family."},"hard":{"en":"Venus is pressing on your natal Moon: for a day or two, what you want and what makes you feel safe can pull in different directions. Notice whether a purchase, a date or a sweet thing is standing in for reassurance you haven’t asked for directly. Ask for the reassurance first, out loud."}},"venus>mercury":{"conj":{"en":"Venus is crossing your natal Mercury: for a day or two you may find yourself choosing words for how they feel, not just for what they mean. It favours the birthday card, the toast, the message that mends a quarrel. Write the thing you’d usually say only after two glasses of wine."},"soft":{"en":"Venus is smoothing the way for your natal Mercury: for a day or two, difficult things may be easier to say kindly, leading with the kindness rather than the complaint. Use it for the awkward email, the favour you need to ask, or the price you want to negotiate down."},"hard":{"en":"Venus is at odds with your natal Mercury: for a day or two it’s easy to say what pleases instead of what’s true — yes to the plan, praise for the bad idea, a purchase because the salesperson was lovely. Before agreeing, ask yourself what you actually think."}},"venus>venus":{"conj":{"en":"Venus is back on your natal Venus: your Venus return, traditionally read as the roughly yearly reset of what you love and what you think you’re worth. For a day or two your taste may be unusually clear. Notice what bores you now, and set this year’s price — in love and at work."},"soft":{"en":"Venus is in easy contact with your natal Venus: for a day or two, liking what you already have can come naturally — the flat, the friend, the coat you nearly returned. Contentment tends to show, and to suit you, once the comparing stops. Spend a little on pleasure, not on proving anything."},"hard":{"en":"Venus is squaring off with your natal Venus: for a day or two this contact brings into view where your appetite and your values disagree — the jacket you can’t afford, the ex who only texts at midnight. Ask whether you want the thing itself, or the feeling of being worth it."}},"venus>mars":{"conj":{"en":"Venus is crossing your natal Mars: for a day or two desire can feel warm and direct, and charm may suit you better than force in going after what you want. Notice who you find yourself drawn to. Make the first move, suggest the date, or pitch the deal with a smile."},"soft":{"en":"Venus is in easy step with your natal Mars: for a day or two drive can soften without losing force, so effort may feel more like play. Think dance class, a match with friends, sex without overthinking, a negotiation handled nicely. Go after the fun thing first."},"hard":{"en":"Venus is pulling against your natal Mars: for a day or two desire and irritation can get tangled — you want them and they’re annoying you, or you spend fast to scratch an itch. Underneath, there is often a wish for more than you’re getting. Say that, instead of picking a fight about the dishes."}},"mars>sun":{"conj":{"en":"Mars is crossing your natal Sun: for several days there may be more fuel, more nerve and much less patience. Being blocked can feel like being erased, which is often why the pushing starts. Give it a target: a hard training week, a project with a deadline, the conversation where you stand your ground."},"soft":{"en":"Mars is fuelling your natal Sun: for several days stamina and the nerve to use it may both be at hand, without the usual fight with yourself. Ask for the raise, start the training plan, take the lead in the meeting, and notice what helps momentum stick."},"hard":{"en":"Mars is squaring off with your natal Sun: for several days walls may seem to be everywhere — a boss, a bank, a partner with a different plan — and each can feel like a challenge to who you are. Choose one fight worth having, and sleep more than you want to."}},"mars>moon":{"conj":{"en":"Mars is crossing your natal Moon: for several days feelings tend to run hot and close to the skin — quick tears, quick temper, a fierce urge to protect your people. Tiredness can turn into anger fast, so move your body daily, eat on time, and keep arguments out of the kitchen."},"soft":{"en":"Mars is in easy step with your natal Moon: for several days standing up for what you need may not have to become a scene, since feeling and action are pulling the same way. Fix the broken shelf, set the house rule, say no to the extra shift."},"hard":{"en":"Mars is pressing on your natal Moon: for several days home may feel crowded, your buttons easier for family to press, and sleep lighter than usual. Anger in these days is often depletion in disguise. Eat properly, go to bed early, and take the long way round the relative who always starts it."}},"mars>mercury":{"conj":{"en":"Mars is crossing your natal Mercury: for several days the mind may run quick and the tongue quicker. It’s a good stretch for cutting through waffle and editing ruthlessly; notice, too, how quickly patience with slower thinkers wears thin. Use it on the report or the negotiation; sleep on any message written in anger."},"soft":{"en":"Mars is sharpening your natal Mercury: for several days focusing hard and speaking plainly may come easily, in a tone closer to confidence than aggression. Cram for the exam, close the deal, have the direct conversation you’ve been softening for weeks."},"hard":{"en":"Mars is clashing with your natal Mercury: for several days the mind can stay braced for an argument — interrupting, assuming the worst, typing faster than you think. Traffic and comment sections tend to feed it. Say less, say it later, and leave the capitals off."}},"mars>venus":{"conj":{"en":"Mars is crossing your natal Venus: for several days attraction tends to turn physical and impatient. You might want the person, the jacket, the weekend away, and want it now, as if desire had stopped asking permission. Make the move if it’s mutual; give anything that costs more than a week’s pay a night’s sleep."},"soft":{"en":"Mars is warming your natal Venus: for several days wanting something and going after it may feel natural rather than greedy. Ask them out, finish the creative project, chase the money you’re owed — charm and push can work as a team."},"hard":{"en":"Mars is goading your natal Venus: for several days love and money can start to feel like a contest — who pays, who texts first, who wanted it more. Jealousy may sit closer to the surface. If you catch yourself spending to win, or to sulk, say the want out loud instead."}},"mars>mars":{"conj":{"en":"Mars is back on your natal Mars: your Mars return, the reset of your drive that comes round every two years or so. For several days you may feel restless and short with anything that wastes your time. Choose what is worth fighting for until the next one, and start this week."},"soft":{"en":"Mars is in easy contact with your natal Mars: for several days body and resolve tend to pull the same way, which can make effort feel productive rather than frustrating. Add weight at the gym, tackle the stubborn job, ask directly for what you want."},"hard":{"en":"Mars is grinding against your natal Mars: for several days drive can meet friction — a plan that stalls, someone pushing back — and the urge may be to push harder. Bruises of either kind, physical or social, often trace back to rushing. Go ten per cent slower than you want to, especially on the road and at the gym."}},"jupiter>sun":{"conj":{"en":"Jupiter is crossing your natal Sun: for a few weeks taking up more room tends to come naturally, and it can suit you. These weeks favour being seen: the boss worth approaching, the mentor worth asking, the old plan that looks doable once you stop apologising for wanting it. Ask for the bigger role, then check your calendar before promising anything."},"soft":{"en":"Jupiter is backing your natal Sun: these weeks favour showing up as yourself. A pitch, an interview or a talk with someone senior can feel easier when you’re not straining to impress. Notice whether you’re waiting to feel ready before you let anyone see you. Say yes to one thing that makes you more visible."},"hard":{"en":"Jupiter is pressing on your natal Sun: for a few weeks ambition can outgrow your calendar. Perhaps you want the promotion or the grand gesture partly to prove a father, an old boss or a doubter wrong. Keep the dream, halve the first step, and check whether it still excites you without an audience."}},"jupiter>moon":{"conj":{"en":"Jupiter is sitting on your natal Moon: for a few weeks home can feel bigger and kinder. It might look like a call from family, guests who stay late, more appetite and more patience. Feeling safe enough to want more is the gift here. Feed people, take the long bath, and notice if comfort is turning into a nightly second helping."},"soft":{"en":"Jupiter is easing your natal Moon: these weeks can loosen the background worry you carry everywhere. Perhaps a call with your mother feels lighter, a room or a flat catches your eye, sleep comes more readily. This rest doesn’t have to be earned. When someone offers to look after you, say yes before listing reasons you don’t need it."},"hard":{"en":"Jupiter is pressing on your natal Moon: for a few weeks feelings can run large, and so can the remedies. Notice the extra takeaway, the extra plans, the yes to every family request, perhaps because a full table feels like being loved. Under it may sit a plainer wish to be held. Ask for that directly, and keep one evening empty."}},"jupiter>mercury":{"conj":{"en":"Jupiter is crossing your natal Mercury: a few weeks when your head may fill with ideas, open tabs and new courses. Talking well and writing fast can come easily, and being heard can feel simpler. What’s worth noticing is breadth: ten plans started, none finished. Pick the idea you’d still explain to a friend next month and write two pages of it."},"soft":{"en":"Jupiter is backing your natal Mercury: for a few weeks your words may land more easily. An application, a negotiation, a class you’ve eyed for months or an email to someone you’ve never dared approach can feel smoother when you sound like you believe it. Send the message you keep drafting in your head on the commute."},"hard":{"en":"Jupiter is pressing on your natal Mercury: these weeks make it easy to promise more than you can read, write or answer. Notice the yes leaving your mouth before the thought is finished, and details waved through because the big picture feels right. Usually that’s enthusiasm, not carelessness. Before you sign or announce anything, read the small print aloud."}},"jupiter>venus":{"conj":{"en":"Jupiter is touching your natal Venus: a few weeks traditionally read as generous for love, money and pleasure. It could be a date that feels easy, a friend who insists on paying, the small glow of feeling worth spending on. Enjoy it, and decide in advance the one thing you’d rather not buy just because the mood is expansive."},"soft":{"en":"Jupiter is easing your natal Venus: for a few weeks warmth and good taste are within easy reach. Making up after a quarrel, asking for a fair rate, repainting a corner of the flat — each may meet less resistance than usual. Use the goodwill to ask for something you normally talk yourself out of wanting."},"hard":{"en":"Jupiter is pressing on your natal Venus: for a few weeks appetite can outrun the budget. The dinner, the dress, the lavish gift, the romance that sounds better than it feels — it’s easy to overdo it when more looks like proof you’re valued. Keep the pleasure, drop the proving. Wait two days before any big purchase or big declaration."}},"jupiter>mars":{"conj":{"en":"Jupiter is crossing your natal Mars: a few weeks that can feel like running on extra fuel. Perhaps you train harder, start the project, say the bold thing in the meeting. When courage feels cheap, overreach tends to feel cheap too. Aim the push at one goal with a finish line, not at every irritation."},"soft":{"en":"Jupiter is backing your natal Mars: these weeks favour effort. A new sport, a renovation, a pitch, a move you’ve been circling — the push and the confidence may be there at once. Notice whether it drains into arguments you’ve already won. Book the first session or set the date while starting still feels easy."},"hard":{"en":"Jupiter is pressing on your natal Mars: for a few weeks the wish to win, and win now, can run hot. You might catch yourself signing up for too much, lifting too heavy, turning a disagreement into a crusade, perhaps because holding back feels like losing. The drive is good; the scale may be off. Choose one fight worth having and let the rest go."}},"saturn>sun":{"conj":{"en":"Saturn is sitting on your natal Sun: a sober chapter of several months. You may feel older, more tired, more watched, as shortcuts lose their appeal. The question it brings into view is what you’re for, and whose approval, a father’s or a boss’s, you’re still chasing. Choose one serious commitment and carry it slowly; what you build patiently can hold."},"soft":{"en":"Saturn is backing your natal Sun: these months favour steady work that becomes visible. A long project may be ready to take shape, someone senior may be worth asking for more, and your name can start to mean reliable. What tends to grow here is the sense of being taken seriously. Put a date and a number on the goal you keep describing vaguely."},"hard":{"en":"Saturn is pressing on your natal Sun: these months can feel like pushing against resistance. If a boss says not yet, a plan stalls or your body wants more sleep than you’d like, the pressure tends to show where your sense of self rests on someone else’s approval. Drop one obligation you keep only for appearances and guard the hours it frees."}},"saturn>moon":{"conj":{"en":"Saturn is sitting on your natal Moon: for months feelings can run quiet and heavy. Perhaps the flat needs repairs, a parent needs care, and you find yourself the adult in every room. If you cope by needing nothing, this chapter quietly questions that habit. Build one comfort routine, a Sunday soup or a phone-free evening, and keep it."},"soft":{"en":"Saturn is backing your natal Moon: these months are a good season for making home solid. Think of signing a lease, fixing the boiler, settling into a regular bedtime, talking to your mother on calmer terms. Steadiness often grows once you stop improvising your basic needs. Put one comforting habit in the calendar, as fixed as a work meeting."},"hard":{"en":"Saturn is pressing on your natal Moon: these months can feel lonely even in company. Family duty, a cold flat, a body spent by evening, and perhaps an old reflex of swallowing need so nobody worries. What this stretch brings into view is that self-reliance has a ceiling. Tell one person what you need, in a full sentence, without apologising."}},"saturn>mercury":{"conj":{"en":"Saturn is crossing your natal Mercury: for some months the mind may turn serious. Perhaps you read slower, check twice, and hear where your words were careless. Exams, contracts or one hard piece of writing ask for discipline, and the inner critic can get loud. Set a daily hour for your hardest thinking and keep it."},"soft":{"en":"Saturn is backing your natal Mercury: these months suit study and slow, solid work. A diploma, a manuscript, a well-checked contract or a difficult conversation tends to reward preparing instead of rushing, and a considered opinion can carry real weight. Commit to one structured course or project, with deadlines you set yourself and actually keep."},"hard":{"en":"Saturn is pressing on your natal Mercury: for months thinking can feel like wading. Maybe paperwork stalls, a reply is slow, and you rewrite one email five times while a voice says you’re not clever enough. That voice often dates from school. Write it down rather than obey it, then finish one small piece by noon."}},"saturn>venus":{"conj":{"en":"Saturn is sitting on your natal Venus: for months love and money ask for honesty. This contact is traditionally read as a test: which bonds want commitment, where the cracks show, where spending meets the budget. Feeling less attractive can simply mean you’re tired of performing for approval. Keep close the bonds that survive plain talk, and price your work at what it costs you."},"soft":{"en":"Saturn is backing your natal Venus: these months favour love that lasts and money that adds up. It might mean talk of moving in, a savings plan, a friendship tested and found steady. Romance can look quieter and more grown-up, and be more trustworthy for that. Have the practical talk — rent, plans, next year — you’ve been calling unromantic."},"hard":{"en":"Saturn is pressing on your natal Venus: these months can bring a feeling of scarcity in love or money. If someone seems distant, a payment runs late or pleasure feels earned rather than given, an old belief may be underneath: that affection must be deserved. Notice where you pay for closeness with extra effort, and stop paying in one place."}},"saturn>mars":{"conj":{"en":"Saturn is sitting on your natal Mars: for some months drive can feel as if it meets a wall. When results are slow, frustration may leak into snapping or quiet rage. Astrologers read this chapter as training effort into stamina. Swap sprints for a schedule: the same workout, the same writing hour, done whether you feel like it or not."},"soft":{"en":"Saturn is backing your natal Mars: these months favour disciplined effort. Training for a race, renovating a room, finishing a long project — stamina tends to hold, and a setback need not knock you off course. Strength built slowly is the kind that stays. Pick a goal that needs months rather than weeks and write down your weekly minimum."},"hard":{"en":"Saturn is pressing on your natal Mars: these months can make anger feel heavy. When rules, a boss, paperwork or your own body stand in the way of the move you want, notice what pushing harder costs: a stiff back, a cold war at home. This contact favours strategy over force. Take one blocked thing and work it in small, unglamorous steps."}},"uranus>sun":{"conj":{"en":"Uranus is crossing your natal Sun: this year, often longer, the life you built can feel a size too small. A new job, a move, a break with a boss or a parent’s expectations: each can start to look like a way to reset who you think you are. The restlessness is honest. Change one thing on purpose rather than leaving it to boredom."},"soft":{"en":"Uranus is backing your natal Sun: this period makes room to reinvent without wreckage. A side project could become a direction, an unusual offer could earn a second look, and the less polished, more-yours version of you may feel easier to show. Say yes to one experiment that the cautious part of you calls a bit odd."},"hard":{"en":"Uranus is pressing on your natal Sun: this period often shakes the scaffolding. A boss, a parent or a role you’ve outgrown can start to feel like a cage, and you may want to quit everything at once. The hunger for freedom is real. Change one thing — the job or the flat, not both — before torching the lot."}},"uranus>moon":{"conj":{"en":"Uranus is crossing your natal Moon: this year home and mood can feel less predictable. Perhaps you catch yourself picturing a move or a different household, or wake at 4 a.m. wanting a different life. Nerves often go on alert when old forms of safety stop fitting. Build stability from rhythms — sleep, meals, a walk — rather than walls."},"soft":{"en":"Uranus is backing your natal Moon: this period favours a freer way of living. It could be a new flat, a fairer split of the chores, a family habit dropped without a scene. Feelings may move faster and recover faster. Try the change to your home life you keep calling impractical, starting with one room or one evening."},"hard":{"en":"Uranus is pressing on your natal Moon: in this period the base itself may feel less solid. If family news jolts you, a move comes unplanned or sleep turns patchy, part of you may want to run, part to cling to routine; both are often fear. Keep two anchors — bedtime and one daily meal at a table — and let the rest change."}},"uranus>mercury":{"conj":{"en":"Uranus is crossing your natal Mercury: this year thinking tends to speed up and turn sideways. New subjects, insights in the shower, a new way of talking. You might notice opinions held for years loosening almost overnight. A mind that is rewiring often runs hot. Keep a notebook for the flashes and test each before announcing it."},"soft":{"en":"Uranus is backing your natal Mercury: this period favours learning something new and slightly odd. Code, a language, a field nobody expected from you. Ideas can land whole, and people who think differently may be easier to find. Sign up for the course or the online group that excites you a little more than it makes sense."},"hard":{"en":"Uranus is pressing on your natal Mercury: a jumpy mind is the classic note of this period. If plans change at the last minute, messages cross or you blurt the blunt thing and then wonder why, overloaded nerves may be the reason: too much changing at once. Cut one input — a feed, a group chat, a news app — and take that attention back."}},"uranus>venus":{"conj":{"en":"Uranus is crossing your natal Venus: this year your taste in love, money and beauty is on the move. It might be an unexpected attraction, a relationship that needs more air, restlessness about how you earn and spend. What used to charm you may start to bore you. Before you blow up a relationship, try rewriting its rules; freedom inside one is a real option."},"soft":{"en":"Uranus is backing your natal Venus: this period lets fresh air into love and money. Think of an unlikely friendship, a new way of earning, a partner who surprises you nicely. It’s often easier to like yourself once you drop the expected script. Say yes to the date, the look or the side income that feels unlike you."},"hard":{"en":"Uranus is pressing on your natal Venus: this period can make closeness feel tight. You may want space, or sense that someone you love wants it, and money can feel erratic. Part of this is often real growth, part a fear of being trapped. Tell the person concerned what kind of freedom you need, before you act it out instead."}},"uranus>mars":{"conj":{"en":"Uranus is crossing your natal Mars: this year tends to bring bursts of courage and a shorter fuse. You might feel the pull to quit, start, move or say the unsayable, and crave a new sport. An abrupt exit can start to look like the answer to everything. Give the restlessness a daily physical outlet, and notice whether the hurry follows you into the car."},"soft":{"en":"Uranus is backing your natal Mars: this period is traditionally read as giving your drive a quick, inventive edge. Acting on ideas faster, taking a considered leap, finding a new way to train or work — courage may feel natural rather than forced. Take the first step of the bold move you’ve been rehearsing: sketch the business, change the routine, try another discipline."},"hard":{"en":"Uranus is pressing on your natal Mars: this period often means friction with rules and anyone who gives orders. Perhaps you snap at limits, chase the thrill, break things — a deal, a habit, sometimes a glass. Often what you’re fighting for is autonomy. Decide which freedom actually matters and fight for that one, openly."}},"neptune>sun":{"conj":{"en":"Neptune is crossing your natal Sun: this year your sense of self can go soft at the edges. Ambition may fade, tiredness come sooner, and art, faith or quiet pull at you. A father figure might seem distant or idealised. Astrologers often read this not as losing yourself but as loosening a rigid self-image. Work gently, and keep a morning walk non-negotiable."},"soft":{"en":"Neptune is backing your natal Sun: this period often lends your life a quiet sense of meaning. Creative work, music, volunteering or prayer may feel natural, and your gentler side easier to show. Inspiration tends to come easily; discipline less so. Give the dream a time slot — an hour, twice a week — for the thing you’d do if nobody paid you."},"hard":{"en":"Neptune is pressing on your natal Sun: this period can fog your sense of direction. Goals may feel pointless, praise hollow, and you might find yourself giving too much to someone who seems to need rescuing. Often the fog thickens when you try to be what others imagine. Before big decisions, get the facts in writing and let one honest friend read them."}},"neptune>moon":{"conj":{"en":"Neptune is crossing your natal Moon: this year feelings tend to become porous. Maybe you absorb a room’s mood, cry at adverts, sleep longer and dream vividly. Home or family can feel like something you’re mourning or idealising. Sensitivity is the gift; boundaries are the work. Protect sleep, go easy on wine, and notice whose sadness you carry."},"soft":{"en":"Neptune is backing your natal Moon: in this period home has a way of growing softer. Picture music in the kitchen, a gentler bond with your mother, an empathy that reaches people before you say a word. Family instincts are often worth trusting now. Make one corner of the flat just for rest — a chair, a lamp, no phone — and actually use it."},"hard":{"en":"Neptune is pressing on your natal Moon: this period is known for blurring where you end and others begin. Perhaps you rescue, absorb, give in, then feel drained and vaguely betrayed. If a relative leans on you more than is fair, it may be because you’ve taught everyone you’re always available. Say “not tonight” once, kindly, and see how the house manages one evening without you."}},"neptune>mercury":{"conj":{"en":"Neptune is crossing your natal Mercury: this year the mind may think in images more than lists. Poetry, music and intuition often sharpen while dates, keys and small print slip. If a conversation leaves you unsure what was agreed, confirm plans by message and keep notes, then let the dreamier mind write, draw or compose without a deadline."},"soft":{"en":"Neptune is backing your natal Mercury: this period favours a softer reach in your words. Writing may grow more beautiful, listening better, and it can be easier to hear what people mean rather than just what they say. Traditionally a good season for fiction, translation, songwriting, any work that depends on listening. Keep a notebook by the bed and give half-formed ideas somewhere to land."},"hard":{"en":"Neptune is pressing on your natal Mercury: this period tends to make misunderstandings easier. It’s tempting to hear what you hope to hear, lose a detail, trust a vague promise, partly because the plain version stings. Before you sign, transfer money or believe a good story, ask the blunt question you’d rather skip, and wait for a straight answer."}},"neptune>venus":{"conj":{"en":"Neptune is crossing your natal Venus: this year love can feel like a film. You might fall for potential, long for the unavailable, or see beauty in strangers and rainy streets. Compassion grows, and so can the temptation to buy a fantasy. Keep the romance, check the facts: who shows up, who pays, who calls back."},"soft":{"en":"Neptune is backing your natal Venus: this period tends to soften love and refine your taste. Tenderness may come easily, and art, music and beautiful rooms can move you more than usual. A relationship can feel close to sacred. Spend time on beauty for its own sake: a museum afternoon, a song learned by heart, a letter written by hand."},"hard":{"en":"Neptune is pressing on your natal Venus: this period makes illusions about love or money easier to fall for. Maybe you idealise someone who doesn’t show up, or spend on something that promises a happier you. Under it there is often a longing to be rescued. Treat your heart like your bank card: look closely before handing it over."}},"neptune>mars":{"conj":{"en":"Neptune is crossing your natal Mars: this year drive tends to go underground. You may feel less sure what you want, tire faster, dodge conflict. Anger can leak sideways as sulking, sarcasm or procrastination, while desire drifts towards something still unnamed. Choose movement that feels like water — swimming, yoga, long walks — and see whether effort for something bigger than winning feels easier."},"soft":{"en":"Neptune is backing your natal Mars: this period favours effort that serves something you believe in. Volunteering, dance, art, a cause — acting from feeling rather than ego can carry further than force, and competition may matter less. Put your strength behind one cause or creative project and give it a regular, protected hour."},"hard":{"en":"Neptune is pressing on your natal Mars: willpower often goes blurry in this period. It might look like starting things and drifting, avoiding a fight you need to have, feeling worn out for no clear reason. Part of it may be the body asking for rest, part a fear of your own anger. Find one honest no you’ve swallowed and say it aloud."}},"pluto>sun":{"conj":{"en":"Pluto is crossing your natal Sun: a long chapter, often several years, traditionally read as being rebuilt from the inside. If power struggles with a boss, a father or an institution come up, they tend to press one question: who are you without their approval? Old ambitions may wither; let them. Ask what you’d do if nobody watched, and do that."},"soft":{"en":"Pluto is backing your natal Sun: this period invites a deeper kind of authority. Speaking with more weight, taking on serious responsibility, calmly ending what has run its course — each may come more naturally, and your intensity can read as trustworthy. Spend it on one long project — the career shift, the inner work, the business — and stay with it past the boring middle."},"hard":{"en":"Pluto is pressing on your natal Sun: power struggles that feel personal are the classic theme of this period. When a boss, a parent or a partner pushes, you might push back harder or shrink. Underneath there may be a fear of being erased. The work here is keeping your shape without needing to win. Name your non-negotiables and stop arguing the rest."}},"pluto>moon":{"conj":{"en":"Pluto is crossing your natal Moon: over this long stretch the oldest feelings tend to surface — about your mother, home, food, safety. A move or a family secret can stir grief and rage you didn’t know you carried. Give them a place to be heard, on the page or with someone you trust. What you dare to look at often loosens its quiet hold."},"soft":{"en":"Pluto is backing your natal Moon: this period favours untangling family patterns at the root. It might mean understanding your mother better, renovating a home full of history, or ending an old habit around food or comfort. Feelings can run deep and still stay bearable. Begin the family talk, the honest journal or the clear-out you’ve been circling for years."},"hard":{"en":"Pluto is pressing on your natal Moon: this period brings power games at home into view. It might be a relative who seems to steer your life, or you catching yourself managing everyone’s moods to feel safe. The old fear says if you let go, everything collapses. Test it gently: hand back one responsibility that was never yours to carry."}},"pluto>mercury":{"conj":{"en":"Pluto is crossing your natal Mercury: this long period tends to sharpen the mind until it seems to see through people. Research, investigation, digging up what was buried in a family story or a company may pull at you. Words gain weight; they can wound or heal. Choose what you say with care, and write the true version for yourself first."},"soft":{"en":"Pluto is backing your natal Mercury: this period lends your thinking depth and stamina. Research, psychology, investigative work, a book on a hard subject — staying with difficult material without flinching may feel possible, and your words can carry conviction. Choose one subject worth years of attention and begin studying it seriously, with a reading list and a schedule."},"hard":{"en":"Pluto is pressing on your natal Mercury: this period has a way of bringing arguments without exits and thoughts that circle at night. Say you catch yourself fixating on a message or a suspicion, or starting a war of words: often something unsaid wants out. Write the thought down, sleep on it, and decide in daylight whether it deserves a reply."}},"pluto>venus":{"conj":{"en":"Pluto is crossing your natal Venus: this long period tends to make love feel all or nothing. Attraction can run intense, jealousy surface, money and intimacy tangle. It brings into view which bonds are lukewarm and which want to go deeper, and can strip your sense of worth back to what’s actually yours. Notice where control creeps in, yours included, and say what you really want."},"soft":{"en":"Pluto is backing your natal Venus: this period favours deeper love and a sharper sense of your own value. Intimacy may grow more honest, a relationship can hold a hard truth, and charging what your work is worth may feel less awkward. Shallow pleasures often lose their pull. Have the conversation about sex, money or the future you’ve avoided because it felt too serious."},"hard":{"en":"Pluto is pressing on your natal Venus: in this period love often gets tangled with jealousy, power plays or money. Clinging, testing, staying in something because leaving feels like dying — the fear driving it is often of being replaceable. Look at where you trade control for closeness, and stop paying that price in one relationship."}},"pluto>mars":{"conj":{"en":"Pluto is crossing your natal Mars: this long period tends to turn drive into force. It can feel as if you could achieve something huge, or burn out trying. Anger may run volcanic, desire obsessive, and conflicts quick to escalate. The point is to own your strength without needing to dominate. Pour it into a demanding physical discipline and one goal measured in years."},"soft":{"en":"Pluto is backing your natal Mars: this period can lend rare staying power. It favours slow, deep work: rebuilding strength, finishing a huge project, keeping your head in a crisis. Pick the goal that scares you a little, commit to it for a year, and tell one person who can hold you to it."},"hard":{"en":"Pluto is pressing on your natal Mars: this period draws attention to standoffs where neither side wants to back down. Rage, ruthless competition, a body pushed past its limit — the fuel is often a terror of being powerless. Practise stopping before scorched earth: when you want to crush someone, walk away, sleep, and decide the next morning."}}},"tarot":{"0":{"en":{"name":"The Fool","essence":"A step taken before the map exists","message":"A young traveller strolls towards a cliff edge with a bundle on a stick, a white rose in one hand and a small dog jumping at his heels. He’s looking at the sky, not the drop. The card points to the part of you that says yes before the spreadsheet is finished: the move, the class, the call you haven’t rehearsed. It asks how much of your caution is only memory, and whether you could carry a little less of it.","today":"Say yes to one small unplanned thing — a different route home, a stranger’s question, a class you’d normally scroll past — and notice how much of your hesitation is simply habit.","shadow":"Calling it courage when you simply haven’t looked down.","question":"What would you try today if you weren’t already sure how it ends?"}},"1":{"en":{"name":"The Magician","essence":"Starting with what’s already on the table","message":"A young man stands at a table laid with a cup, a sword, a coin and a wand — one of everything. One hand lifts a wand to the sky, the other points at the ground: idea above, result below, himself the wire in between. The card asks which tools are already within reach and still unused: a skill, a contact, a free hour. Its trick is starting with them rather than waiting for better ones.","today":"Pick one thing you’ve been “preparing” to do and take the first visible step with what you already have: send the draft, book the call, buy the paint.","shadow":"Talking so well about the plan that nobody notices it hasn’t started.","question":"Which tool already in your hands have you been ignoring?"}},"2":{"en":{"name":"The High Priestess","essence":"What you know before you can explain it","message":"A woman sits between a black pillar and a white one, a half-hidden scroll in her lap, a veil of pomegranates behind her and a crescent moon at her feet. She isn’t hiding anything; she seems to wait until you’re quiet enough to hear. Perhaps a hunch about the flat, or about a friend who has gone vague, arrived before your reasons did. The card asks you not to dismiss it for that alone.","today":"Keep one decision to yourself until evening. Don’t poll friends or search it online; take it on a walk or into the shower, and notice which answer keeps coming back.","shadow":"Mistaking an old fear for intuition because it speaks in your voice.","question":"What do you already know that you haven’t yet said out loud?"}},"3":{"en":{"name":"The Empress","essence":"What grows from care, not pressure","message":"A woman reclines on soft cushions in a garden gone generous: ripe wheat at her feet, a waterfall in the trees behind, a heart-shaped shield resting beside her. Nothing here grows under orders. The card sides with whatever thrives when fed — a plant, a child, a body, a business, a meal made slowly — and treats pleasure not as the prize for finishing the list but as fertiliser.","today":"Feed something slowly today: cook one proper meal, water the plants, stretch for ten minutes, or give an hour to the project that’s been growing quietly. Enjoy it while you do it.","shadow":"Smothering what you love with more care than it asked for.","question":"What in your life grows best when you stop rushing it?"}},"4":{"en":{"name":"The Emperor","essence":"Rules that end the daily argument with yourself","message":"A grey-bearded ruler sits on a stone throne carved with rams’ heads, armour under his red robe, sceptre in one hand and orb in the other. Behind him, bare mountains: nothing soft grows here, and nothing collapses either. His gift is structure — the budget, the bedtime, the boundary said once and kept. The card invites you to set one rule, so that you need not haggle with yourself every tired evening.","today":"Make one rule and write it down: a spending limit, a time you close the laptop, a no you don’t explain twice. Keep it once today and see what it frees up.","shadow":"Confusing being in charge with being right about everything.","question":"Where would one firm rule save you a dozen small arguments?"}},"5":{"en":{"name":"The Hierophant","essence":"What tradition and good teachers already know","message":"A priest in a triple crown sits between two grey pillars, one hand raised in blessing, two kneeling students before him and a pair of crossed keys at his feet. He stands for the tested way: your grandmother’s recipe, the course with a syllabus, the mentor who has already made your mistakes. The card suggests that not every rule is a cage; some are a shortcut someone else paid for.","today":"Ask someone who has done what you’re attempting — a renovation, a hard conversation, a career change — for the one mistake they’d avoid. Then take their advice once, even if you’d have done it differently.","shadow":"Following the rulebook so you never have to decide anything yourself.","question":"Whose experience could save you from learning this the hard way?"}},"6":{"en":{"name":"The Lovers","essence":"Choosing what you love, and meaning it","message":"A man and a woman stand naked beneath an angel who spreads its wings from the clouds. Behind her grows a tree with fruit and a serpent; behind him, a tree of flames. The card is traditionally read as desire, and even more as choice. A full yes to one person, city or job means letting the others go, which may be why keeping everything vague feels so tempting.","today":"Find one place where you’re keeping two options open so nobody is disappointed. Choose one, tell the person it affects, and notice how the day feels afterwards.","shadow":"Keeping every door open so you never have to walk through one.","question":"What would you choose if no one could be disappointed by it?"}},"7":{"en":{"name":"The Chariot","essence":"Willpower that steers without reins","message":"An armoured driver stands in a stone chariot under a canopy of stars. Two sphinxes, one black and one white, sit before it facing different ways, and there are no reins. He steers by resolve alone. The card brings a familiar split into view: the part of you that wants rest and the part that wants the promotion, held together long enough to reach somewhere both can live with.","today":"Name the one result you want by tonight — the report sent, the room cleared, the run done — and steer back to it each time a mood or a message pulls you sideways.","shadow":"Forcing your way forward and calling the exhaustion discipline.","question":"Which two parts of you need to pull in the same direction today?"}},"8":{"en":{"name":"Strength","essence":"Gentle hands on a wild thing","message":"A woman in a white dress, crowned with flowers, rests her hands on a lion’s jaws and closes them without a fight. There’s no whip and no sweat on her. Her kind of strength is patience: with a temper, a craving, a frightened child, your own heart racing before a hard call. The lion here is calmed rather than defeated, and the card treats it as yours: something to befriend, not beat.","today":"If something flares today — irritation in a meeting, a craving, a sharp text — slow your breath before you answer, and approach it like a nervous dog: slowly, without arguing.","shadow":"Swallowing every feeling and taking the numbness for strength.","question":"What in you needs taming with kindness rather than force?"}},"9":{"en":{"name":"The Hermit","essence":"A small light carried somewhere quiet","message":"An old man in a grey cloak stands alone on a snowy peak, holding a lantern with a six-pointed star inside and looking down at the path. He isn’t lost; he left on purpose. Sometimes you keep asking around because your own answer is the one you’re avoiding. Such an answer tends to surface on a long walk, with the phone left in another room, and the card invites that kind of quiet.","today":"Take thirty minutes alone with no input — no podcast, no feed, no one to reply to — and ask yourself the question you’ve been outsourcing to other people.","shadow":"Retreating so far that no one can reach you with help.","question":"What would you hear if you stopped asking everyone else?"}},"10":{"en":{"name":"Wheel of Fortune","essence":"The turn you didn’t schedule","message":"A great wheel turns in the sky, marked with letters. A snake slides down one side, a jackal-headed figure rises on the other, and a sphinx sits calmly on top with a sword. In the corners, four winged creatures read their books, unbothered. The card draws attention to what shifts without your say: a deal that falls through, an old friend who calls. Often what wears you out is less the turning than insisting the wheel stand still.","today":"If something changes without your permission today — a cancelled plan, a surprise bill, an unexpected yes — ask what the new position makes possible before you mourn the old one.","shadow":"Deciding the wheel is rigged, so nothing you do matters.","question":"Which change are you fighting that could also be a way out?"}},"11":{"en":{"name":"Justice","essence":"Clear accounts and honest consequences","message":"A figure in a red robe sits between two pillars, a raised sword in one hand and level scales in the other. One white shoe peeks out from under the hem, ready to step forward. The card reads justice as accuracy rather than revenge: the bill split fairly, the apology you owe, the contract read to the end. Life tends to get simpler when you stop rounding the truth in your favour.","today":"Settle one account today: pay back the money, answer the email you’ve dodged, correct the small lie, or read the terms before you sign. Be precise, not harsh.","shadow":"Judging others by rules you quietly excuse yourself from.","question":"What would be fair here if you weren’t on either side?"}},"12":{"en":{"name":"The Hanged Man","essence":"What you see once you stop pushing","message":"A man hangs upside down by one ankle from a living tree, the other leg bent behind his knee, hands behind his back. His face is calm, and a halo glows around his head. He isn’t being punished; he chose the pause. Pushing harder often only tightens the knot. The stuck project, the reply that hasn’t come, the decision on hold: the card invites you to read the delay as information.","today":"Stop forcing one stuck thing for a day. Instead of sending a third reminder or rewriting the plan again, ask what this delay might show you that speed would hide.","shadow":"Stalling indefinitely and wearing the delay like a halo.","question":"What would you see if you looked at this problem upside down?"}},"13":{"en":{"name":"Death","essence":"An ending that clears the ground","message":"A skeleton in black armour rides a white horse under a banner marked with a white rose. A king has fallen, a priest pleads, and a child simply looks up. Far off, the sun rises between two towers. The card is traditionally read as an ending rather than a literal death: a role, a habit, a version of you that stopped fitting a while ago. Such endings tend to hurt most where you’ve invested most.","today":"Let one thing end cleanly today: unsubscribe, delete the draft that has sat unsent for months, clear the shelf, or tell someone you’re stepping back. Skip the funeral; open the window.","shadow":"Keeping something on life support because letting go feels like failure.","question":"What has already ended that you’re still paying rent on?"}},"14":{"en":{"name":"Temperance","essence":"The right mix, poured slowly","message":"A winged angel stands with one foot in a pool and one on dry land, pouring water from one cup into another so steadily that none spills. Behind, a path climbs towards a sunrise between the hills. What the card teaches is dosage: work and rest, coffee and water, honesty and tact. All-or-nothing can feel decisive; the slow mix is what tends to last.","today":"Find one place where you’ve swung to an extreme — skipped meals then a takeaway binge, silence then a rant — and correct it by a quarter turn, not a full reversal.","shadow":"Diluting everything until nothing you do has any taste.","question":"What in your day needs a little more of something, not a total change?"}},"15":{"en":{"name":"The Devil","essence":"The chain you could slip off","message":"A horned figure crouches on a black pedestal, torch pointed down. Chained to the block below stand a naked man and woman with small horns of their own. The chains hang loose around their necks. The card turns the light on the habit that can end up running you — the scroll at midnight, the ex you check on, the spending that soothes. Such a habit often holds because it still pays you something: relief, numbness, an excuse.","today":"Pick the habit that ate the most time or money yesterday and make it slightly harder: log out, leave the card at home, put the phone in another room after ten.","shadow":"Blaming the chain while keeping one hand wrapped around it.","question":"What do you keep going back to, and what does it give you?"}},"16":{"en":{"name":"The Tower","essence":"The crack that was already there","message":"Lightning strikes a tall tower on a rock and knocks the crown from its top. Flames burst from the windows and two figures fall headfirst through the dark. It looks like disaster, and for a moment it is. But the tower stood on something false, and the card asks what in your life rests on similar ground: a plan that couldn’t hold, a story you keep telling yourself. A sudden truth often costs less than a slow collapse.","today":"Find one thing you’re propping up that’s already cracked — a plan, a pretence, a polite silence — and stop spending effort hiding the crack. Say the true sentence.","shadow":"Blowing everything up because slow repair feels too humiliating.","question":"Which part of your life is standing on a story you no longer believe?"}},"17":{"en":{"name":"The Star","essence":"Hope that heals by being shared","message":"After the Tower, a woman kneels naked by a pool under one large star and seven small ones, pouring from two jugs — one back into the water, one onto the earth. Nothing is rushed. The card invites you to notice what is quietly returning after a hard stretch: appetite, sleep, the wish to make something again.","today":"Give a little attention to whatever is recovering — a friendship, your stamina, an old idea — and feed it without demanding it bloom on schedule.","shadow":"Waiting for a sign instead of filling the jug yourself.","question":"What might be coming back to life in you, and how could you tend it today?"}},"18":{"en":{"name":"The Moon","essence":"When fear draws shapes in the dark","message":"A full moon with a sleeping face hangs between two towers. Below, a dog and a wolf howl at it, and a crayfish crawls out of a pool onto a path that winds off into the hills. Everything looks bigger at night. The card asks you to sort through the worry about money or the message you read three ways: some of it may be instinct, some just tiredness wearing a mask.","today":"Before you act on a fear today, check it in daylight: eat something, drink water, ask one direct question. Leave anything big until after you’ve slept.","shadow":"Treating every 3 a.m. thought as a prophecy.","question":"Which fear might shrink if you said it plainly to someone?"}},"19":{"en":{"name":"The Sun","essence":"Plain joy, nothing to prove","message":"A naked child rides a white horse beneath a huge, smiling sun, arms flung wide, a red banner streaming behind. Sunflowers lean over a garden wall. Nothing in this card is hiding. It’s warmth without strategy: laughing out loud, being good at something in public, a day that simply goes well. The card invites you to stop bracing for a hidden snag.","today":"Do one thing today purely because it’s fun or warm — call the friend who makes you laugh, eat outside, show someone what you made — and don’t apologise for enjoying it.","shadow":"Performing happiness so no one notices you’re tired.","question":"What would you do today if you didn’t have to look serious?"}},"20":{"en":{"name":"Judgement","essence":"The call you can’t pretend not to hear","message":"An angel blows a trumpet from the clouds, a flag with a red cross hanging from it. Below, grey figures rise from open coffins floating on the water, arms raised towards the sound. The card is about waking up: seeing your own life clearly and being unable to unsee it, an old ambition stirring, an old excuse that no longer works. It asks you to answer while the sound is loud.","today":"Write down the thing you keep promising yourself you’d do “one day” — the course, the move, the apology — and take the first step that makes it awkward to back out.","shadow":"Replaying old mistakes instead of climbing out of them.","question":"What might be calling you back that you’ve been ignoring?"}},"21":{"en":{"name":"The World","essence":"Finishing well, and knowing you have","message":"A dancer floats inside a great oval wreath tied with red ribbons, a wand in each hand, a purple sash wrapped around her. In the four corners, an angel, an eagle, a lion and a bull look on. The card brings into view a circle that has closed: a degree finished, a debt cleared, a year survived. It invites a bow before you rush to the next thing; otherwise nothing ever quite feels finished.","today":"Mark one thing you’ve finished, however small — the tax return, the hard week, the wall you painted. Tell someone, tick it off properly, and take an hour before starting anything new.","shadow":"Never calling anything finished, so you never have to let it go.","question":"What have you completed that you haven’t yet let yourself celebrate?"}},"22":{"en":{"name":"Ace of Wands","essence":"The spark before the plan","message":"A hand reaches out of a cloud holding a living wand, fresh leaves sprouting from it, a few already drifting down. Below lie a river, green hills and a castle in the distance. The card is read as desire at its first flicker: the idea in the shower, the urge to start a band or a business. A spark like this rarely stays so bright for long, so it invites you to act while it’s hot.","today":"Catch one idea that excites you today and give it a body within the hour: a note with three next steps, a rough sketch, a message to someone who’d help.","shadow":"Collecting exciting beginnings and never letting one become a middle.","question":"What makes you want to start something right now?"}},"23":{"en":{"name":"Two of Wands","essence":"Restless in a castle you built","message":"A man in a red hat stands on castle battlements, a small globe in one hand and a wand in the other, a second wand fixed to the wall beside him. He owns what he can see and is still looking past it. Perhaps you’ve built something decent — a job, a routine, a city — and the comfort hasn’t cured the itch. Then the question the card raises is no longer whether, but where.","today":"Spend twenty minutes sketching where you’d go next if you stopped waiting: write two real options, one concrete step for each, and pick which one to test this week.","shadow":"Planning the trip forever from the safety of the balcony.","question":"What do you keep looking at beyond the walls you’ve built?"}},"24":{"en":{"name":"Three of Wands","essence":"Watching for the ships you sent","message":"A man stands on a ridge with his back to us, three staves planted in the ground, looking out over a golden bay where ships are already sailing. He made his move and is watching it unfold. It could be an application submitted, a pitch sent, a first order or two. Once a plan has met the world, the card draws attention to a familiar temptation: standing on the cliff, refreshing your inbox.","today":"If something you started is already moving, plan the next leg instead of checking on it again: who to contact if it works, what to prepare, where you’d take it next.","shadow":"Demanding results before the ships could possibly have landed.","question":"What have you already set in motion that deserves a bigger plan?"}},"25":{"en":{"name":"Four of Wands","essence":"A welcome worth stopping for","message":"Four wands stand in the ground with a garland of flowers and fruit strung between them like a gate. Two figures raise bouquets in greeting, and a castle and a small crowd wait beyond. The card celebrates arriving somewhere you worked to reach: the keys to a new flat, the probation passed, the first dinner in a finished kitchen. Unmarked, such effort tends to turn invisible, even to you.","today":"Turn one small win into a shared moment today: tell your family the news, bring cake to work, have friends over with no bigger reason than the win itself.","shadow":"Waiting for a bigger reason before you let anyone celebrate you.","question":"What small win deserves a toast with the people who helped?"}},"26":{"en":{"name":"Five of Wands","essence":"Everyone swinging, no one leading","message":"Five young men raise their staves and swing them at each other in a jumble of angles. Nobody’s hurt, nobody’s winning, and it isn’t clear what they’re fighting about. It looks like any group with no agreed direction: the meeting where everyone talks, the family plan with five versions, the group chat argument. Often the fight is really about who gets heard.","today":"If a disagreement starts today, say what you want in one sentence, ask the other person to do the same, and check whether you’re arguing about direction or just about who’s driving.","shadow":"Picking fights just to feel something when everything else is stuck.","question":"What are you really competing for in this argument?"}},"27":{"en":{"name":"Six of Wands","essence":"Being seen for what you did","message":"A rider crowned with laurel sits high on a white horse, holding a wand with a second wreath tied to it, while a crowd on foot lifts their staves around him. The card is about credit given in public: praise in the team meeting, a post that lands, a client who tells a friend. Letting it in is the harder part. Brushing off praise doesn’t make you humble, just harder to thank.","today":"Say yes to visibility today: share the result, put your name on the work, accept the compliment with a plain thank you. If someone helped, name them in public too.","shadow":"Needing the crowd’s applause before your work feels real.","question":"What did you do well recently that you’ve been too modest to mention?"}},"28":{"en":{"name":"Seven of Wands","essence":"Holding your ground from higher up","message":"A man stands on a ledge, fending off six staves that rise from below with one held crossways in both hands. Look at his feet: one boot, one shoe. He didn’t have time to dress for this. The card speaks to defending a position you’ve earned — your price, your idea, your boundary — while others want a piece of it. Being outnumbered isn’t the same as being wrong.","today":"If someone pushes back today, restate your position once, calmly, without new justifications. Hold it unless they show you a fact you didn’t have — not just more pressure.","shadow":"Treating every question as an attack you must repel.","question":"What are you defending that’s genuinely worth the effort?"}},"29":{"en":{"name":"Eight of Wands","essence":"Everything moving at once, fast","message":"Eight staves fly through a clear sky in parallel, angled down towards a green valley and a river. No people, no hands, nothing to stop them. Its subject is speed: replies landing together, plans confirmed, tickets booked, news faster than you can take it in. If something that stalled for weeks starts to move, the card invites you to catch rather than push.","today":"Clear the runway: answer the three messages you’ve been sitting on, confirm the plan, send the invoice. Keep replies short and decisions quick, and let momentum do some of the work.","shadow":"Replying to everything instantly and thinking about nothing.","question":"What might shift if you answered today instead of letting it wait?"}},"30":{"en":{"name":"Nine of Wands","essence":"Tired, wary, and still on watch","message":"A man with a bandaged head leans on a wand and glances over his shoulder, eight more staves standing behind him like a fence. He’s been hit before and stands braced for another blow. It is a card of last stretches: the final month of a degree, the renovation, the hard year. Wariness like this is earned. Worth noticing, too, is how much of the distance is already behind you.","today":"Protect your reserves for one more push: cancel one optional thing, eat properly, ask for a hand with the heaviest task. Then take the next step, not the whole remaining distance.","shadow":"Suspecting everyone because the last person let you down.","question":"Who could you let past the fence to help with the final stretch?"}},"31":{"en":{"name":"Ten of Wands","essence":"Carrying more than anyone asked you to","message":"A man trudges towards a distant town with ten heavy staves clutched in his arms, bent so low that his face is hidden behind them. He can’t see where he’s going. Each stick can stand for something you said yes to, one at a time: the extra shift, the family admin, the friend’s move, the project nobody else wanted. The card asks whether all of it was ever yours to carry.","today":"List everything you’re carrying this week, then put one stick down: hand it over, delay it, or say plainly that you can’t. Notice who notices — often fewer people than you feared.","shadow":"Turning exhaustion into proof that you’re good and needed.","question":"Which stick in your arms belongs to someone else?"}},"32":{"en":{"name":"Page of Wands","essence":"Curiosity with its sleeves rolled up","message":"A youth in a feathered cap and a tunic patterned with salamanders stands in the desert, holding a tall sprouting staff and studying it as if it were about to speak. There’s no plan yet, only fascination. The card describes the beginner’s thrill: the first guitar lesson, the new language app, the hobby you’d be embarrassed to explain. The point is to be bad at it happily.","today":"Try something new at beginner level: watch a tutorial and do the first exercise, book a trial class, ask an expert a naive question. Let it be clumsy.","shadow":"Announcing big plans to everyone before you’ve tried them once.","question":"What are you curious about that you’ve never let yourself be bad at?"}},"33":{"en":{"name":"Knight of Wands","essence":"Passion at full gallop","message":"A knight in armour and a salamander-patterned tunic rides a rearing horse in the desert, flame-coloured plumes streaming from the helmet, staff held high. The rider is moving before deciding where. The card embodies the urge to act now: quit, book the flight, text first, start the business on Monday. That heat can get things done; it can also burn through people and plans if nobody steers.","today":"Put your impatience to work: pick the one task you’ve been circling and finish it in one fast sitting. Save the big irreversible moves for after you’ve slept.","shadow":"Mistaking the thrill of leaving for knowing where you’re going.","question":"Where is your impatience useful, and where is it just running away?"}},"34":{"en":{"name":"Queen of Wands","essence":"Warmth that knows its own worth","message":"A queen holds a staff and a sunflower on a throne carved with lions, a black cat at her feet. She sits wide and easy, clearly in charge. The confidence this card shows is practical: running a household, a team or a dinner party without losing your temper or your shine. The card makes it easier to notice how people respond once you stop asking permission to take up room.","today":"Walk into one room today — a meeting, a party, a family call — as if you’re welcome there. Speak first, take the good seat, give your opinion without the apology in front of it.","shadow":"Needing to be the brightest person in every room.","question":"What would you do today if you trusted that people like you?"}},"35":{"en":{"name":"King of Wands","essence":"Vision with the nerve to lead it","message":"A king leans forward on a throne carved with lions and salamanders, a flowering staff in hand, a small salamander at his feet. He looks about to stand and give an order. This is leadership by vision: the founder, the coach, the friend who says “here’s where we’re going.” The card’s quiet point: people tend to follow someone who has decided, not the loudest voice in the room.","today":"Make the call someone has been waiting on: set the date, choose the direction, assign the tasks. Say it in one clear sentence, and own it if it proves wrong.","shadow":"Leading so hard that nobody else gets a say.","question":"Where are people waiting for you to decide?"}},"36":{"en":{"name":"Ace of Cups","essence":"A heart full enough to spill over","message":"A hand reaches out of a cloud holding a single cup, and it is already overflowing: five streams fall into a pond of lilies while a dove drops a small white wafer into it. The cup is given, not earned. The card draws attention to feeling that wants back in: a crush, a crying jag that clears the air, an unexpected fondness for someone you’d written off.","today":"Let one feeling all the way in today instead of managing it: say the warm thing out loud, cry at the song, text the person who crossed your mind first.","shadow":"Treating a rush of feeling as a promise someone made you","question":"What feeling do you keep postponing because you’re too busy to have it?"}},"37":{"en":{"name":"Two of Cups","essence":"Meeting someone exactly halfway","message":"Two people stand face to face, each holding out a cup to the other, as if signing something without paper. Above them floats a staff crowned with a winged lion’s head: desire, and the words that keep it honest. The card asks where you are met as an equal — a date that goes both ways, a colleague who returns the favour, an apology answered with another.","today":"Make one exchange even today. Answer the message with the same care it was sent with, split the bill or the chore fairly, and notice who meets you halfway without being asked.","shadow":"Mirroring someone so closely you forget what you wanted","question":"Who do you feel like an equal with, and when did you last tell them?"}},"38":{"en":{"name":"Three of Cups","essence":"The friends who make you laugh again","message":"Three women dance in a ring with their cups raised high, and the ground at their feet is heaped with pumpkins and grapes. Nobody is in charge; nobody watches from the edge. Here friendship works as nourishment, and you might recognise it in the group chat that turns a bad day into a joke, the birthday you nearly skipped, the people who knew you before you had it together.","today":"Make a plan with friends rather than waiting to be invited: a coffee, a walk, a ridiculous voice note. Celebrate one small win out loud, yours or someone else’s.","shadow":"Hiding in the crowd so no one notices how you actually are","question":"Who do you laugh with most easily, and when did you last see them in person?"}},"39":{"en":{"name":"Four of Cups","essence":"What boredom keeps you from seeing","message":"A young man sits under a tree with his arms folded, glaring at three cups lined up on the grass. From a cloud beside him, a hand offers a fourth, and he hasn’t noticed. The card points to the flatness that follows too much of the same: the scroll, the same three takeaway places, a friend you’ve stopped listening to. Sometimes boredom is a disappointment not yet admitted.","today":"Say yes today to one thing you’d normally wave away — an invitation, a new route, a different lunch. Then ask yourself, privately, whether a disappointment sits underneath the boredom.","shadow":"Refusing every new cup because the old ones let you down","question":"What have you stopped noticing because you decided in advance it wouldn’t help?"}},"40":{"en":{"name":"Five of Cups","essence":"Grief that hasn’t turned around yet","message":"A figure in a long black cloak bows over three spilled cups, their contents soaking into the ground. Behind him two more stand upright, and a bridge crosses the river towards home; he hasn’t turned to see them. The card honours loss — a breakup, a job, the parent you hoped for and didn’t get — and quietly draws attention to what is still standing.","today":"Give the loss its due: name it, write it down, or tell one person it still hurts. Then turn round once and count what’s still standing — two cups is not nothing.","shadow":"Replaying the spill so long you forget the bridge home","question":"What is still standing behind you that you haven’t turned to look at?"}},"41":{"en":{"name":"Six of Cups","essence":"Simple kindness that tastes like childhood","message":"In an old courtyard, a boy bends to hand a smaller girl a cup full of white flowers. Five more cups bloom around them, and a guard walks away, as if nothing here needs guarding. The card calls up the sweetness of the familiar — a grandmother’s recipe, a friend from school, the street you grew up on — and asks how you were before you learned caution.","today":"Do one thing the younger you would have loved: the old song, the cheap sweets, the drawing, the call to a childhood friend. Give a small gift with no reason attached.","shadow":"Living in the old days because today asks more of you","question":"What did you love at ten that you could bring back into this week?"}},"42":{"en":{"name":"Seven of Cups","essence":"Too many dreams, not one decision","message":"A dark figure stands before seven cups floating on a cloud, each holding a different prize: a castle, a pile of jewels, a wreath, a snake, a dragon, a veiled glowing shape. From here, all of them look possible. You might recognise the twelve open tabs — flats, career pivots, people you could date — and the card asks you to notice the quiet comfort of never choosing.","today":"Pick one of the daydreams and give it a real-world test today: a price, a date, a phone call, one hour of actual work. The rest can wait.","shadow":"Keeping every option open so you never have to lose one","question":"Which of your daydreams would survive a Tuesday morning?"}},"43":{"en":{"name":"Eight of Cups","essence":"Walking away from what no longer feeds you","message":"Under a watchful moon, a figure in a red cloak walks away from eight cups stacked neatly on the shore. Nothing is broken; there’s only a gap where one cup should be, and he has stopped pretending not to see it. Often read as the quiet leaving, the card asks where fine has become the problem: the job that’s fine, the friendship that’s fine, the city that’s fine.","today":"Notice one place where you keep showing up out of habit. There’s no need to leave today. Ask honestly whether it’s enough, and write down anything that’s missing.","shadow":"Leaving every time things get ordinary and calling it growth","question":"What are you staying with only because leaving would be awkward?"}},"44":{"en":{"name":"Nine of Cups","essence":"Letting enough feel like enough","message":"A well-fed man sits on a bench with his arms crossed and a satisfied grin, nine cups lined up on the shelf behind him like trophies. Traditionally it is the wish card, and it asks you to notice whether something you wanted is already here. The harder part, for many people, is letting it be enough: eating the good meal slowly instead of photographing it and planning the next.","today":"Enjoy something you already have, deliberately: the coat you saved for, the quiet flat, the person beside you. Say thank you to someone who made it possible.","shadow":"Smugness, or needing others to see how well you’re doing","question":"Which wish of yours has already come true without a celebration?"}},"45":{"en":{"name":"Ten of Cups","essence":"Home as the people, not the walls","message":"A couple stands arm in arm, free hands lifted towards a rainbow of ten cups. Beside them two children dance, ignoring the view, and a small house sits on the hill. The whole picture is one of belonging you can live inside: a Sunday lunch that runs long, the friend who has your spare key, the chosen family who turn up when the boiler breaks.","today":"Make home feel like home in one small way today: cook for someone, call the relative you actually like, fix the drawer, set the table properly. Notice who you’d tell good news to first.","shadow":"Performing a perfect family for photos while nobody talks","question":"Who feels like home to you, and do they know it?"}},"46":{"en":{"name":"Page of Cups","essence":"A tender impulse worth taking seriously","message":"A young page in a flowered tunic stands by the sea, holding up a cup — and a small fish has popped its head out to look at him. He isn’t alarmed; he’s charmed. The card favours tender, unguarded impulses: an odd idea for a story, a shy message you’d like to send, a feeling you’d usually laugh off before it had finished forming.","today":"Take one strange, soft impulse seriously today: write the silly poem, send the shy message, buy the flowers for no reason. Don’t explain it to anyone.","shadow":"Sulking like a teenager when a feeling isn’t returned","question":"What small, odd idea keeps surfacing that you keep dismissing as silly?"}},"47":{"en":{"name":"Knight of Cups","essence":"Romance offered at a walking pace","message":"A knight in a winged helmet rides a white horse at a slow walk, holding a cup out in front of him like a proposal. He isn’t charging anywhere; he wants to be seen arriving. The card describes the quality of the gesture — the invitation, the long message, the plan pitched with your whole heart — and asks whether you love the offer more than the follow-through.","today":"Make one generous offer today and mean it: the invitation, the compliment, the “I’d love to help with that”. Then put the next step in your calendar, so the offer comes with a follow-through.","shadow":"Falling for the idea of someone instead of the person","question":"Who are you courting in your head instead of in real life?"}},"48":{"en":{"name":"Queen of Cups","essence":"Listening until you hear what isn’t said","message":"A queen sits on a throne at the very edge of the sea, gazing at an ornate cup with a lid — the only covered cup in the suit. She isn’t drinking from it; she’s listening to it. The card points to emotional intelligence as a quality you can practise or recognise: hearing the real problem under the small one, sitting with someone’s mess without trying to tidy it.","today":"In one conversation today, listen for the feeling under the words and name it gently: “that sounds exhausting”. Do the same for yourself before bed.","shadow":"Absorbing everyone’s moods until you can’t find your own","question":"Whose feelings are you carrying today that were never yours to hold?"}},"49":{"en":{"name":"King of Cups","essence":"Calm in the middle of rough water","message":"A king sits on a stone throne in the middle of a choppy sea, a cup in one hand, a sceptre in the other. A ship strains on one side, a fish leaps on the other; he feels the swell without letting it steer. Notice what feeling held steady looks like: a parent keeping their voice level through a supermarket tantrum, a manager answering a furious email without heat.","today":"When something stirs you up today, wait ten minutes before you reply, speak or buy. Feel the whole wave, then answer from the far side of it.","shadow":"Staying so calm that nobody can tell what you feel","question":"What would you say right now if you weren’t managing everyone’s reaction?"}},"50":{"en":{"name":"Ace of Swords","essence":"One clear thought that cuts through fog","message":"A hand bursts from a cloud gripping a sword straight up, its point through the ring of a golden crown hung with olive and palm. Below lie bare mountains: nothing soft here. The card invites a moment of clarity — the sentence that names the problem plainly, the honest feedback, the “no” you’ve been circling for weeks. Clear truth tends to feel sharp, and often a little cold.","today":"Write what’s bothering you in one plain sentence today — no adjectives, no excuses. Read it back slowly: the answer is often already inside the wording.","shadow":"Being right so sharply that nobody can hear it","question":"What do you already know but haven’t yet said in plain words?"}},"51":{"en":{"name":"Two of Swords","essence":"Refusing to look so you needn’t choose","message":"A blindfolded woman sits on a stone bench with her back to the sea, arms crossed over her chest, a long sword balanced in each hand. She is perfectly still, as if moving would mean choosing. The card makes it easier to notice a stand-off you might be postponing: two job offers, a friend’s two versions of one story, a conversation you avoid by never starting it.","today":"Take the blindfold off for a quarter of an hour: write both options side by side with what each would cost you. You don’t have to decide today, only to look.","shadow":"Calling it peace when it’s only refusing to feel","question":"What decision are you avoiding by keeping yourself perfectly balanced?"}},"52":{"en":{"name":"Three of Swords","essence":"A painful truth, allowed to be felt","message":"A red heart hangs in a grey sky, pierced clean through by three swords, while rain pours behind it. There’s no figure, no story, only the hurt itself. The card asks you to look at a hurt you may already carry — an overheard comment, a text you weren’t meant to see, something that was true all along. Pain named accurately often heals more cleanly.","today":"Name one hurt you’ve been carrying — new or old — exactly as it is, to yourself or one trusted person. Then let it rain for an evening without fixing anything.","shadow":"Reopening the wound so often it never gets to close","question":"Which hurt are you still explaining away instead of feeling?"}},"53":{"en":{"name":"Four of Swords","essence":"Lying down before you fall down","message":"In a quiet church, a knight lies stretched out on a tomb, hands folded, eyes closed. Three swords hang on the wall above him and a fourth rests beneath, put down for now. A stained-glass window lets in the only colour. The scene invites rest as a decision rather than a collapse: the phone in another room, the cancelled evening, the afternoon nap you stop apologising for.","today":"Schedule twenty minutes of real nothing today: no phone, no podcast, no tidying. A tired mind tends to make every problem look like a threat; let it go quiet first.","shadow":"Hiding from a problem and calling it a break","question":"What would you stop worrying about if you’d slept properly for three nights?"}},"54":{"en":{"name":"Five of Swords","essence":"Winning the argument, losing the people","message":"A man smirks as he gathers up swords, three in his arms and two left on the ground, while two figures walk off towards the shore, one with a hand over his face. The sky is torn with wind. The card asks about the argument won and then regretted: the group chat pile-on, the last word at dinner, a point made so well that nobody calls back.","today":"Before you send a sharp reply today, ask what you’d actually win and who you’d lose. Sometimes the strongest move is putting the sword down and going home.","shadow":"Needing to be right because being wrong feels like disappearing","question":"Which fight are you still trying to win that costs more than it’s worth?"}},"55":{"en":{"name":"Six of Swords","essence":"Moving towards calmer water, slowly","message":"A ferryman poles a boat across the water, a hunched woman and a child huddled beside six upright swords. The water is choppy on one side, smooth on the side they’re heading towards. The card is read as leaving a hard stretch behind — a move after a breakup, a new job after a bad one. The swords come along; the card asks who else could steer for a while.","today":"Accept help getting from here to there today — a lift, a friend’s advice, someone who has done it before. Choose the calmer route, even if it takes longer.","shadow":"Leaving the place but packing every argument to take along","question":"What are you ready to leave behind, and who could row for a while?"}},"56":{"en":{"name":"Seven of Swords","essence":"Getting away with it — or trying to","message":"A man tiptoes away from a camp of bright tents, five swords clutched awkwardly in his arms, grinning back over his shoulder. Two swords stay stuck in the ground behind him: he couldn’t carry everything. The scene holds the clever shortcut up for inspection — an excuse that isn’t quite true, credit quietly taken, a plan kept to yourself because it might not survive a question.","today":"Check one shortcut you’re tempted by today: would you be comfortable explaining it out loud? If yes, take it quietly. If not, carry less and do it straight.","shadow":"Lying to yourself first so the lie to others feels fine","question":"What are you doing alone because you’re afraid of being asked about it?"}},"57":{"en":{"name":"Eight of Swords","essence":"A cage made mostly of thoughts","message":"A woman stands blindfolded with her arms loosely tied, eight swords planted in the mud around her. Look closer: the swords don’t close the circle, and the knots are slack. She could walk out if she could see. The card points to a trap built from thoughts — “I can’t afford it”, “they’d never let me”, “it’s too late” — repeated until they feel like walls.","today":"Write down one “I can’t” you’ve said this week and test it: one question to a real person, one search, one small step. Plenty of walls are thinner than they sound.","shadow":"Waiting to be rescued from knots you could untie","question":"Which “I can’t” in your life is really “I’m scared to”?"}},"58":{"en":{"name":"Nine of Swords","essence":"The 3 a.m. thoughts that lie","message":"A woman sits bolt upright in bed in the dark, face in her hands, nine swords lined up on the black wall behind her. Notice that none of them touch her. This is often called the 3 a.m. card: the email you replay, the symptom you search, the conversation rehearsed until it becomes a catastrophe. Worry tends to be louder at night, when there’s nothing to do with it.","today":"Take the worry out of your head and onto paper today: write the fear, then the next practical step, then when you could take it. Fears often shrink in daylight and in writing.","shadow":"Treating a frightening thought as proof that it’s true","question":"What is the actual worst case, and what would you do on day one?"}},"59":{"en":{"name":"Ten of Swords","essence":"An ending that lets you stop","message":"A man lies face down by the water with ten swords in his back — the deck’s most dramatic card, almost theatrical. But look past him: the black sky is breaking into a gold line of dawn over a calm sea. The card asks what has truly run its course — a project, a pretence, a relationship you kept resuscitating. Naming an ending plainly can bring its own relief.","today":"If something has clearly ended, stop reviving it today: delete the draft, cancel the subscription, stop rereading the old thread. Then do one ordinary, steadying thing slowly — a shower, a walk, breakfast.","shadow":"Making a drama of the ending so you needn’t start again","question":"What is already over that you keep giving one more chance?"}},"60":{"en":{"name":"Page of Swords","essence":"Curious, alert, asking one more question","message":"A young page stands on a windy hilltop, sword raised in both hands, glancing back over his shoulder as if he heard something. Clouds race, birds scatter, trees bend. He is all attention. Call it a beginner’s mind with an edge, a quality worth practising: the question nobody else asks in the meeting, the article you fact-check, the new skill you’re clumsy at but hungry for.","today":"Ask the question you’ve been too polite to ask today — at work, in a shop, on a family call. Then check one thing you believe against a reliable source.","shadow":"Gossip and suspicion passed off as curiosity","question":"What are you curious about that you’ve been pretending to already understand?"}},"61":{"en":{"name":"Knight of Swords","essence":"Full speed towards the point","message":"A knight charges at full gallop, sword raised, leaning so far forward he’s ahead of his own horse. Clouds are ripped sideways, trees bend in the wind he makes. The card shows thought turned into speed: the email sent in two minutes, the plan pitched before anyone’s finished their coffee, the decision made on the train. Useful for a deadline, often rough on whoever stands in the way.","today":"Use the speed on one stuck task today: draft it, send it, book it within the hour. For anything involving feelings, slow down by half and listen first.","shadow":"Cutting people off mid-sentence because you’re sure you know","question":"Where would going slower actually get you there faster?"}},"62":{"en":{"name":"Queen of Swords","essence":"Kind enough to tell you the truth","message":"A queen sits in profile on a throne set high among the clouds, sword upright in one hand, the other lifted as if to say “go on, I’m listening — but get to the point.” A single bird flies above her. The card holds up clear-eyed kindness, in others or in you: the friend who reads your contract, straight feedback from a boss, a no without a lecture.","today":"Say one true thing plainly today without padding it in apologies: the price, the deadline, the “that doesn’t work for me”. Warmth and directness can share a sentence.","shadow":"Cutting people with accuracy because softness once got you hurt","question":"Where are you over-explaining something that needs only one sentence?"}},"63":{"en":{"name":"King of Swords","essence":"The fair decision, made and owned","message":"A king sits facing you squarely, sword upright and slightly tilted, eyes level. His throne is carved with butterflies, but nothing about him flutters. The card brings into view judgement you can trust, a quality you can borrow: reading all the small print, hearing both sides and then actually deciding — like a fair referee, or a parent who sets a rule and explains it once.","today":"Settle one decision you’ve been putting off today: gather the facts, give yourself an hour, choose, and tell whoever it affects why — in two sentences.","shadow":"Rules applied so coldly that nobody dares tell you anything","question":"What would you decide if you were advising a friend instead of yourself?"}},"64":{"en":{"name":"Ace of Pentacles","essence":"A real start you can hold","message":"From a cloud, an open palm offers a single gold coin, heavy and bright, above a garden of white lilies. Beyond the hedge, an arch opens onto a path towards the mountains. The card draws attention to opportunity in solid form, the kind you can hold: a first paid client, a savings account opened, the gym membership actually used. Small, real and yours to plant.","today":"Plant one small, tangible seed today: put a little money aside, send the invoice, sign up for the class, buy the good shoes. Something you could point to next month.","shadow":"Waiting for the perfect offer while ignoring the one in your hand","question":"What small, concrete thing could you start today that would still matter in a year?"}},"65":{"en":{"name":"Two of Pentacles","essence":"Juggling well, with a little rhythm","message":"A young man in a tall hat dances on the spot, keeping two coins in the air, linked by a ribbon that loops like a figure eight. Behind him, two ships climb huge waves. He doesn’t control the sea, only his footwork. The card asks how you keep things moving — two jobs, rent and a birthday, the school run and the deadline — with rhythm, or with panic.","today":"List what you’re juggling today and decide which two balls matter most. Keep those moving, let one drop on purpose, and move your body between tasks.","shadow":"Saying yes to everything and calling the chaos flexibility","question":"Which of the things you’re juggling could you put down without anyone noticing?"}},"66":{"en":{"name":"Three of Pentacles","essence":"Good work, made better by others","message":"In a stone church, a mason stands on a bench working at an arch while a monk and a man holding the plans look up and talk it through. Three pentacles are carved into the stone above them. Each knows something the others don’t. The card is traditionally read as skilled teamwork: a colleague who checks your draft, a builder who listens, a project that improves because you asked.","today":"Show unfinished work today to one person whose eye you trust, and ask a specific question: “what would you cut?” Credit someone by name for their part in a shared win.","shadow":"Doing it all yourself because nobody else does it properly","question":"Whose skill would make your work better if you stopped being proud about asking?"}},"67":{"en":{"name":"Four of Pentacles","essence":"Holding on tight to feel safe","message":"A crowned man sits with a city behind him, hugging one coin to his chest, another balanced on his head, two pinned under his feet. He can’t stand up, eat or wave without losing something. Worth noticing here is safety that tightens into a grip: savings worth protecting, and the small pleasure or chance refused even when affordable, perhaps because enough has never felt like enough.","today":"Today, loosen your grip on one thing by a notch — money, a role, a plan, a person: spend a little on something good, share the task, ask for help.","shadow":"Confusing control with safety, and stinginess with good sense","question":"How much would actually feel like enough, and how would you know?"}},"68":{"en":{"name":"Five of Pentacles","essence":"Out in the cold, near a lit door","message":"Two figures limp through falling snow, one on crutches, the other wrapping a thin shawl tighter. Above them glows a stained-glass window, warm and lit, and they walk right past it. The card speaks of a hard patch — an overdraft, a week laid up, the feeling of being left out — and asks whether pride or shame is stopping you knocking on the door that’s right there.","today":"Ask for one concrete kind of help today, however awkward: a payment plan, a lift, a shared meal, a day off. If you’re doing fine, offer one instead.","shadow":"Believing you deserve the cold, so not knocking","question":"Who would help you right now if you let them know what’s going on?"}},"69":{"en":{"name":"Six of Pentacles","essence":"Giving and receiving, weighed fairly","message":"A well-dressed merchant holds a set of scales in one hand and drops coins into the open palm of one of two kneeling figures. The other waits his turn. Nobody here is equal yet, and the scales suggest he’s thinking about fairness. The card brings give and take into view: the loan, the tip, the favour, the raise — and who might feel small afterwards.","today":"Give something today in a way that leaves the other person their dignity: pay promptly, tip well, help without a speech. And accept one offer without arguing it down.","shadow":"Giving so you can stay the one in charge","question":"Where do you find it easier to give than to receive, and why?"}},"70":{"en":{"name":"Seven of Pentacles","essence":"Leaning on the hoe, checking the growth","message":"A young farmer leans on his hoe and studies a leafy bush heavy with six coins, one more lying at his feet. The work isn’t finished; he’s stopped to look. The card invites an honest mid-point check: savings that grow slowly, the language app at day forty, a relationship you’re tending. Patience matters, and so does asking whether this crop deserves another season.","today":"Pick one long project and measure it honestly today: what you’ve put in, what’s grown, what hasn’t. Then decide: keep watering, change method, or stop.","shadow":"Digging up the seeds every day to check they’re growing","question":"What are you impatient with that is actually growing at the right speed?"}},"71":{"en":{"name":"Eight of Pentacles","essence":"Getting good by doing it again","message":"A craftsman sits at his bench, head down, tapping a design into a coin. Six finished ones hang on the post beside him; another waits on the floor. The town is far behind, and he doesn’t look up. The card favours skill built the unglamorous way: the scales you practise, the code you rewrite, the sourdough on its ninth attempt. Repetition is often where talent becomes something reliable.","today":"Give one skill a focused, phone-free half hour today and do the boring part properly. Don’t judge the result; count the repetitions.","shadow":"Perfecting one detail forever so you never have to finish","question":"What would you be excellent at in a year if you practised it daily?"}},"72":{"en":{"name":"Nine of Pentacles","essence":"Earned comfort, enjoyed in your own company","message":"A woman in a robe stitched with flowers stands alone in a ripe vineyard, a hooded falcon resting on her gloved hand. The grapes are heavy; the house behind her is hers. The falcon’s hood hints at the price: discipline. The card is a portrait of self-made ease — a flat furnished on your own salary, an evening enjoyed without company, the good coffee you can simply afford.","today":"Prove to yourself today that you can look after yourself well: cook a proper meal for one, pay a bill early, book yourself a table. Then enjoy your own company, phone face down.","shadow":"Independence so complete that needing anyone feels like failure","question":"Where could you trust your own resources instead of waiting for someone to provide?"}},"73":{"en":{"name":"Ten of Pentacles","essence":"What lasts longer than one life","message":"Under a stone archway an old man in a patterned robe sits stroking two white dogs, while a couple talks nearby and a child reaches towards a dog. Ten coins hang over the scene like a family tree. The card turns attention to wealth measured in decades: a house that stays in the family, a recipe, a pension, the habits grandparents pass on, good and bad, without noticing.","today":"Give the long term one small act today: sort an important document, ask an older relative for a family story, put a little aside, label the old photos.","shadow":"Living by the family script without asking if it fits","question":"What do you want to pass on, and what should stop with you?"}},"74":{"en":{"name":"Page of Pentacles","essence":"A beginner studying something real","message":"A young page stands in a spring field, holding a single coin up in both hands and staring at it as if it might explain itself. Behind him a ploughed patch waits. He hasn’t done anything yet; he’s paying attention. The card describes a student’s patience at the start of something practical: a first budget spreadsheet, an evening course, the first week in a new job, a vegetable bed.","today":"Learn one practical thing properly today: how your payslip is calculated, how to change a tyre, how a recipe really works. Then explain it to someone else, out loud.","shadow":"Collecting courses and plans while the field stays unploughed","question":"What practical skill would make next year noticeably easier?"}},"75":{"en":{"name":"Knight of Pentacles","essence":"Slow, steady and actually finishing","message":"A knight sits on a heavy black horse that is standing completely still at the edge of a ploughed field. He holds his coin and looks at it, not at the horizon. Of all the knights, he’s the only one not moving. The card values the reliable grind: a run three mornings a week, a debt paid down monthly, the colleague who always delivers. Boring, and hard to beat.","today":"Do the dull, necessary task first today — the expense report, the laundry, the twenty minutes on the course — at a steady pace, and finish it completely before anything fun.","shadow":"Mistaking a rut for reliability and refusing every change","question":"Which small routine, kept for three months, would change the most?"}},"76":{"en":{"name":"Queen of Pentacles","essence":"Care you can eat, wear and sleep in","message":"A queen sits in a garden thick with roses, a big gold coin cradled in her lap like something alive. A rabbit hides in the grass. Her throne is carved with fruit and goats: plenty, but earned. The card honours care made practical, a quality to give and receive: a full fridge, clean sheets, a friend who brings soup and also fixes your CV, a budget with room for flowers.","today":"Look after someone properly today, yourself included: a real meal, an early night, clean sheets, a walk in daylight. Then make one corner of home easier to live in.","shadow":"Looking after everyone so nobody notices you’re running on empty","question":"Who looks after you the way you look after everyone else?"}},"77":{"en":{"name":"King of Pentacles","essence":"Solid ground built to be shared","message":"A king sits in a garden so overgrown with grapevines that they’ve crept onto his robe. One hand rests on a gold coin, the other holds a sceptre; bulls are carved into his throne and a castle stands behind him. The card is often read as success that feeds people: a business that pays on time, a parent who helps with a deposit, something built for others to stand on.","today":"Handle one money or work matter today the way a calm, solvent adult would: pay on time, name a fair price, spend an hour on something that could still stand next year.","shadow":"Measuring your worth, and everyone else’s, by what they earn","question":"What are you building that other people could rely on?"}}}};
